INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('fcc1d2c5cd0616afe7e2872685257c7d5b177380e60342e3aa38086ef536b0b5','5a1d4f16-65d1-4404-9613-3bb5c8bcd70d',replace('Eren Yeager is the central character of Attack on Titan, and his development is one of the most dramatic parts of the story. At the beginning, Eren is a loud, angry, impatient child who hates the walls because he sees them as a prison. He cannot accept that people are satisfied living safely inside a cage. To him, comfort without freedom is humiliating. This makes him different from many people around him, who fear the outside world so much that they prefer ignorance and safety.\n\nEren''s hatred becomes personal after the fall of Shiganshina. He watches his mother die during the Titan attack, and that trauma turns his already intense desire for freedom into a violent vow of revenge. He joins the military because he wants to destroy the Titans. Early Eren thinks in simple terms: humanity is good, Titans are evil, and freedom will come once the monsters are eliminated. This simplicity is important because the story later breaks it apart.\n\nEren''s Titan power makes him both special and dangerous. When he first transforms, he does not fully understand what he is. Other soldiers fear him because his existence destroys their assumptions about humans and Titans. The Survey Corps decides to use him as a weapon, but even his allies are not fully comfortable with him. Eren wants to prove that he is useful to humanity, but he is also reckless and emotionally unstable. He often charges forward before thinking clearly.\n\nOne of Eren''s strongest traits is his refusal to submit. This can look heroic when he is fighting Titans or resisting corrupt authority. It can also look terrifying when he decides that no moral limit should stop him from reaching freedom. Eren is not simply brave; he is extreme. He does not tolerate cages, humiliation, or helplessness. When he believes something is blocking freedom, he wants to destroy it.\n\nHis relationships with Mikasa and Armin reveal different sides of him. Mikasa is fiercely protective of Eren, but Eren often resents being protected because it makes him feel weak. At the same time, he depends on her more than he admits. Armin represents Eren''s original dream of the outside world. Armin''s curiosity about the ocean, deserts, and unknown lands helped shape Eren''s desire to leave the walls. Eren''s bond with Armin is tied to wonder, while his bond with Mikasa is tied to survival, family, and painful attachment.\n\nAs Eren learns the truth about the outside world, he changes. The revelation that Titans are transformed Eldians and that humanity outside the walls still exists destroys his old worldview. He no longer sees the conflict as humans versus Titans. He sees a world where his people are hated, feared, and targeted because of history. Reaching the ocean should have been the fulfillment of his childhood dream, but for Eren it becomes another wall. He points beyond the ocean and understands that his enemies are not gone; they are waiting across the sea.\n\nAfter the time skip, Eren becomes colder and more secretive. He acts independently, infiltrates Marley, and forces his friends into a battle they did not fully choose. His attack on Liberio shows how far he has moved from his younger self. He understands that his enemies are human, including children and civilians, but he attacks anyway. He no longer needs to dehumanize the enemy to kill them. This is one of the most disturbing parts of his character. He has gained empathy and still chooses violence.\n\nEren''s idea of freedom becomes increasingly absolute. He believes that if the world will not allow Paradis to live, then the world must be crushed. He also wants his friends to live long lives, but his method of protecting them is catastrophic. His love for his friends and his desire for freedom do not make his actions morally clean. They make him more tragic and more dangerous, because he commits enormous violence while believing there is no other path.','\n',char(10)),'Eren Yeager, the central character of Attack on Titan, undergoes significant development as he navigates his desire for freedom and revenge against the Titans, leading to a complex and tragic transformation.','[{"start": 0, "end": 3889}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Yeager", "Mikasa", "Armin", "Titans", "Survey Corps", "Marley", "Paradis", "Liberio"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "9f14281e-d924-4a6d-b2a6-48bfe4c7fdbc", "preset_name": "nvdia", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "llm_base_url": "https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 10, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}','/0643e2fa-e4b9-456d-8a12-01a5ee714d5a/','2026-06-30 21:54:45');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('c0e60f1d3c63119b74cf8c7a2bea8f77f0e586cafe5acde331f75065acb6d0c5','5a1d4f16-65d1-4404-9613-3bb5c8bcd70d',replace('o live, then the world must be crushed. He also wants his friends to live long lives, but his method of protecting them is catastrophic. His love for his friends and his desire for freedom do not make his actions morally clean. They make him more tragic and more dangerous, because he commits enormous violence while believing there is no other path.\n\nEren also has a complicated relationship with fate and choice. Through the Attack Titan and the Paths, he experiences memories that blur past and future. He sees parts of what will happen and moves toward them. This creates a disturbing question: is Eren free, or is he trapped by the future he has seen? The story suggests that even if future memories influence him, the future aligns with his own deepest desires. He is not merely controlled by destiny. He chooses what he wants, even when what he wants is monstrous.\n\nBy the end, Eren becomes both protagonist and antagonist. He is still the boy who wanted freedom, but his pursuit of freedom becomes global destruction. He is not a simple villain because his motives include fear, love, rage, and desperation. He is not a simple hero because he commits mass murder. His tragedy is that he cannot imagine freedom without eliminating every threat. He hated the walls, but his mind remained trapped in a world divided between those who are free and those who must be destroyed.\n\nEren''s character works because the story does not make his transformation feel random. The seeds are present from the beginning: his rage, his absolutism, his refusal to accept captivity, and his willingness to fight violently for what he believes is freedom. What changes is the scale. As a child, he wanted to kill all Titans. As an adult, he decides to crush most of the world. The target changes, but the intensity remains. That continuity makes his arc powerful, disturbing, and tragic.','\n',char(10)),'Eren''s character is complex, driven by a desire for freedom and protection of his friends, but his methods are catastrophic and morally ambiguous, leading to a tragic transformation from protagonist to antagonist','[{"start": 3539, "end": 5412}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Attack Titan", "The Paths", "Titans", "Freedom"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "9f14281e-d924-4a6d-b2a6-48bfe4c7fdbc", "preset_name": "nvdia", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "llm_base_url": "https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 10, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}','/0643e2fa-e4b9-456d-8a12-01a5ee714d5a/','2026-06-30 21:54:54');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('75844f3a4e4157632821a29144a38534bd11d3b1a68ae7f7a1d474d1ec910252','24b38eda-70c7-459c-a32f-70b95ae2685c',replace('Grisha Yeager is Eren''s father and one of the most important hidden causes behind the story. He was originally an Eldian from Marley, where Eldians were oppressed and treated as dangerous because of their connection to Titan power. After his sister was killed by Marleyan officers, Grisha became involved with the Eldian Restorationists. He later inherited the Attack Titan from Eren Kruger and entered the walls on Paradis Island.\n\nInside the walls, Grisha became a doctor, married Carla, and raised Eren. After the fall of Shiganshina, he gave Eren Titan powers by injecting him and allowing Eren to eat him in Titan form. Grisha also stole the Founding Titan from the Reiss family. His actions shaped Eren''s future, but Grisha himself was not simply evil or heroic. He was driven by grief, guilt, ideology, and desperation.','\n',char(10)),'Grisha Yeager, Eren''s father, was an Eldian from Marley who became involved with the Eldian Restorationists after his sister''s death and later inherited the Attack Titan, shaping Eren''s future with his actions','[{"start": 0, "end": 826}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Grisha Yeager", "Eren", "Eldian Restorationists", "Marley", "Paradis Island", "Carla", "Eren Kruger", "Reiss family"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "9f14281e-d924-4a6d-b2a6-48bfe4c7fdbc", "preset_name": "nvdia", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "llm_base_url": "https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 10, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}','/0643e2fa-e4b9-456d-8a12-01a5ee714d5a/','2026-06-30 21:55:27');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('c54c142c6d876619dfbb9d314a99b600e143ac6c37e8a4553402dd33322be333','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('# Attack on Titan: A Detailed Narrative Chronicle\n\n## Part One: The Day the World Changed\n\n### The Breach\n\nThe morning of the breach started like any other day in the Shinzou District of Wall Maria. Eren Yeager, a brown-haired boy of fifteen, woke in his bed, his eyes opening to the familiar ceiling of his home. His adoptive sister, Mikasa Ackerman, was already awake, her dark eyes watching him with the quiet intensity that had defined her since childhood. The wooden beams of their small house creaked as Eren stretched, and outside, the sounds of merchants opening their stalls drifted through the window.\n\nEren had always felt something burning inside him—a restless energy that made him want to explore beyond the walls, to see the outside world that humanity had been locked away from for one hundred and seven years. The titans existed beyond those walls, the massive creatures that had once nearly driven humanity to extinction. But that was ancient history, or so everyone believed. The walls had held for over a century. Humanity was safe.\n\nOr so they thought.\n\nEren was eating breakfast when Mikasa placed a hand on his shoulder. "You''re going to be late for the Scout recruitment," she reminded him quietly. Eren nodded, his determination evident in the set of his jaw. He had been talking about joining the Survey Corps for months—that elite but practically suicidal group of soldiers who actually left the walls and fought titans in the open field. It was a dream that Mikasa didn''t share. She wanted Eren to join the Garrison, to stay within the walls, to stay alive.\n\nBut Eren''s mind was made up.\n\nThe recruitment ceremony was held in the open plaza, and dozens of young people had gathered—some eager, some pressed by their families, some simply looking for an opportunity. A tall woman with blonde hair stood before them, watching with calculating eyes. This was Commander Shadis of the Survey Corps, and he would be evaluating each of them. His expression was stern, almost contemptuous of their youth and their presumed innocence.\n\nEren stood tall, his hands clenched at his sides. He watched as Shadis evaluated each recruit, often dismissing them with harsh words. When Shadis approached Eren, he stared down at the boy with intensity.\n\n"Why do you want to join the Survey Corps?" Shadis demanded.\n\n"To fight the titans. To destroy them," Eren answered, his voice burning with conviction. "Humanity can''t remain trapped behind these walls. We have to take back the world."\n\nShadis''s eyes narrowed. He didn''t speak, just turned and walked away. Eren remained standing, waiting to see if he would be accepted.\n\nNear Eren, a blonde-haired boy with a more pragmatic demeanor had also attracted attention. This was Reiner Braun, who had given a more measured response about wanting to protect humanity within the walls. His friend, a darker-haired boy named Bertolt Hoover, stood quietly nearby. Both had come from the outer walls, from districts that had seen more hardship.\n\nAs the recruits were being organized into lines, another figure caught attention—a girl with dark hair tied back, moving with unusual precision. This was Annie Leonhart, whose expression remained carefully neutral, her gray eyes observing everyone around her with the calculating gaze of a fighter.\n\nThe ceremony continued through the morning, and by midday, the chosen recruits had been separated from those who wouldn''t make the cut. Eren had been accepted. As he looked around at his fellow recruits, he felt a mixture of pride and anticipation. He had no way of knowing what was coming.\n\n### The Colossus\n\nThe world changed at 1:47 in the afternoon.\n\nArwin Smith, the Survey Corps'' leader and a man of high intelligence and hidden ambitions, was reviewing reports in his office when a scout burst through the door, face flushed with panic. The scout''s words were barely coherent, but their meaning was unmistakable: a titan had appeared. Not just appeared—it had been spotted near the walls.','\n',char(10)),'On the morning of the Titan breach in the Shinzou District, fifteen-year-old Eren Yeager prepares for the Survey Corps recruitment ceremony, encouraged by his adoptive sister Mikasa Ackerman. The ceremony is led by Commander Shadis, where E','[{"start": 0, "end": 3992}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Yeager", "Mikasa Ackerman", "Shadis", "Reiner Braun", "Bertolt Hoover", "Annie Leonhart", "Colossal Titan", "Survey Corps"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:44:21');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('2165ace7a246f47530558c74cc37e8064a9c6d9c4a571fb99ad388faf8b67462','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('ternoon.\n\nArwin Smith, the Survey Corps'' leader and a man of high intelligence and hidden ambitions, was reviewing reports in his office when a scout burst through the door, face flushed with panic. The scout''s words were barely coherent, but their meaning was unmistakable: a titan had appeared. Not just appeared—it had been spotted near the walls.\n\nThe message spread through the district like wildfire. Eren, still in the plaza with his fellow recruits, first heard the commotion from crowds gathering and pointing. Some people were running; others stood frozen in shock. Then came the sound—a booming crack that split the sky like thunder, followed by the alarm bells.\n\nThe wall had been breached.\n\nBut not by ordinary means. As the dust cleared and people scattered in every direction, a head appeared over Wall Maria. It was massive beyond comprehension—sixty meters tall, with the proportions of a human but the sheer scale of a nightmare. The Colossal Titan pulled itself up and over the wall with terrible, methodical slowness, and as it did, the breach grew larger.\n\nEren stood frozen, his eyes wide, watching as this impossible creature moved across the sky above the wall. It was real. Despite everything the government had said about safety, about the walls being impenetrable, the titans had found a way through.\n\nThe Colossal Titan, having torn open the wall, simply vanished. It disappeared as mysteriously as it had appeared, leaving behind a gaping hole in humanity''s primary defense and absolute chaos in its wake.\n\nThe immediate consequences were catastrophic. The breach was in Wall Maria''s outer district, and beyond that wall lay nothing but open ground and, more importantly, hundreds of regular titans that had been kept at bay for generations. Those monsters, smaller than the Colossus but still ten to twenty meters tall, began pouring through the hole, their hunger driving them forward.\n\nThe evacuation began immediately. Citizens were herded toward the inner gates, toward Wall Rose, the second layer of human civilization. But the inner wall was far away for those in the outer districts, and the titans were fast. What followed was a massacre unlike anything in recent history. Titans that had never tasted human flesh for over a century now feasted on thousands.\n\nEren watched it all from the relative safety of the evacuation route. He saw titans rip people apart. He saw a woman torn in half. He saw the indifferent, almost curious expressions on the titans'' faces as they consumed human beings like we might eat livestock. And he saw something else—something that would stay with him forever.\n\nHe saw his mother.\n\n### The Loss\n\nIn the chaos, Eren and Mikasa had been separated from their home, pushed along in the crowd of refugees. Carla Yeager, their mother, had been unable to move quickly enough due to an old injury to her leg. She was calling out to them, trying to make her way through the crowd, but the tide of humanity swept them forward.\n\nEren fought against the current, trying to turn back. Mikasa, with her usual clarity of thought, grabbed his hand firmly.\n\n"We have to go," she said, and her voice carried an authority that Eren couldn''t argue with.\n\n"Mother!" Eren screamed, reaching back toward the crowd, but it was too late.\n\nAs they reached the gate to Wall Rose, refugees continued to pour through. Eren looked back one final time and saw a fifteen-meter-class titan—one of the regular breed—turn toward a group of people who hadn''t made it to the gate. Among them was a familiar figure: his mother, Carla, her face turned up toward the monster in fear.\n\nThe titan bent down and picked her up as easily as one might lift a child''s toy. Eren heard the scream. He heard the sound of her body breaking. And then the crowd pushed him through the gate, and the doors began to close behind them.','\n',char(10)),'The Colossal Titan breaches Wall Maria, allowing smaller titans to invade and massacre civilians. During the chaotic evacuation to Wall Rose, Eren Yeager witnesses the Colossal Titan''s appearance, the subsequent titan incursion, and is sepa','[{"start": 3642, "end": 7490}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Arwin Smith", "Eren", "Colossal Titan", "Wall Maria", "Wall Rose", "Carla Yeager", "Mikasa"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:44:25');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('cf5e81328f4c3fbf5b159274515843a9827a00f0594868508a00761425034656','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('t to the gate. Among them was a familiar figure: his mother, Carla, her face turned up toward the monster in fear.\n\nThe titan bent down and picked her up as easily as one might lift a child''s toy. Eren heard the scream. He heard the sound of her body breaking. And then the crowd pushed him through the gate, and the doors began to close behind them.\n\nEren''s world shattered in that moment. He stared at the closing gate in absolute shock, unable to process what he had just witnessed. The door sealed with a massive clang, cutting off the outer district completely. Thousands remained trapped outside. His mother was gone.\n\nMikasa stood beside him, her dark eyes looking forward with the same measured expression she always wore, but her grip on his hand was tight enough to hurt.\n\n## Part Two: The Struggle for Survival\n\n### The Garrison and First Assignments\n\nThe weeks following the breach were a blur of military reorganization, fear, and grim determination. Eren, Mikasa, and a silent boy named Arwin who had grown up with them in their district all found themselves conscripted into military service. The world no longer had the luxury of waiting for volunteers among children—they needed soldiers.\n\nEren joined the Garrison, the military police force tasked with defending the inner walls. The decision had been made for him: his aptitude evaluations suggested he was suitable for this role, and frankly, the military needed bodies. His rage and his determination to kill titans were exactly what they needed, or so the officers believed.\n\nBut Eren was not at peace. Every day in the barracks, he carried the weight of what he had seen, the memory of his mother''s death. He would lie awake at night, his fists clenched, planning how he would kill titans. He would become strong. He would become a soldier who could actually fight the titans, not just defend static walls.\n\nMikasa had been placed in the same unit by some bureaucratic fortune, and she remained his anchor. She could move with a grace and precision that surpassed most soldiers twice her age. Even in training, it was clear she would become something special. But she was focused primarily on one thing: keeping Eren alive.\n\nThe boy named Arwin had also been conscripted, but he was assigned to a different unit. Eren didn''t see him often after that.\n\nTraining under the Garrison proved harsh. The commanding officers had little patience for green recruits, and they drove the young soldiers relentlessly. There was no time for gentleness; the titans were at the gates, literally, and soldiers had to be ready to face them.\n\nThree months after the breach, the Garrison received orders. The military had decided to conduct a reconnaissance mission into the outer districts—to assess the damage, to map out the titan movements, and to recover any supplies that might be salvageable. The outer districts had been sealed off since the breach; no one was quite sure what conditions they would find inside.\n\nEren was assigned to this mission. It would be his first time facing a titan since the day of the breach.\n\n### The Outer District Reconnaissance\n\nThe gates to the outer district were opened with grinding slowness, and a squad of fifty Garrison soldiers marched through, their hands gripping their swords or their spears. Eren could feel his heart pounding as he crossed into the wasteland that had once been his home.\n\nThe district was eerily quiet. That was the first thing he noticed. No sounds of commerce, no voices of children, no songs. Just wind blowing through empty streets, and the remnants of buildings that had been partially consumed—the roofs torn off, the interiors exposed like wounds.\n\nBodies still lay in some of the streets. They had begun to decompose in the weeks since the breach, and the smell was overwhelming. Soldiers gagged and covered their faces, but they pushed forward. This was the reality of the world now.','\n',char(10)),'Following a titan breach that killed Eren''s mother, Carla, Eren, Mikasa, and Armin are conscripted into military service. Eren joins the Garrison and is soon assigned to a reconnaissance mission into the devastated outer district, his first','[{"start": 7140, "end": 11054}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Mikasa", "Armin", "Carla", "Garrison", "titans", "outer district", "breach"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:44:29');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('4f0be120e8c228afb1ea1eb1f654a9dedffdac2dbacdf9814a2bb6b3a7cc79e9','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('he remnants of buildings that had been partially consumed—the roofs torn off, the interiors exposed like wounds.\n\nBodies still lay in some of the streets. They had begun to decompose in the weeks since the breach, and the smell was overwhelming. Soldiers gagged and covered their faces, but they pushed forward. This was the reality of the world now.\n\nEren found his way to his old neighborhood. The house where he had grown up was still standing, though the front door had been torn off its hinges. He entered cautiously, sword drawn, half-expecting to find a titan inside.\n\nThe interior was exactly as they had left it that morning, except for the dust and the silence. Eren''s room was still there, his bed unmade. In the kitchen, his mother''s shawl lay over a chair where she had left it. He picked it up and held it to his face, breathing in what remained of her scent.\n\nHe was pulled from his memories by a sound—movement from deeper within the house. Eren''s grip tightened on his sword. His fellow soldiers, stationed outside, could hear nothing. He crept forward, his training overriding his fear.\n\nWhat he found was not a titan, but something worse in its way: his mother''s remains. She had been partially consumed, left in the corner of the adjacent room like discarded waste. There was nothing left to bury, nothing left to identify except her position. Eren stood looking at what remained of the woman who had raised him, and something in his chest twisted so violently he thought it might stop his heart.\n\nHe exited the house without reporting what he had found. The Garrison had no protocol for claiming remains in such conditions, and there was nothing to be gained by forcing others to witness this.\n\nThe mission continued. Soldiers searched through buildings, finding caches of old weapons and supplies, noting the positions where titan nests had been established in some of the abandoned buildings. The titans in this area, it seemed, had moved on—possibly pushed further in by their territorial nature, possibly seeking greener pastures.\n\nOne soldier, a veteran sergeant named Hange Zoe, was particularly interested in examining the remains of titans found in the district. Hange was a tall, dark-haired woman with an almost unnatural fascination with the creatures. While other soldiers saw the titans as nothing but monsters to be destroyed, Hange saw them as subjects of study, mysteries to be understood.\n\n"They''re not just mindless beasts," Hange explained to a junior soldier who was helping her examine a dead titan. "Look at the structure of their mouths, the way they''re designed. They have no stomachs—the digestive system seems almost vestigial. So why do they eat us if not for nutrition?"\n\nIt was the kind of question that most soldiers didn''t bother asking. Titans ate humans; that was all anyone needed to know. But Hange''s curiosity suggested there was more to the story.\n\nThe reconnaissance mission lasted four days. When it concluded and the soldiers returned to Wall Rose, Eren felt fundamentally changed. He had faced the absence of titans and found it somehow worse than facing the creatures themselves. The emptiness was a different kind of terror.\n\n### The Push Back\n\nNews arrived in the weeks following the reconnaissance that shocked the entire military structure. Commander Erwin Smith, whose ambitions had always been carefully hidden beneath a veil of competent leadership, had orchestrated a plan. The Survey Corps would launch a counteroffensive—a push beyond Wall Rose to assess the situation, to gather intelligence, and to begin the process of what he called "reclamation."\n\nIt was a suicide mission, and everyone knew it.\n\nThe Survey Corps mustered four hundred and fifty soldiers—the finest titans fighters humanity had to offer. Eren watched them prepare from behind Wall Rose, and he felt the weight of his powerlessness. He was Garrison, not Survey Corps. He would not be part of this push.','\n',char(10)),'A soldier named Eren returns to his war-torn neighborhood and finds his mother''s remains, while a veteran sergeant named Hange Zoe studies titan anatomy with curiosity. The Survey Corps, led by Commander Erwin Smith, prepares a dangerous co','[{"start": 10704, "end": 14650}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Hange Zoe", "Erwin Smith", "Wall Rose", "Survey Corps", "Garrison"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:44:32');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('27470c82e83cb2c3b90259972b1c2449aa561d842c281a5f1fa98ed7c67447f2','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('hat he called "reclamation."\n\nIt was a suicide mission, and everyone knew it.\n\nThe Survey Corps mustered four hundred and fifty soldiers—the finest titans fighters humanity had to offer. Eren watched them prepare from behind Wall Rose, and he felt the weight of his powerlessness. He was Garrison, not Survey Corps. He would not be part of this push.\n\nBut he was watching when the Survey Corps rode out, their green cloaks billowing behind them, their formation precise and disciplined. The gates closed behind them, and the watchers on the wall waited for news.\n\nWhat came back first were the casualty reports.\n\nOver three hundred soldiers died on that mission. The titans, it turned out, were far more numerous than anyone had imagined, and they were far more strategic in their hunting patterns. The Survey Corps faced what Erwin would later call "a coordinated titan advance"—multiple creatures working in patterns that suggested intelligence or at least instinctive pack behavior.\n\nThe few soldiers who returned spoke in hushed tones about what they had witnessed. One soldier, a young man named Oluo, described titans that seemed to focus on specific targets. Another mentioned a scout who had been taken not by a wandering monster but by what appeared to be an organized assault.\n\nAnd there were other, stranger reports. Some soldiers swore they had seen something impossible—a titan that moved differently from the others, a titan that seemed to fight the other titans rather than simply hunt humans.\n\nThese reports were filed away and largely dismissed by the military hierarchy. In the official records, the mission was marked as a tactical reconnaissance, with acceptable losses for information gained. In reality, it had been a catastrophe that had shaken everyone''s faith in the military''s ability to protect them.\n\n### Growing Tensions\n\nIn the weeks after the failed Survey Corps mission, tensions within the military began to rise. The military police, who answered directly to the nobility rather than to the commanding officers, began to consolidate power. There were whispers about the Survey Corps being too ambitious, about Erwin Smith having dreams of glory that didn''t match humanity''s actual capabilities.\n\nEren, still training in the Garrison, felt increasingly frustrated. He wanted to fight. He wanted to kill titans. But all around him, he sensed a military structure that was more concerned with maintaining power and controlling information than with actually protecting people.\n\nIt was during this period that a special unit began to form—a team of soldiers chosen for their aptitude and their tactical ability. This unit was ostensibly part of the Garrison but took orders from both the military police and, secretly, from Erwin Smith himself. It was a shadowy operation, one that operated in the margins between the official military structure.\n\nEren was selected for this unit, along with several others, including Reiner Braun and Bertolt Hoover—the two boys from his recruitment class who had caught Shadis''s eye. With them came several other soldiers of varying experience levels.\n\nThe unit''s first assignment was strange: they were to conduct surveillance of a particular section of Wall Rose that had been marked for "reinforcement." The assignment seemed mundane, but Eren sensed there was more to it.\n\nAs it turned out, there was.\n\n## Part Three: The Crack in the Foundation\n\n### The Second Breach\n\nOn a clear morning, exactly ten months after the first breach, the second wall fell.\n\nEren was training in the barracks when the alarm bells rang out—the same pattern, the same rhythm as the day of the first catastrophe. His blood went cold. It was happening again.\n\nThe breach occurred not at Wall Maria, which had already been breached, but at Wall Rose—the second and supposedly more secure barrier. The breach point was in the Trost District, one of the largest population centers within Wall Rose.','\n',char(10)),'The Survey Corps'' reclamation mission results in heavy casualties and reports of coordinated titan behavior, including a titan that fought others. Military tensions rise, and Eren is selected for a special unit with Reiner Braun and Bertolt','[{"start": 14300, "end": 18241}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Survey Corps", "Erwin Smith", "Reiner Braun", "Bertolt Hoover", "Wall Rose", "Trost District", "Oluo"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:44:36');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('83221dcebb28f1e86aae1e6a576712e8b082d400c61ba3b2f609f594e472f30d','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('e same pattern, the same rhythm as the day of the first catastrophe. His blood went cold. It was happening again.\n\nThe breach occurred not at Wall Maria, which had already been breached, but at Wall Rose—the second and supposedly more secure barrier. The breach point was in the Trost District, one of the largest population centers within Wall Rose.\n\nWhat made this catastrophe different was what came through the breach: the Colossal Titan appeared once again, tearing open the wall with the same methodical deliberation as before. And behind it, just as before, came the regular titans, a flood of bodies and hunger flowing through the gap in humanity''s defenses.\n\nBut this time, there was something else. As the Colossal Titan pulled itself up and over the wall, Eren saw something that would haunt him: a flash of something that might have been human, a silhouette inside the titan''s form, visible for just a moment as the creature crested the wall.\n\nThe evacuation of Trost District was chaos. Unlike the outer districts, Trost was densely populated, and people couldn''t escape quickly enough. The military attempted to organize a defense, to hold a corridor for citizens to escape toward the inner wall, but the titans were overwhelming in their numbers and in their hunger.\n\nEren''s unit was immediately mobilized to help manage the evacuation. They were not sent to fight—that would come later—but to help organize the panicked crowds, to direct them toward safety. It was a futile effort; the chaos was too great, and the titans moved too fast.\n\nFrom his position trying to direct refugees, Eren saw things that burned themselves into his mind. A mother being torn away from her child. A man crushed beneath a falling building as a titan pulled it down. A boy, no more than eight years old, staring in shock at the blood covering his arms, not comprehending what had happened.\n\nAnd everywhere, the sound of the alarm bells, ringing and ringing, a steady pulse of warning and horror.\n\n### The Siege\n\nWhat followed was not a simple catastrophe like the first breach. Instead, the Colossal Titan seemed to have sealed the breach after allowing the other titans through, leaving thousands of the creatures inside the walls to hunt and feed. The regular titans didn''t leave; they spread throughout Trost District and the surrounding areas, creating what amounted to a siege.\n\nThe military was forced to adjust its tactics. They couldn''t evacuate everyone at once—the roads were jammed with refugees, and the outer walls couldn''t accommodate them all. A defensive line was established within Trost itself, an attempt to hold certain sections of the city while organizing evacuations in stages.\n\nEren''s unit, along with hundreds of other soldiers, was assigned to this defensive line. They would stand against the titans using traditional weapons—swords and spears—which were, by any objective measure, utterly inadequate against creatures that could regenerate from nearly any wound and that possessed strength beyond measure.\n\nThe first night of the siege was a slaughter.\n\nTitans hunted through the streets and buildings of Trost, and soldiers fought them with a desperate, almost ritualistic determination. The tactical doctrine of anti-titan warfare had been developed against occasional incursions; it was never designed to handle sustained combat against hundreds of creatures.\n\nSoldiers would engage a single titan using traditional blades, trying to sever its limbs or injure its spine. Sometimes they succeeded; the titan would collapse, allowing soldiers to move on to the next target. More often, the soldier would be caught or trampled or torn apart. The loss rate was horrendous.\n\nReiner Braun proved himself in this combat, moving with a soldier''s discipline and training, working in coordination with his unit. Eren fought with a fury that bordered on madness, driven by his rage at the titans, by his helplessness, by the memory of his mother''s death.','\n',char(10)),'The Colossal Titan breaches Wall Rose at Trost District, allowing Titans to flood in and create a siege. The military establishes a defensive line while attempting organized evacuations, with Eren''s unit and Reiner Braun participating in th','[{"start": 17891, "end": 21861}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Colossal Titan", "Wall Rose", "Trost District", "Reiner Braun", "Military", "Titans", "Siege"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:45:19');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('46a00fa3d88e5626ed37b8f41a8dead23514baf30ea06d0321c69ac615a6cdc6','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('er would be caught or trampled or torn apart. The loss rate was horrendous.\n\nReiner Braun proved himself in this combat, moving with a soldier''s discipline and training, working in coordination with his unit. Eren fought with a fury that bordered on madness, driven by his rage at the titans, by his helplessness, by the memory of his mother''s death.\n\nBy dawn, the defensive line had held, barely. They had managed to kill or disable approximately fifteen titans in Trost District. There were hundreds more to go.\n\nBut something changed that night. As soldiers were being rearranged and resupplied for the next push, a scout brought word that would shift everything: a new type of soldier had appeared, something that shouldn''t exist.\n\nThere were reports of a soldier fighting the titans with a capability far beyond what was humanly possible. This soldier was moving with speed and strength that seemed impossible, taking down titans alone that would normally require teams of soldiers.\n\nNo one could identify this soldier. They seemed to appear and disappear as the titan crisis developed, always where the fighting was thickest. Some soldiers thought they were hallucinating. Others began to whisper about myths and legends, about old stories of soldiers with powers beyond mortal capacity.\n\n### The Armored Titan\n\nOn the third night of the siege, as the military was attempting a coordinated assault on a group of titans blocking an evacuation route, something unprecedented happened.\n\nA fifteen-meter-class titan appeared on the battlefield—nothing remarkable about that. But this titan was different. Its hide was darkened, almost metallic in appearance, and it moved with a purpose that seemed almost intelligent. And as soldiers engaged this titan, they realized something was terribly wrong.\n\nThe creature was armored. Not merely thick-skinned, but plated, with hardened sections of its body that conventional blades couldn''t cut through.\n\nThis titan, which would come to be known as the Armored Titan, tore through the military line with devastating efficiency. Soldiers that might have survived an encounter with a normal titan found themselves shattered and broken against this creature''s armored hide.\n\nOne soldier, a veteran sergeant, managed to strike what should have been a killing blow, severing what appeared to be the Armored Titan''s ankle. But the creature simply regenerated, the limb growing back within moments.\n\nThe military line broke. Soldiers fell back, some screaming, some moving in cold, calculated retreat. The evacuation route was compromised.\n\nIt was in the chaos that followed that something impossible occurred.\n\n### The Emergence\n\nEren was falling back with his unit when he was caught. A stray titan—a nine-meter-class—emerged from between buildings and grabbed him by the arm. The creature''s grip was crushing, the pressure mounting in Eren''s limb until he knew it was about to break.\n\nThis was death. This was the moment where his story would end, torn apart like his mother had been.\n\nThe last thing he remembered before the pain became overwhelming was looking back at Mikasa, seeing her face contort with a fury that mirrored his own.\n\nThen there was darkness.\n\nEren''s consciousness fragmented. Pain and pressure and heat and the sensation of being inside something vast and wrong. There were flashes of sensation, as though he were experiencing things from a perspective that wasn''t his own. He saw the world as the titan saw it, from a height of nine meters, with a crushing sense of need and hunger.\n\nAnd then, impossibly, he pushed back.\n\nIt started as a sensation of resistance within the titan''s body. Then it became a force, something pushing from inside the creature, forcing itself outward. The titan convulsed, its body rigid with whatever was happening inside it.','\n',char(10)),'During the siege of Trost District, soldiers including Reiner Braun and Eren Yeager battle titans, facing a new intelligent Armored Titan that breaks the military line. In the chaos, Eren is captured by a titan but experiences a transformat','[{"start": 21511, "end": 25328}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Reiner Braun", "Eren Yeager", "Mikasa", "Armored Titan", "Trost District", "Titans"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:45:24');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('1afefe324c33881f99d405c65a387da6d31bce8f088e32023cf78c3385db2352','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('aw it, from a height of nine meters, with a crushing sense of need and hunger.\n\nAnd then, impossibly, he pushed back.\n\nIt started as a sensation of resistance within the titan''s body. Then it became a force, something pushing from inside the creature, forcing itself outward. The titan convulsed, its body rigid with whatever was happening inside it.\n\nThe creature''s limbs were still moving, still attempting to lift Eren—or what had been Eren—to its mouth. But now there was a counterforce, something inside the titan fighting its own instincts.\n\nSoldiers nearby stopped their retreat, watching in absolute confusion as the titan''s body convulsed. Then, with a surge of movement, something emerged from within the titan''s form.\n\nIt was massive. It was humanoid. It was approximately fifteen meters tall and covered in muscle, its skin darkened to almost the same shade as the Armored Titan. And it was, impossibly, moving with intent and purpose, moving with what appeared to be intelligence.\n\nThe soldiers watched in shock as this new titan—or thing that looked like a titan—grabbed the nine-meter-class creature that had been holding Eren and, in a movement that could only be described as rage-fueled, tore the creature limb from limb.\n\nThe nine-meter titan, despite its regenerative abilities, couldn''t survive being completely dismembered. It collapsed, and as it died, the new creature—this manifestation of Eren, though no one could know it was Eren—turned toward the other titans on the battlefield.\n\nAnd then it charged.\n\nWhat followed was one of the most shocking scenes in the entire war: a titan fighting other titans with what appeared to be a soldier''s discipline and tactics. The humanoid creature (which soldiers would later identify, without certainty, as a human-like titan) moved with purpose, engaging the nine-meter and ten-meter-class titans that had been pursuing the retreating soldiers.\n\nIt fought like Eren might have wanted to fight—with an urgency that bordered on suicidal, with a fury that was almost beautiful in its intensity. Whenever it took damage, the creature would regenerate. Whenever it was struck down, it would rise again.\n\nThe other titans, confused by this new entity, attempted to subdue it just as they would subdue a human. But this creature didn''t run. It didn''t hide. It fought back.\n\nSoldiers watched in absolute confusion as the creature disabled three titans in quick succession, clearing a path through the monster army. And then, as suddenly as it had emerged, the creature collapsed. The light in its eyes seemed to fade, and it fell backward, slamming against a building with enough force to crack the structure.\n\nThe creature didn''t rise again.\n\nIn the immediate aftermath, soldiers rushed forward cautiously, weapons drawn. What they found was the creature''s corpse beginning to decompose at an accelerated rate, the flesh seeming to evaporate like steam. And within the titan''s body, impossibly, was a human form.\n\nIt was Eren Yeager.\n\nHe was unconscious, badly injured, his uniform torn and stained with blood, but he was alive. And he was completely, impossibly human.\n\n## Part Four: Questions Without Answers\n\n### The Investigation\n\nThe military''s response to Eren''s existence was swift and, in many cases, chaotic. Soldiers who had witnessed the transformation reported what they had seen, but without photographic or documented evidence, their accounts were dismissed as hysteria or confusion caused by the stress of combat.\n\nEren himself regained consciousness three days later in a military medical facility. His first memory was of pain—a deep, aching pain throughout his entire body, as though he had been beaten from the inside out. His second memory was of Mikasa''s face above him, her dark eyes showing something that might have been relief.\n\n"You''re awake," she said quietly, as though she had been waiting by his side for those entire three days. She likely had.\n\n"What happened?" Eren''s voice was hoarse, barely a whisper.','\n',char(10)),'A humanoid titan emerges from within a nine-meter titan that was holding Eren, kills it, fights other titans to clear a path for soldiers, and then collapses, revealing an unconscious Eren Yeager inside. Eren later wakes up in a military fa','[{"start": 24978, "end": 28975}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Yeager", "Mikasa", "Armored Titan", "nine-meter titan", "humanoid titan", "military"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:45:28');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('39033c51f9303d3c195c71b08e1bb51c2da65f573a8e92df0a597392e04fd366','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('body, as though he had been beaten from the inside out. His second memory was of Mikasa''s face above him, her dark eyes showing something that might have been relief.\n\n"You''re awake," she said quietly, as though she had been waiting by his side for those entire three days. She likely had.\n\n"What happened?" Eren''s voice was hoarse, barely a whisper.\n\nMikasa didn''t answer immediately. She seemed to be choosing her words carefully. "You were taken by a titan. And then... something happened."\n\nIt was clear she didn''t understand what had happened any more than anyone else.\n\nThe military hierarchy''s response was split. Some officials, particularly within the military police, believed Eren was a threat—a potentially weaponized titan that needed to be contained or executed immediately. Others, including Erwin Smith and Hange Zoe, recognized the unprecedented opportunity: if a human could transform into a titan, then titans were not what everyone believed them to be.\n\nHange, in particular, became obsessed with studying Eren. She would visit his medical quarters with countless questions, scribbling notes furiously as Eren attempted to describe what he had experienced. He could remember the sensation of being inside the titan''s body, of seeing through its eyes, of moving its limbs. He could remember the hunger that the creature felt—an overwhelming compulsion to consume human flesh. But he couldn''t explain why he had been able to resist that hunger, why he had fought the titan''s nature.\n\n"This changes everything," Hange said more than once, her dark eyes gleaming with an intensity that was almost frightening. "Everything we thought we knew about the titans is wrong."\n\nMeanwhile, in political chambers far from the front lines, discussions were taking place about what should be done with Eren. The military police, representing the interests of the nobility that controlled the interior territories, pushed for Eren to be executed as a potential threat. Erwin Smith countered with the argument that Eren represented a potential solution to humanity''s problems, and that studying him could yield weapons that might turn the tide in the war against the titans.\n\nThe decision was made to keep Eren alive and to enlist him in the Survey Corps. If he could transform into a titan and retain his human consciousness and training, he could become the most powerful weapon humanity had ever possessed.\n\nEren was given little choice in the matter. His options were to agree to join the Survey Corps or face execution. He agreed, partly out of his own desire to fight, partly because it seemed like the only path to survival.\n\n### The Formation of the Special Operations Squad\n\nWith Eren integrated into the military structure as a special asset, Erwin Smith took the next logical step: he assembled an elite unit of soldiers specifically designed to support Eren in combat. This unit would be officially designated as part of the Survey Corps but would operate under Erwin''s direct command.\n\nThe squad consisted of five core members: Eren himself, as the potential titan and the driving force of the unit; Arwin, Eren''s childhood friend, who had proven himself a skilled soldier and who would serve as Eren''s psychological anchor; Mikasa, Eren''s adoptive sister and one of the most talented combat soldiers humanity had produced; Jean Kirstein, a soldier with natural leadership instincts and a tactical mind; and Sasha Blouse, whose seemingly casual demeanor masked a keen tactical awareness and an almost supernatural ability to move through urban terrain.\n\nActually, there were several others added to the squad as well, including Connie Springer, a somewhat clumsy but determined young man who had proven himself in the Trost siege, and others who would fill specific tactical roles.','\n',char(10)),'After Eren Yeager''s transformation into a Titan, military officials debate his fate. Erwin Smith and Hange Zoe advocate for studying him, while the military police demand his execution. A compromise is reached: Eren joins the Survey Corps a','[{"start": 28625, "end": 32421}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Yeager", "Mikasa Ackerman", "Hange Zoe", "Erwin Smith", "Survey Corps", "Military Police", "Special Operations Squad", "Titans"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:45:32');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('2b15bf45c77faea55c536d1f45761fb54a6146fc62a01b936652ab4bae5709d2','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('mingly casual demeanor masked a keen tactical awareness and an almost supernatural ability to move through urban terrain.\n\nActually, there were several others added to the squad as well, including Connie Springer, a somewhat clumsy but determined young man who had proven himself in the Trost siege, and others who would fill specific tactical roles.\n\nThe unit''s mission was clear: when the Survey Corps pushed beyond the walls, this elite squad would support Eren in his explorations, protecting him if he transformed and gathering intelligence about the titans and the world beyond the walls.\n\nThe first preparation for this mission involved testing Eren''s transformation ability. Military officials wanted to understand the parameters of his power: Could he transform at will? How much of his human consciousness remained when he transformed? How long could he maintain the titan form?\n\nThese tests were conducted in secret, in a specialized facility built specifically for containing a transformed Eren. The facility was essentially a reinforced box, designed to contain a fifteen-meter-class titan for observation.\n\nIn his first voluntary transformation attempt, Eren tried to trigger the change by biting his own hand. It didn''t work. He simply wounded himself without experiencing any change.\n\n"Again," Hange instructed, watching carefully.\n\nEren tried again, applying more force, creating a deeper wound. Nothing.\n\nThrough multiple attempts, it became clear that the transformation wasn''t automatic or easily controlled. Eren had to be in a specific mental state—a state of urgency or desperation or rage—to trigger the change.\n\nIt was only when he was attacked by soldiers using blunt weapons, when he was forced into genuine combat against human opponents, that he felt the transformation coming. It surged up from within him like a wave, an overwhelming need to fight, to protect himself, to win.\n\nWhen it happened, the sensation was indescribable. His bones grew and lengthened. His muscles expanded. His perspective shifted upward as he grew to tower above the soldiers around him. And within that titan form, he was still himself—he could still think, still understand, still feel the weight of his humanity even as the overwhelming hunger of the titan threatened to consume his consciousness.\n\nThe transformation lasted for approximately five minutes before exhaustion forced him back into his human form. The reversion was as violent as the transformation, his body shrinking and compressing until he fell to the ground, gasping, completely drained.\n\nAfter the transformation, Eren was unconscious for twelve hours.\n\nWhen he awoke, Hange''s observations were comprehensive: Eren''s titan transformation took approximately ten seconds, his combat duration was limited to about five minutes of active fighting, and the energy expenditure was enormous. He would need to eat vast quantities of food to recover from each transformation.\n\nBut the transformation was real. It was controllable, at least to some degree. And it suggested possibilities that no one had considered before.\n\n"If one human can become a titan," Erwin said quietly after reviewing Hange''s findings, "then it''s possible that titans themselves are human. Or that they were human. That changes the nature of this entire war."\n\n### Political Complications\n\nWhile the military was conducting these tests, political forces were moving in the background. The military police, representing the nobility''s interests, were growing increasingly concerned about the power that Erwin Smith and the Survey Corps were consolidating.\n\nA coup was being planned.\n\nThe details were murky, known only to the highest levels of government, but the goal was clear: to neutralize Erwin Smith and the Survey Corps as a political force, to consolidate control over military operations, and to ensure that the nobility''s interests remained protected.','\n',char(10)),'An elite squad is formed to support Eren Jaeger, whose titan transformation is tested in secret. Experiments reveal he can transform under duress, retaining his consciousness, but only for about five minutes. Commander Erwin Smith suggests ','[{"start": 32071, "end": 35976}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Jaeger", "Hange Zoë", "Erwin Smith", "Connie Springer", "Survey Corps", "Trost siege", "Military Police", "Coup"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:45:36');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('2a35d3af86435b80d23a4fadaa5df168c7634cbd92be0a19203b2f413b6a147e','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('ith and the Survey Corps were consolidating.\n\nA coup was being planned.\n\nThe details were murky, known only to the highest levels of government, but the goal was clear: to neutralize Erwin Smith and the Survey Corps as a political force, to consolidate control over military operations, and to ensure that the nobility''s interests remained protected.\n\nEren, without knowing it, was the key to this political struggle. Whoever controlled Eren controlled the most powerful military asset humanity possessed.\n\nThe military police leadership, under the command of a tall man named Nile Dok, began to maneuver into position. Orders were issued subtly, shifting units and resources, creating the groundwork for a coordinated strike.\n\nBut Erwin, whose intelligence network was extensive and sophisticated, was aware of these movements. He began his own counter-maneuvers, positioning his people, preparing for the political confrontation that would inevitably come.\n\nEren, still recovering from his transformation training and preparing for his first mission with the Survey Corps, had no awareness of the political chess game being played with his existence as the prize.\n\n### The Wall Reclamation Mission\n\nBefore the coup could fully develop, Erwin moved forward with his plan to utilize Eren in a major military operation. He organized what was officially called a "Wall Reclamation Mission"—an attempt to re-establish military control over the outer districts of Wall Maria and to reclaim what had been lost in the initial breach.\n\nThe Survey Corps was mobilized in force, approximately seven hundred soldiers, arranged in a massive formation designed to sweep through the outer districts in a systematic pattern. The Armored Titan and other specialized creatures that had appeared in the recent past suggested that the titans were not simply mindless monsters. Coordinating a large-scale military operation, Erwin believed, might allow them to observe these creatures'' behavior patterns.\n\nEren was positioned at the center of this formation, with his elite squad surrounding him. The plan was relatively straightforward: if Eren encountered a titan that the standard soldiers couldn''t handle, he would transform and engage it directly. The soldiers would gather intelligence on his transformation and combat abilities while also achieving their tactical objectives.\n\nThe mission moved forward systematically, soldiers clearing buildings section by section, disposing of titans they encountered through coordinated assaults. It was tedious work, but it was working. The outer districts were being systematically cleared.\n\nAnd then the Armored Titan appeared.\n\nIt emerged from the rubble of a collapsed building, its armored hide making it immediately identifiable. Behind it, moving with unusual coordination, were several other titans—a nine-meter-class, a ten-meter-class, and others that seemed to be deliberately moving in support of the armored creature.\n\nErwin, observing from a vantage point, immediately recognized what this represented: a coordinated titan assault. These creatures were not acting randomly; they were attacking with apparent strategic intent.\n\nEren transformed on command, emerging from the crowded center of the military formation as a fifteen-meter-class titan. And then, in front of the entire Survey Corps, he engaged the Armored Titan in direct combat.\n\nThe fight was spectacular and terrifying. Two massive creatures, each ten times the size of a normal human, collided with forces that could level buildings. Eren''s opponent was stronger, with its armored hide providing protection that Eren''s muscles couldn''t penetrate. But Eren moved with the training of a human soldier, fighting with tactics and strategy rather than pure animal instinct.\n\nThe Armored Titan drove Eren backward, pressing its advantage. Eren felt something snap in his arm—actual broken bones, even in titan form—and the pain was surprising. He didn''t think he could be injured while transformed.','\n',char(10)),'A coup is planned to neutralize Erwin Smith and the Survey Corps, with Eren as the key political asset. Nile Dok leads the military police, but Erwin counters their moves. Erwin then leads a large-scale Wall Reclamation Mission to retake te','[{"start": 35626, "end": 39623}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Erwin Smith", "Eren", "Survey Corps", "Armored Titan", "Nile Dok", "Military Police", "Wall Reclamation Mission", "Wall Maria"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:46:20');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('49825ffb9c7ae92eee7caf02588bee11e8c1c522f4a70b20091266f0dcc1db78','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('ate. But Eren moved with the training of a human soldier, fighting with tactics and strategy rather than pure animal instinct.\n\nThe Armored Titan drove Eren backward, pressing its advantage. Eren felt something snap in his arm—actual broken bones, even in titan form—and the pain was surprising. He didn''t think he could be injured while transformed.\n\nBut as the Armored Titan pressed its advantage, Eren''s elite squad moved into action. Soldiers rushed forward with specialized equipment—long-handled tools designed for close combat with titans. Working in perfect coordination, they moved against the Armored Titan''s legs, trying to immobilize it.\n\nFor just a moment, during the chaos of the coordinated assault, Eren saw something. Inside the Armored Titan''s eye, there was a flash of something—consciousness, intelligence, recognition. And in that moment, Eren felt certain of something he couldn''t prove: the Armored Titan was not a beast. It was intelligent. It was possibly human.\n\nThe Armored Titan broke off the engagement, pulling back from Eren''s assault with surprising agility for something so massive. And then, impossibly, it began to run, moving through the urban terrain with surprising speed given its size.\n\nEren moved to pursue, but exhaustion was setting in. His transformation had lasted several minutes already, longer than the initial tests had suggested. His body was beginning to strain, beginning to shut down.\n\nThe Armored Titan escaped, disappearing into the distance with the other supporting titans, leaving Eren in the midst of the Survey Corps, weakening as his transformation came to an end.\n\nAs he reverted to human form, consciousness fading, Eren''s last thought was not of victory but of mystery. What was the Armored Titan? How could it move so strategically? And most importantly, was it possible that everything humanity knew about the titans was built on a fundamental misunderstanding?\n\n## Part Five: Secrets and Revelations\n\n### The Female Titan\n\nSix months passed. Eren recovered from his injuries, slowly building his strength back, learning to control his transformation better through continued training and exposure. The Survey Corps conducted regular missions beyond the walls, each one serving Erwin''s dual purpose: gathering intelligence about the titans and the world while also conducting military operations to reclaim territory.\n\nBut something was wrong. The titans seemed to be adapting. Where previously the Survey Corps could mount systematic operations with acceptable casualty rates, they now found themselves ambushed and targeted. Titans that should have been ranging randomly instead seemed to position themselves strategically to intercept Survey Corps missions.\n\nThe losses mounted. Soldiers who had survived multiple campaigns began to die under mysterious circumstances. Scouts reported seeing titans that didn''t behave like normal creatures. One scout reported seeing a titan that moved with what he described as "too much intelligence, too much purpose."\n\nAnd then, on a reconnaissance mission to investigate reports of an unusual titan sighting, the Survey Corps encountered something that would shake the foundations of everything they believed.\n\nA female form emerged from the trees—a Female Titan, as she would come to be called, approximately eight-meter-class, with a somewhat feminine upper body structure and a startling level of tactical awareness. She moved through the Survey Corps formation like a predator through prey, engaging specific soldiers with lethal precision.\n\nBut what was most shocking was her behavior. She didn''t simply kill indiscriminately; she seemed to be hunting for something specific. She would engage a group of soldiers, eliminate them, then move on to the next group, as though searching for a particular target.','\n',char(10)),'Eren battles the Armored Titan, which shows intelligence, and later encounters the Female Titan, who hunts with purpose, raising questions about titan nature.','[{"start": 39273, "end": 43091}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Armored Titan", "Female Titan", "Survey Corps", "Erwin"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:46:25');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('cbb257099a4c478c0e223bdfe028862a7b7030a1d0e9e2686eb7793bcfaf5e4c','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('ion like a predator through prey, engaging specific soldiers with lethal precision.\n\nBut what was most shocking was her behavior. She didn''t simply kill indiscriminately; she seemed to be hunting for something specific. She would engage a group of soldiers, eliminate them, then move on to the next group, as though searching for a particular target.\n\nThe elites squad, with Eren transformed and ready for combat, engaged the Female Titan. Eren felt the same certainty he had experienced with the Armored Titan: this creature was intelligent. It was conscious. It was, he was certain now, human in some fundamental way.\n\nDuring their fight, the Female Titan made a deliberate choice to flee—to break off combat and retreat—when Eren gained a tactical advantage. This was not the behavior of a mindless creature. This was a calculated decision to preserve itself.\n\nEren moved to pursue, but Arwin intervened, calling him back. "It''s a trap," Arwin said, pointing to where dozens of regular titans were converging on their position. "She''s bait. She''s luring you into an ambush."\n\nEren, in his titan form, looked at the approaching regular titans and understood. The Female Titan was being used as bait to draw Eren into a situation where he could be surrounded and overwhelmed. It was a tactic designed by someone who understood both military strategy and Eren''s behavior.\n\nThe Squad retreated, with Eren covering their escape. By the time he had driven off the regular titans and reverted to human form, the Female Titan was long gone.\n\nBack at headquarters, the implications of this encounter were analyzed endlessly. The Female Titan exhibited tactical behavior that suggested intelligence. She had been positioned in a way that could only make sense if there was coordination with the other titans. And most unsettling, she seemed to have a specific objective—she was hunting for something or someone.\n\n"She was looking for Eren," Arwin realized, speaking his thought aloud during a briefing. "The entire operation was designed to locate and either capture or kill him."\n\nThis realization sent shockwaves through the military leadership. If the titans were capable of coordination, if they had objectives and goals, if they were hunting with purpose, then the entire war had changed. They were no longer fighting mindless beasts; they were fighting an intelligent enemy with strategy and resources.\n\nAnd that enemy was looking for Eren.\n\n### The Truth Emerges\n\nIt was Arwin who first began to suspect the truth, though he didn''t articulate it fully until much later. In the weeks after the Female Titan encounter, Arwin began to notice patterns. He studied the movements of the specialized titans—the Armored Titan, the Female Titan, now reports of other unusual creatures—and he began to map their locations against the Survey Corps'' known missions.\n\nAnd then he found something that shouldn''t have been there: a strategic map, hidden in Bertolt Hoover''s quarters. The map showed military positions, survey routes, and notation about titans'' locations that was far too detailed and accurate to have been compiled through random observation.\n\nArwin took the map to Eren with shaking hands. "Bertolt," he said simply. "He''s been feeding information to someone."\n\nEren''s response was immediate and visceral. "Get Reiner. Bring him in for questioning."\n\nBut when soldiers went to retrieve Reiner and Bertolt for interrogation, they found the barracks empty. A message was left behind—not a note, but a message spelled out in physical objects: an arrow pointing away from the camp, toward Wall Maria, toward the outer districts.\n\nReiner Braun and Bertolt Hoover had defected.\n\nWorse, they had taken with them detailed intelligence about the Survey Corps'' operations, the soldier capabilities, and most damning of all, critical information about Eren''s transformation abilities and limitations.','\n',char(10)),'The Female Titan demonstrates intelligent, tactical behavior during combat, hunting specifically for Eren. Arwin discovers evidence that Reiner and Bertolt have been spying and defecting, revealing that the titans are coordinated and target','[{"start": 42741, "end": 46633}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Arwin", "Female Titan", "Armored Titan", "Bertolt Hoover", "Reiner Braun", "Survey Corps", "Wall Maria"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:46:30');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('74faa82f16f351a94ab67ea1bcf2ba7d6a0f2aefe6e5ad65495635f1ad9b4ca9','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace(' an arrow pointing away from the camp, toward Wall Maria, toward the outer districts.\n\nReiner Braun and Bertolt Hoover had defected.\n\nWorse, they had taken with them detailed intelligence about the Survey Corps'' operations, the soldier capabilities, and most damning of all, critical information about Eren''s transformation abilities and limitations.\n\nThe implications were staggering. Reiner and Bertolt, who had been trained alongside Eren, who had fought in his unit, who had been integrated into the elite squad—they were traitors. But more than that, they represented the organized intelligence gathering behind the specialized titans.\n\nThe connection was made in a series of urgent meetings: the Armored Titan''s movements matched Reiner''s patrol schedules. The timing of coordinated titan attacks matched Bertolt''s position reports. The specialized titans represented an organized force, with objectives and planning.\n\nAnd that force was hunting Eren.\n\n### The Colossal''s Secret\n\nIn investigating Bertolt''s quarters, soldiers found more than just a strategic map. They found personal effects, letters, and most importantly, a journal that detailed Bertolt''s thoughts and experiences.\n\nThe journal was written in Bertolt''s hand, but the observations within revealed something shocking: Bertolt knew about titans. He knew things about their nature, their biology, their creation that shouldn''t have been common knowledge. He made references to a "mission" and to "coordinating with assigned units."\n\nHange, examining the journal with intense focus, looked up at Erwin with an expression of dawning understanding. "He wasn''t a soldier who defected," she said. "He was a spy, implanted from the beginning. Both of them were. They were soldiers from the beginning, but not human soldiers. Or not... not just soldiers."\n\nThe hypothesis that emerged from this analysis was almost too impossible to believe: Reiner and Bertolt had been implanted within the military specifically to gain intelligence about Eren and to coordinate with the other specialized titans. They were, in essence, double agents for an organized intelligence operation that existed outside of humanity''s known civilization.\n\nAnd if they had been implanted, if they had been trained as soldiers alongside everyone else, if they had been present for all the key moments and transitions—then they might have information about the titans'' origins, their purpose, and their ultimate goals.\n\nErwin''s response was swift and strategic. The military was reorganized. Several soldiers came under suspicion of being implants or collaborators. Interrogations were conducted. And all the while, the pieces of a far larger puzzle were beginning to come together.\n\nThe titans were not a natural disaster. They were a constructed enemy, created or controlled by an organized intelligence. And Eren, in his ability to transform, represented either the key to understanding that intelligence or a threat to those who controlled it.\n\n### The Battle of Shiganshina\n\nThe strategic situation was becoming critical. With Reiner and Bertolt''s defection, the Survey Corps had lost one of its most experienced teams, but more importantly, they had lost the element of surprise. Their operations could no longer be kept secret from an organized enemy that had infiltrated their ranks.\n\nErwin decided to take the offensive. He planned a massive incursion into the outer districts, a sweep that would be designed to draw out the specialized titans and engage them in direct combat. The goal was to capture or identify their leadership, to understand what was being coordinated.\n\nThis mission would take place in Shiganshina District, the section of Wall Maria where the original breach had occurred five years previously. It was a symbolic choice—to retake the site of humanity''s greatest shame and loss.','\n',char(10)),'Reiner Braun and Bertolt Hoover are revealed to be traitors who defected, taking critical intelligence about Eren''s abilities and the Survey Corps. An investigation into Bertolt''s journal suggests they were implanted spies for an organized ','[{"start": 46283, "end": 50128}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Reiner Braun", "Bertolt Hoover", "Eren", "Survey Corps", "Armored Titan", "Colossal Titan", "Erwin", "Hange"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:46:36');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('7208b8cf09f1b72c885b5b1f47eea82f2ae40867eab3c323fcd106a8a092b170','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('gage them in direct combat. The goal was to capture or identify their leadership, to understand what was being coordinated.\n\nThis mission would take place in Shiganshina District, the section of Wall Maria where the original breach had occurred five years previously. It was a symbolic choice—to retake the site of humanity''s greatest shame and loss.\n\nThe Survey Corps mobilized in force, approximately thirteen hundred soldiers. Eren, with his elite squad, was positioned as the main fighting force. Additional units were arranged in strategic positions to intercept any titans attempting to retreat or to flank the main assault.\n\nThe plan was comprehensive and detailed, drawn up by Erwin himself with input from the most experienced commanders. It should have worked. It should have been a comprehensive victory.\n\nInstead, it was an ambush from the very beginning.\n\nAs the Survey Corps moved into Shiganshina, they found the district already occupied by titans—far more titans than any natural population would suggest. And they were arranged strategically, positioned in ways that could only have been coordinated by an intelligence that understood military tactics.\n\nThe Armored Titan appeared, leading an organized assault. The Female Titan emerged from a different direction, cutting off a retreat path. And above the district, creating an ominous shadow, appeared the Colossal Titan once again.\n\nThe Colossal Titan''s appearance was different this time, however. It didn''t simply breach the wall; it didn''t simply vanish. Instead, it stood there, directly above the Survey Corps, steam rising from its massive form, and then it began to lean backward deliberately.\n\nThose who understood military strategy realized what was happening: the Colossal Titan was falling backward, its massive weight about to come down on top of the Survey Corps formation.\n\nErwin, observing from a vantage point, realized in that moment that this entire operation had been a trap designed specifically to eliminate him and the leadership of the Survey Corps. He had been outmaneuvered by an enemy he still didn''t fully understand.\n\nEren transformed to try to push the Colossal Titan aside, but he couldn''t generate enough force. The massive creature fell, creating an explosion of devastation in the center of the Survey Corps formation.\n\nHundreds of soldiers were crushed. Entire squads were obliterated. Commanders were killed. In that moment, in that single action, the Survey Corps was broken.\n\nAnd in the confusion and chaos, something else happened. A figure emerged from the carnage—a girl, young, maybe late teens, with shoulder-length blonde hair and a confused expression. She appeared to be searching for something or someone among the wreckage.\n\nThis was Annie Leonhart, who had been unremarkable in her early military training, quickly forgotten, but who had never truly left the military structure. She had been embedded, waiting, becoming the Female Titan when necessary, performing her assigned tasks.\n\nEren, his rage at absolute peak, moved toward her. They collided, with Eren reaching for Annie and Annie transforming deliberately, summoning her own titan form to meet his assault.\n\nTheir fight was brutal and personal, but Eren''s rage was starting to make him careless. In the chaos of their combat, Annie managed to pin Eren''s arm, and then she did something that shocked everyone: she began to move toward the wall, dragging Eren with her.\n\nUnderstanding what she was attempting, Eren''s squad moved to intercept, but they were too late. Annie reached the wall and began to climb, dragging Eren''s titan form upward, pulling him away from his support and toward the top of the barrier.\n\nAt the wall''s apex, with the entire District visible below them, Annie''s transformation ended. She was human again, vulnerable, at the top of the wall. Eren, still in his titan form but smaller now, reached for her.','\n',char(10)),'The Survey Corps launches a mission to retake Shiganshina District, aiming to capture enemy leadership, but is ambushed by the Armored, Female, and Colossal Titans. The Colossal Titan''s attack decimates the Corps, while Annie Leonhart emerg','[{"start": 49778, "end": 53685}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Annie Leonhart", "Erwin", "Colossal Titan", "Armored Titan", "Female Titan", "Survey Corps", "Shiganshina District"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:46:39');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('c1ed3430ddd43e5236e6f7f1731476ef3fd2fa2ab41f7db23bf792520ab85656','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace(' the wall and began to climb, dragging Eren''s titan form upward, pulling him away from his support and toward the top of the barrier.\n\nAt the wall''s apex, with the entire District visible below them, Annie''s transformation ended. She was human again, vulnerable, at the top of the wall. Eren, still in his titan form but smaller now, reached for her.\n\nWhat happened next was never entirely clear. Some reports suggested that Annie deliberately fell backward, attempting to end her own life rather than be captured. Others suggested that she was knocked backward by Eren''s movement. What was certain was that Annie fell backward into the inner wall, falling dozens of meters toward the ground below.\n\nShe impacted the ground with crushing force, but somehow, her body remained intact. Conscious or unconscious, no one could determine. Erwin''s soldiers moved to secure her, to take her prisoner for interrogation.\n\nBut the battle wasn''t over. The Armored Titan was still fighting. The Colossal Titan was recovering. And the regular titans were closing in.\n\nEren, exhausted from multiple transformations, reverted to human form. Around him, the Survey Corps was attempting to organize a retreat, but the casualties had been catastrophic. Hundreds of soldiers were dead or dying. The mission had failed, despite the incredible effort and sacrifice.\n\nAs they pulled back toward Wall Rose, carrying Annie''s unconscious form with them, Erwin''s expression was grim. This battle was a defeat, but it was also an revelation. The titans were not a natural phenomenon. They were orchestrated. They were being controlled or coordinated by an intelligence that understood human military tactics, human psychology, and human weakness.\n\nAnd that intelligence was still out there, still operating in the world beyond the walls, still planning something that Erwin didn''t yet understand.\n\n## Part Six: Walls and Truths\n\n### The Investigation of Annie\n\nAnnie Leonhart regained consciousness in a specialized holding cell, designed for containment of potentially dangerous individuals. She was isolated from the general population, kept under heavy guard, and subjected to multiple interrogation sessions.\n\nBut Annie refused to speak. Through hours of questioning, she said almost nothing, remaining silent with a composure that was unnerving to her interrogators. When she did speak, her responses were cryptic and revelatory only in their evasion.\n\n"Who were you coordinating with?" commanders demanded.\n\n"I don''t know what you mean," she replied.\n\n"We know you''re the Female Titan. We know you''re not human—or you''re not entirely human. Why were you attacking us? What do you want?"\n\n"I was just a soldier doing my duty," she said with a small, sad smile.\n\nDespite the interrogation techniques used—some of them bordering on torture—Annie provided no actionable intelligence. She seemed almost resigned to her capture, as though this had always been an expected outcome.\n\nHange, however, found her fascinating. The scientist pushed for extended observation periods, for psychological evaluation, for any opportunity to study the girl. Through these observations, Hange began to develop a profile: Annie was not a mindless monster. She was intelligent, educated, trained. She had been raised within the walls, had lived as a human, had suffered and struggled like any other soldier.\n\nBut she had a secret. A fundamental transformation, a duality to her nature that she kept hidden or controlled with an iron will.\n\nIn one particularly telling interrogation session, Eren confronted Annie directly.\n\n"Why did you do it?" he asked, his voice barely controlled rage. "You were one of us. You trained with us. You fought beside us."\n\nAnnie looked at him with eyes that seemed to carry a weight beyond her apparent age. "I was following orders," she said simply. "Just like you are following orders now."\n\n"I''m not following orders to become a monster," Eren shot back.','\n',char(10)),'After a battle, Annie Leonhart is captured and held for interrogation. She remains silent during questioning, while Hange studies her and Eren confronts her about her betrayal. The text reveals that the titans are being controlled by an int','[{"start": 53335, "end": 57281}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Annie Leonhart", "Eren", "Hange", "Erwin", "Female Titan", "Armored Titan", "Colossal Titan", "Survey Corps"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:47:20');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('2fa18e657d0b4dddb45f74dbd8e6b8fec517e4eb551fac6bdc5fd57c46ecf2e8','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace(' it?" he asked, his voice barely controlled rage. "You were one of us. You trained with us. You fought beside us."\n\nAnnie looked at him with eyes that seemed to carry a weight beyond her apparent age. "I was following orders," she said simply. "Just like you are following orders now."\n\n"I''m not following orders to become a monster," Eren shot back.\n\n"Aren''t you?" Annie replied quietly. "You''re a weapon. You''re being used just as surely as I was being used. You''re just too invested in your own mythology to see it."\n\nAfter this exchange, Eren left the interrogation chamber without getting the answers he sought. But Annie''s words haunted him, raising questions about his own agency and purpose.\n\n### The Revelation\n\nIt was Arwin who finally obtained a breakthrough, through means that were questionable but ultimately effective. Through careful study of Annie''s psychological profile and her weaknesses, Arwin managed to get her to open up during a moment of emotional vulnerability.\n\nWhat Annie revealed, haltingly and with obvious reluctance, recontextualized everything.\n\nShe was not a spy in the traditional sense. She was a soldier—a warrior from a civilization that existed beyond the walls, from a nation or organization that controlled multiple titans through a method that was apparently capable of creating warriors like herself and like Bertolt and Reiner.\n\n"We were sent here," she explained, her voice quiet and measured. "We were supposed to investigate the walls, to understand the military structure, to gather intelligence. And we were supposed to find the coordinate. The person with the memories. The key to everything."\n\n"The coordinate?" Arwin pressed.\n\n"That''s all I know. There''s someone in these walls, someone with abilities or knowledge that''s critical. We were supposed to find them and retrieve them."\n\n"Eren," Arwin realized.\n\n"Maybe," Annie said. "Or maybe someone else. Someone older, someone whose memories matter."\n\nThis revelation opened entirely new lines of inquiry. If there was an organized group working to find a specific person, a person with critical knowledge or abilities, then the entire military structure needed to be reconsidered.\n\nErwin, on receiving this information, initiated a broad investigation into the personnel records of the Survey Corps, the Garrison, and the military police. He was looking for someone who fit a profile: someone who had appeared unexpectedly, someone whose background didn''t quite add up, someone who might be connected to the titans'' origins.\n\nThe investigation was subtle and careful, as Erwin had learned that there were infiltrators within the military. But slowly, a profile emerged.\n\n### The Underground\n\nThere was a man named Rod Reiss. He held no official position, had no military rank, but he maintained a subtle influence over the military police leadership through connections to the nobility. His background was obscure—or rather, it was officially recorded but suspiciously incomplete.\n\nInvestigation revealed that Rod Reiss had a family connection to one of the most powerful noble houses in the interior regions. And more importantly, he had genetic connections to the original military leadership that had founded humanity''s current civilization.\n\nWhen Erwin''s people finally located Rod Reiss, they found him in the most unexpected place: the underground regions beneath the walls, in a section that officially didn''t exist in any military records.\n\nBeneath the innermost wall, the investigation revealed, was an entire civilization. Hidden from the outside world, unknown to the vast majority of humanity, there was a section of the original city that had been preserved and maintained in secret. And in this underground region, there were facilities—research facilities, storage facilities, living quarters—that suggested a level of organization and planning that predated the walls themselves.','\n',char(10)),'Annie reveals she and her comrades were sent to find ''the coordinate'' - a person with critical abilities or memories within the walls, possibly Eren or someone else. Erwin investigates and discovers Rod Reiss, connected to noble houses and ','[{"start": 56931, "end": 60829}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Annie Leonhart", "Eren Yeager", "Armin Arlert", "Erwin Smith", "Rod Reiss", "Bertolt Hoover", "Reiner Braun", "the coordinate"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:47:24');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('d82831cddeaec76c68e85e86d400303c65c632a9625095f9284e822068edef03','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('the outside world, unknown to the vast majority of humanity, there was a section of the original city that had been preserved and maintained in secret. And in this underground region, there were facilities—research facilities, storage facilities, living quarters—that suggested a level of organization and planning that predated the walls themselves.\n\nAmong the materials found in these underground facilities were documents. Old documents, written in a script that had to be deciphered by scholars, but documents that provided context and history.\n\nThe story they told was staggering.\n\nHumanity had not been driven to the brink of extinction by titans. Titans had been created. Engineered. Constructed as weapons by a people who had lived before the walls were built, before the world was supposedly reset.\n\nThere was a nation—they had various names in the documents, but "Marley" was the designation that appeared most frequently. Marley was an organized military and political entity that had engineered titan-warriors as biological weapons. Bertolt, Reiner, and Annie were among these titan-warriors—soldiers who had been trained to transform into titan forms, to serve as weapons in Marley''s conflicts.\n\nThe walls had been constructed not as a defense against some natural disaster of titans, but as a strategic barrier to protect a hidden population—a population that was significant enough and influential enough to warrant this extraordinary measure. The wall building was an act of deliberate separation, creating isolation between the free humans within the walls and the broader world controlled by Marley.\n\nBut why? Why would Marley create walls to contain a population? What was so significant about the humans within the walls that they needed to be separated, contained, controlled?\n\nThe answer lay in another document—a series of them, actually—that referenced something called the "Founding Titan."\n\n### The Founding Titan\n\nAccording to the documents, there existed a titan—not a creature, but a being—with capabilities beyond anything else in existence. This being, designated the Founding Titan, had abilities that could alter the physical nature of titans themselves. This being could command titans, could modify their forms, could essentially control the entire titan population through some form of biological imperative.\n\nAnd this being was within the walls.\n\nThe original construction of the walls was not merely a physical barrier; it was also a biological lock. The Founding Titan was imprisoned within the walls, contained behind the barriers, unable to leave, unable to access the world outside.\n\nAnd if Marley''s warriors, if Reiner and Bertolt and Annie and the others, had been infiltrated into the military, it was specifically to locate the Founding Titan—to find this imprisoned being and either release it or eliminate it.\n\nThe documents were unclear about which objective was the priority.\n\nEren, on learning this, experienced a profound sense of dislocation. He had always believed himself to be just a soldier, someone with an unusual ability. But what if he was something more? What if his transformation, his unusual capacity for consciousness while in titan form, was evidence of something fundamental about his nature?\n\n"We need to test him," Hange urged Erwin. "If there''s a possibility that Eren is connected to the Founding Titan, we need to understand the parameters of his abilities."\n\nBut Erwin was more cautious. "If Eren is the Founding Titan, or if he has some connection to it, then revealing this could make him a target. We need to be very careful about how we proceed."\n\n### The March to the Walls','\n',char(10)),'A secret underground city beneath the walls contains ancient documents revealing that Titans were engineered by Marley as biological weapons. The walls were built not for defense but to imprison the Founding Titan, a being with control over','[{"start": 60479, "end": 64131}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Founding Titan", "Marley", "Bertolt", "Reiner", "Annie", "Hange", "Erwin"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:47:29');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('049d18b69224000c190d0f7f2cd414348e100eee70c65e196d0d1ca670b9e4db','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('. "If there''s a possibility that Eren is connected to the Founding Titan, we need to understand the parameters of his abilities."\n\nBut Erwin was more cautious. "If Eren is the Founding Titan, or if he has some connection to it, then revealing this could make him a target. We need to be very careful about how we proceed."\n\n### The March to the Walls\n\nThe revelation of the underground civilization and the documents it contained triggered a crisis within the military hierarchy. The nobility, who had maintained the underground facilities and the secrets they contained, now found their secret exposed. And the military police, who had been serving the nobility''s interests, found their authority questioned.\n\nA military coup was narrowly averted through careful political maneuvering by Erwin. But the fundamental nature of the military had changed. The organization could no longer simply fight titans; it now had to grapple with the reality that there was an organized human civilization beyond the walls that was actively working against them.\n\nThe priority shifted from random exploration and titan subjugation to information gathering and strategic defense. Erwin began a methodical process of identifying and removing infiltrators from the military structure.\n\nBut there was another complication: Rod Reiss, the man at the center of the underground civilization, was missing. When soldiers went to apprehend him, they found his chambers empty except for one thing—another message, this one a written statement.\n\nThe statement, written in Rod Reiss''s hand, explained that he was taking measures to ensure humanity''s survival. He referenced the Founding Titan and suggested that he was moving to take control of or contact this entity directly. The statement also suggested that not all of humanity was united in its desire to preserve the wall civilization—that there were factions within the nobility and the military that had different objectives.\n\nAnd then, three days after the statement was discovered, reports came in from the outer districts: there was a massive titan in the region, far larger than any previously recorded. This titan was approximately sixty meters tall—similar in size to the Colossal Titan, but shaped differently, with a more robust and muscular form.\n\nThis was the Beast Titan, and according to the reports, it was accompanied by a small army of regular titans. It moved with clear intent, moving toward the inner walls, moving toward Wall Rose.\n\nThe military mobilized in response, attempting to intercept this new threat. But the Beast Titan was incredibly powerful, capable of projecting rocks at opponents with accuracy and force, capable of organizing the regular titans like an army commander might direct troops.\n\nIn the chaos of the conflict, Eren once again transformed and engaged the Beast Titan directly. The fight was brutal and fierce, but Eren''s rage and his determination to protect the people within the walls drove him forward.\n\nThe Beast Titan had combat experience equal to Eren''s, however, and the battle was a stalemate. Neither side could gain a decisive advantage. But as the fight continued, Eren realized something: the Beast Titan had emotional responses to the combat. It showed frustration. It showed what might have been sadness.\n\nAnd when Eren finally managed to land a decisive blow, knocking the Beast Titan backward and forcing it to revert to human form from exhaustion, Eren found himself staring at a man he recognized.\n\nIt was Zeke—a man whose face was familiar but whose context was unknown. Zeke, who somehow Eren knew, somehow Eren had a memory of, though that memory seemed impossible.\n\n## Part Seven: The Breaking Point\n\n### Awakening Memories\n\nIn the moments after Zeke reverted to human form, before soldiers rushed forward to apprehend him, something happened to Eren. A surge of something—memory, knowledge, sensation—flooded through his consciousness.','\n',char(10)),'Following the discovery of an underground civilization and documents revealing a connection between Eren and the Founding Titan, military tensions rise as Rod Reiss disappears and a massive Beast Titan attacks, leading Eren to confront it i','[{"start": 63781, "end": 67716}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Founding Titan", "Erwin", "Rod Reiss", "Beast Titan", "Zeke", "military coup", "underground civilization"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:47:33');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('6b96f70f93498207184c1f5d12bedbd2172c9891c363cc5ddda27fe98d4be85b','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('Eren knew, somehow Eren had a memory of, though that memory seemed impossible.\n\n## Part Seven: The Breaking Point\n\n### Awakening Memories\n\nIn the moments after Zeke reverted to human form, before soldiers rushed forward to apprehend him, something happened to Eren. A surge of something—memory, knowledge, sensation—flooded through his consciousness.\n\nHe saw images that weren''t his own memories but seemed to be implanted in his mind. He saw the outside world, beyond the walls, a sprawling landscape of civilizations and warfare. He saw Marley—a massive nation with its own military, its own political structure, its own goals and ambitions.\n\nHe saw a family—a family he recognized but had no context for recognizing. He saw a woman and a man in a different setting, in clothes from before the walls. He saw himself, but not as Eren Yeager. He saw himself as something else, someone else, with a different name and a different life.\n\nAnd he saw Zeke—Zeke, who was somehow family, somehow connected to him through blood and through history.\n\nWhen Eren collapsed, unconscious, Hange rushed to examine him. "What happened?" she demanded. "Did the transformation cause an injury?"\n\nBut there was no physical injury. Eren''s body was fine. What had happened was internal, psychological, perhaps even spiritual.\n\nWhen Eren regained consciousness hours later, he found Arwin sitting beside him, waiting with the patience that had always characterized their friendship.\n\n"I remember," Eren said immediately, his voice hollow. "I remember something that I shouldn''t remember. I remember things from before."\n\n"Before what?" Arwin asked carefully.\n\n"Before I was Eren Yeager," he said. "Before I came to these walls. Before everything."\n\nArwin''s expression didn''t change, but his grip on Eren''s shoulder tightened. "We need to tell Erwin."\n\n### The Founding''s Power\n\nThe information that Eren provided, based on these returning memories, was fragmentary and unclear, but it was enough to begin constructing a new narrative.\n\nEren was not simply a boy who had been born within the walls. Eren Yeager was a persona, a constructed identity given to someone who had arrived within the walls carrying a critical secret: the genetic and spiritual legacy of the Founding Titan.\n\nThere was a family—a family with a specific genetic lineage. This family possessed the ability to inherit and transmit the power of the titans through blood. The Founding Titan itself was not a person but a power, a biological and supernatural force that could be wielded by those with the appropriate genetic background.\n\nEren had been sent into the walls as a child with a specific mission: to locate and unlock the Founding Titan, to find a way to use its power to free humanity or to protect humanity or—the documents were unclear about the end goal.\n\nBut the presence of the Founding Titan within the walls was not a simple thing. It was complicated by the existence of another member of the family—the Beast Titan user, Zeke—who had his own agenda and his own understanding of what should be done with the Founding Titan''s power.\n\nZeke, upon regaining consciousness after his capture, was remarkably calm and philosophical about his situation. When interrogated, he spoke openly, almost eagerly, about the nature of the titans and the true situation humanity faced.\n\n"You''re all slaves," he said to the military leaders who questioned him. "You''re slaves to a power you don''t understand, trapped in walls built to contain a force that one family has been using to manipulate and control you for centuries."\n\n"The titans are weapons of war," Erwin replied. "Made by Marley, sent to infiltrate and destroy us."\n\n"No," Zeke said, shaking his head. "Titans are far older than Marley. Marley simply learned how to weaponize them. The true origins of the titans go back further than any of your histories record. And the family with the power—my family—we''ve been managing that power for generations."','\n',char(10)),'After Zeke reverts to human form, Eren experiences a flood of foreign memories showing Marley, a family, and his connection to Zeke, revealing he was sent into the walls with the Founding Titan''s legacy. Zeke, captured, calmly explains the ','[{"start": 67366, "end": 71330}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Yeager", "Zeke", "Marley", "Founding Titan", "Armin Arlert", "Hange Zoë"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:47:39');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('d9750f6381529ad2babd1136d25f87a68c4911787ac9ef4086ea384798acd5be','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('n replied. "Made by Marley, sent to infiltrate and destroy us."\n\n"No," Zeke said, shaking his head. "Titans are far older than Marley. Marley simply learned how to weaponize them. The true origins of the titans go back further than any of your histories record. And the family with the power—my family—we''ve been managing that power for generations."\n\n"Your family sent infiltrators to assassinate our soldiers and capture Eren," Arwin interjected angrily.\n\nZeke smiled sadly. "My family sent warriors to complete a mission. Some of them succeeded in their infiltration. Some of them, like Annie, were captured. And some of them, like Bertolt, died serving a cause they only partially understood."\n\nThis information was valuable, but it raised more questions than it answered. If Marley hadn''t created the titans, where had they come from? If the family that Eren and Zeke belonged to had controlled the power for generations, what was the source of that power? And most critically, what were the limitations of the Founding Titan''s abilities?\n\n### The Rumbling\n\nIt was Zeke who provided the answer to the last question, and his answer recontextualized everything the military had been struggling with.\n\n"The Founder can control titans," Zeke explained. "That''s the primary power. But there''s another power, something more primal. The Founder can move the earth. The Founder can command a force that sleeps within the walls themselves."\n\n"Explain," Erwin demanded.\n\n"The walls aren''t just stone," Zeke said. "They''re reinforced with a material that''s been... prepared. Treated. Inside the walls, interwoven with their very structure, are titans. Titans embedded in the stone, maintaining the barriers. If the Founding Titan were to awaken fully, were to exert its complete power, those titans would emerge. The walls themselves would collapse. And everything—every person, every civilization, everything within the walls—would be crushed."\n\nThe implications of this revelation were staggering. The walls that had protected humanity for centuries, that they believed were inert structures, were actually alive. They were composed partially of titan material, maintained by some form of active biological process.\n\nAnd the Founding Titan had the power to destroy them completely.\n\nErwin''s expression became grave. "Then we must ensure that the Founding Titan does not have a reason to emerge."\n\n"Or," Zeke replied with a slight smile, "we must ensure that when it emerges, it does so under controlled circumstances, with a purpose we can guide."\n\n### Civil Conflict\n\nThe revelation that the walls themselves were composed of and maintained by titan material triggered a political crisis. Some factions within the military and the nobility wanted to investigate this further, to study the walls and understand their construction. Others wanted to cover up the information entirely, maintaining the existing social structure.\n\nBut there was a third faction—a faction that had been present in the shadows of power for generations—that wanted to move toward the revelation that Zeke had suggested. They wanted to wake the Founding Titan. They wanted to unlock the power.\n\nThis faction, it turned out, included members of the military police leadership and several high-ranking nobles who had been secretly working toward this goal for years. They saw in the revelation of the titans'' true nature an opportunity to gain power and control that they had never possessed before.\n\nErwin, recognizing the threat, moved decisively to consolidate his power base. The Survey Corps was mobilized not for an external mission but for an internal one. Soldiers loyal to Erwin were positioned in strategic locations. Officers who were suspected of being part of the conspiracy to awaken the Founding Titan were quietly removed from their positions.\n\nBut there was one factor that Erwin hadn''t fully accounted for: Eren''s own agency in the matter.','\n',char(10)),'Zeke reveals that the walls are made of titan material and can be awakened by the Founding Titan, causing the Rumbling. This triggers a political crisis and internal power struggle within the military factions.','[{"start": 70980, "end": 74906}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Zeke", "Eren", "Arwin", "Erwin", "Annie", "Bertolt", "Marley", "Founding Titan"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:48:19');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('39a1c6291657aff25df7635eb18c99628b7999b135668a745d1b0619408196b4','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('zed not for an external mission but for an internal one. Soldiers loyal to Erwin were positioned in strategic locations. Officers who were suspected of being part of the conspiracy to awaken the Founding Titan were quietly removed from their positions.\n\nBut there was one factor that Erwin hadn''t fully accounted for: Eren''s own agency in the matter.\n\nEren, still struggling with the returned memories and the fragmented sense of identity that came with them, was not content to be controlled. He was not content to be manipulated by Erwin or by Zeke or by any faction. He wanted answers, genuine answers, about his identity and his purpose.\n\nHe sought out Zeke, demanding to be taken to him. The encounter that followed, in a secured chamber with Arwin and several guards present, was tense and revealing.\n\n"You''re my brother," Zeke said simply, upon seeing Eren''s face.\n\n"I don''t remember you," Eren replied, his fists clenched.\n\n"But you''re starting to, aren''t you? The memories are coming back. The Founding Titan''s power awakens memories across generations. As you access the power, you access the memories of all the Founding Titans that came before."\n\nEren struggled with this concept. "Why? Why would the power carry memories?"\n\n"Because the Founding Titan doesn''t just control titans," Zeke explained. "The Founding Titan connects consciousness across time and space. It links the past and the future. Every holder of the power carries within them the experiences and knowledge of every previous holder."\n\n### The Divergence\n\nIt was this information—this revelation about the nature of the Founding Titan''s power—that caused the final schism.\n\nEren realized that his goals and Zeke''s goals were fundamentally opposed. Zeke believed that the power of the Founding Titan should be used to end the cycle of warfare and suffering by using the Rumbling—the catastrophic awakening of the titans within the walls—to destroy the external world. In Zeke''s vision, the Founding Titan would activate the embedded titans and level all opposition to the wall civilization, creating a isolated world where suffering could eventually be ended.\n\nBut Eren, with the memories that were emerging, saw a different path. He believed the Founding Titan''s power should be used to genuinely free humanity, not to isolate it further, not to subject it to another form of slavery.\n\n"We need to use the power to break down the walls," Eren insisted. "To see the world beyond them, to allow humanity to understand what''s outside."\n\n"That leads only to destruction," Zeke countered. "The outside world is controlled by Marley. It''s a world of war and suffering. Isolation is the only path to peace."\n\nTheir disagreement was fundamental, and it created an opportunity for Erwin to move against Eren.\n\nErwin, who had been monitoring the conversation, moved to separate the brothers and to take Eren into military custody. The goal was clear: Erwin wanted to control the Founding Titan''s power for himself, to use it to enhance the military''s capabilities and to advance his own vision for humanity''s future.\n\nBut Arwin intervened, helping Eren escape the military facility where he was being held. It was a moment of personal loyalty overriding military duty, a moment where Arwin chose to support his childhood friend over his commanding officer.\n\nWith Arwin''s help, Eren fled into the city, pursued by military units loyal to Erwin.\n\n## Part Eight: The Final Ascension\n\n### The Path to the Founder\n\nAs Eren fled through the city and toward the interior regions, he was moving toward something he didn''t fully understand but that the awakening memories within him seemed to compel. The memories of previous Founding Titans, fragments of their experiences and knowledge, were guiding him toward a specific location.\n\nHe was being drawn to the original Wall Maria, to a location within the wall that housed something critical—something that might be the physical manifestation or the seat of the Founding Titan''s power.','\n',char(10)),'Eren confronts Zeke, learning the Founding Titan''s power connects consciousness across time, leading to their ideological split over its use. Erwin attempts to seize control, but Armin aids Eren''s escape as he is drawn toward Wall Maria.','[{"start": 74556, "end": 78552}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Zeke", "Erwin", "Armin", "Founding Titan", "Wall Maria", "Marley", "The Rumbling"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:48:25');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('362d68b57b2059f541f6096b49aa88cfa5baa07a7eee0c36e37aa3b178ab28d0','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('med to compel. The memories of previous Founding Titans, fragments of their experiences and knowledge, were guiding him toward a specific location.\n\nHe was being drawn to the original Wall Maria, to a location within the wall that housed something critical—something that might be the physical manifestation or the seat of the Founding Titan''s power.\n\nMikasa, learning of Eren''s flight and capture, had moved immediately to join him. She had always been the one person who would follow Eren without question, and that loyalty had not wavered despite everything that had transpired.\n\nTogether, Eren and Mikasa, joined by Arwin and a handful of other soldiers loyal to them rather than to the military hierarchy, moved toward the walls. What they found there was something no one had expected: evidence of the walls'' true construction, visible now that they knew to look for it.\n\nThe stone of the walls was not uniform. There were layers, sections that seemed to have been carefully constructed and maintained. And as Eren approached closer, touching the surface of the wall, he could feel the presence of the titans embedded within—he could feel their consciousness, dormant and sleeping, waiting for the Founding Titan to command them.\n\nIt was in this moment, standing before the wall with his hand against its surface, that Eren experienced a complete awakening. All the fragmented memories that had been returning to him cohesed into a complete narrative.\n\nHe remembered his previous life—before the walls, in a time when he had been part of a family that wielded the Founding Titan''s power. He remembered his father, who had consumed a previous Founding Titan and passed the power on to Eren before entering the walls and becoming the man known as Grisha Yeager. He remembered being sent into the walls as a child with the explicit mission to seek out and consume the current Founding Titan holder and to use the awakened power to accomplish a specific goal.\n\nBut he also remembered something else—something that was uniquely his own memory, not borrowed from previous Titan holders. He remembered his mother. He remembered his life within the walls. He remembered falling in love with the idea of freedom and exploration, not because it was part of his mission but because he had genuinely connected with this world and its people.\n\nAnd he realized that the previous plans for the Founding Titan, the plans made generations before he was even born, might not be aligned with what he wanted to do with the power now.\n\n### The Confrontation\n\nErwin, anticipating that Eren would seek out the walls, had positioned military units at key locations along the barriers. When Eren emerged at the location where he felt the Founding Titan''s power most strongly, soldiers were waiting.\n\nBut Eren was no longer a soldier who would submit to military authority. He was the Founding Titan, whatever that meant, and he was ready to assert that power.\n\nHe transformed, but not into a fifteen-meter-class titan like his normal transformation. This was something different—something larger, something more connected to the embedded titans in the wall itself. His transformation reached twenty meters, then twenty-five, then larger still. His body shifted and changed, becoming something that was part-human, part-titan, something that wasn''t clearly defined by the normal parameters of titan classification.\n\nIn this form, Eren could feel the presence of every titan in the area, could sense their consciousness, could command them with a thought. He could reach out with his mind and touch the titans embedded in the walls, could feel their readiness to awaken, could understand the scope of the power available to him.\n\nSoldiers fired weapons at him, but they were insignificant. Nothing could hurt him in this form, not because he was invulnerable but because he was connected to something far greater than himself.','\n',char(10)),'Eren, guided by Founding Titan memories, awakens fully to his power and identity at Wall Maria, discovering the walls'' true construction and embedded Titans. He confronts the military led by Erwin, asserting his power as the Founding Titan ','[{"start": 78202, "end": 82107}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Yeager", "Mikasa", "Armin", "Erwin", "Founding Titan", "Wall Maria", "Grisha Yeager", "Military"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:48:30');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('3105fac345964b192b6bc90982349426fcdbe19e4a323184d9d8aa8025e45c19','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('ith his mind and touch the titans embedded in the walls, could feel their readiness to awaken, could understand the scope of the power available to him.\n\nSoldiers fired weapons at him, but they were insignificant. Nothing could hurt him in this form, not because he was invulnerable but because he was connected to something far greater than himself.\n\nZeke appeared, having broken free from his confinement, transforming into the Beast Titan form as well. Brother faced brother, not in a fight but in a moment of understanding and disagreement.\n\n"You''re awakening it completely," Zeke said, his voice surprisingly calm despite being in the form of a massive titan. "You''re going to cause the Rumbling. Thousands will die."\n\n"No," Eren replied, his voice echoing with a power that seemed to come from multiple places at once. "I''m going to use the power differently. The titans won''t attack the humans. I won''t command them to attack. Instead, I''m going to command them to leave the walls. To depart. To abandon their posts in the barriers."\n\n"That''s impossible," Zeke said. "The titans are embedded in the walls. They are the walls. If they leave, the barriers will collapse."\n\n"Yes," Eren agreed. "And then humanity will face the outside world directly. Not through the walls. Not in hiding. But openly, with the knowledge and the power to understand and adapt."\n\nZeke was silent for a long moment. Then, slowly, he reverted to human form, conceding without words that this struggle between them was not his to win anymore.\n\n### The Awakening\n\nWhat followed was perhaps the most consequential moment in human history since the walls had been built.\n\nEren, fully awakened to the power of the Founding Titan, reached out with his consciousness and commanded the titans embedded in the walls. The command was not for destruction but for liberation. He told them that they were free, that they were no longer required to maintain the barriers, that they could choose what to do with their existence.\n\nThe response was immediate and overwhelming.\n\nThe titans began to emerge from the walls. They didn''t break through them violently; instead, they simply left, their forms shifting and changing as they departed from the stone barriers that had contained them for centuries. The walls, suddenly deprived of their structural support, began to collapse.\n\nThe sight was apocalyptic. Wall Maria, Wall Rose, even Wall Sina—all three barriers, which had seemed eternal and indestructible, began to crumble. Sections fell away, revealing the interior of the barriers and the empty space beyond them.\n\nMillions of humans watched as the walls that had protected them for centuries fell apart. It was a moment of absolute fear and absolute liberation at the same time.\n\nBut Eren had not abandoned his people to face annihilation. As the walls fell, he used the power of the Founding Titan to protect them. The emerging titans, rather than attacking the humans, served as barriers themselves, creating a new structure, a new protection for the population. And the knowledge embedded in Eren''s consciousness—the knowledge of every previous Founding Titan—allowed him to guide this transition with purpose and design.\n\n### The New World\n\nIn the aftermath of the wall''s collapse, humanity faced a fundamental shift in its existence.\n\nThe outside world was revealed, and it was far more complex and varied than anyone within the walls had imagined. There were civilizations, cities, societies—some hostile, some neutral, some open to contact and exchange.\n\nMarley, the nation that had sent infiltrators into the wall civilization, found itself facing a crisis. Without the isolated and contained population of the wall civilization to dominate, their strategic situation changed fundamentally. The resources they had expected to extract from the walls were no longer available in the quantities they had anticipated.','\n',char(10)),'Eren uses the Founding Titan''s power to command the wall titans to leave their positions, causing the walls to collapse and humanity to face the outside world directly, while Zeke concedes their struggle.','[{"start": 81757, "end": 85653}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Zeke", "Founding Titan", "Wall Maria", "Wall Rose", "Wall Sina", "Marley", "The Rumbling"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:48:33');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('ad7de355623108d69a7231a698ad03d292f91344d41927450f164081c2f5ccb2','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('he nation that had sent infiltrators into the wall civilization, found itself facing a crisis. Without the isolated and contained population of the wall civilization to dominate, their strategic situation changed fundamentally. The resources they had expected to extract from the walls were no longer available in the quantities they had anticipated.\n\nAnd at the center of all this change stood Eren Yeager—or rather, the consciousness that inhabited Eren''s body, a consciousness that was simultaneously Eren and the accumulated knowledge and experience of every previous Founding Titan.\n\nEren struggled with this duality. Part of him wanted to simply end the power, to release control and allow humanity to find its own path forward. But the other part of him, the part that was connected to generations of Founding Titans before him, understood that simply releasing the power would not solve the problems. It would only distribute the power among people who might be less careful with it.\n\nSo Eren maintained the connection, maintained the power, and worked to guide humanity toward a new form of civilization. One that was no longer dependent on isolation and barriers but that embraced the complexity and danger of the outside world.\n\n### The Soldier''s Burden\n\nArwin, who had followed Eren through all of this, found himself in a position of profound sadness. The childhood friend who had been by Eren''s side for so long was now separated from him by something fundamental. Eren, in accessing the Founding Titan''s power, had moved beyond the realm of normal humanity. He could not be touched by conventional weapons. He could not be killed through ordinary means. He was, in essence, immortal as long as he maintained his connection to the power.\n\nThe final conversation between them was poignant in its restraint.\n\n"I don''t know if what I''m doing is right," Eren admitted to Arwin. "I don''t know if freeing everyone from the walls and exposing them to the outside world was the correct choice."\n\n"It was your choice," Arwin replied. "That''s what matters. It was genuinely your choice, not dictated by circumstance or by the power you carry."\n\nMikasa, for her part, remained close to Eren even as he transformed into something beyond normal human comprehension. She served as his anchor to humanity, the one person he could confide in about his doubts and fears.\n\nThe Survey Corps, the Garrison, the military police—all these organizations were reorganized and reformed to serve the new reality. Hange, the scientist who had always been interested in understanding the titans, found new opportunities to study the revealed world and the mysteries it contained.\n\nThe nobles who had sought to hide the truth about the titans'' nature were removed from power. A new governmental structure was established, one that was designed to be more representative and more accountable to the population at large.\n\nAnd the infiltrators from Marley—Reiner, Bertolt, Annie—were treated with complexity. They were recognized as victims as well as agents, as individuals who had been used as tools by their own government just as surely as the humans of the wall civilization had been controlled by their hidden rulers.\n\n## Part Nine: The Complexity of Freedom\n\n### The Outside Relations\n\nThe collapse of the walls precipitated a series of crisis negotiations between the wall civilization and the external powers, particularly Marley, who had been expecting to eventually conquer and absorb the wall region into their empire.\n\nThe first diplomatic delegations from Marley arrived seeking to understand what had happened and what the intentions of the wall civilization were now that the walls had fallen. They expected to find chaos and vulnerability. Instead, they found a civilization that, though shocked and disrupted, was quickly reorganizing under the guidance of someone who appeared to possess power beyond anything Marley had ever encountered.','\n',char(10)),'After the fall of the walls, the nation that had infiltrated them faces a crisis due to lost resources. Eren Yeager, now merged with the Founding Titan''s collective consciousness, struggles with his dual nature and chooses to maintain his p','[{"start": 85303, "end": 89242}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Yeager", "Arwin", "Mikasa", "Hange", "Marley", "Founding Titan", "Survey Corps", "Wall Civilization"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:48:41');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('57eff1a5a4be7a1b4f2519a61aec8fd5d9650ef852a339b72c978b3e79fe4661','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('what had happened and what the intentions of the wall civilization were now that the walls had fallen. They expected to find chaos and vulnerability. Instead, they found a civilization that, though shocked and disrupted, was quickly reorganizing under the guidance of someone who appeared to possess power beyond anything Marley had ever encountered.\n\nEren, in his capacity as the Founding Titan, did not position himself as a dictator or ruler. Instead, he worked with the military leadership and the remaining legitimate government officials to establish a framework for negotiation with external powers. The message was clear: the wall civilization was not aggressive, but it would not submit to Marley''s dominance.\n\nThe Armored Titan—Reiner Braun—presented a particularly complex situation. He had infiltrated the wall civilization as a soldier and as a spy, but he had also genuinely bonded with his fellow soldiers, had fought alongside them, had even saved lives during the conflicts. When he learned what had transpired, when he learned that the walls had fallen and that the Founding Titan had awakened, he found himself torn between his loyalty to Marley and his genuine connections to people within the wall civilization.\n\nUltimately, Reiner chose to stay within the wall region, to work toward a peaceful resolution between Marley and the wall civilization. This decision was not without consequences; Marley declared him a traitor, but his presence as a mediator proved invaluable in the early negotiations.\n\nBertolt Hoover, who had been captured before his transformation abilities were fully understood, was eventually allowed to return to Marley, not as a prisoner but as an envoy. He carried messages from the wall civilization''s leadership to Marley''s government, explaining the new reality and proposing terms for coexistence rather than conflict.\n\nAnnie Leonhart remained imprisoned, but her status gradually shifted. As it became clear that she possessed valuable information about Marley''s operations and strategies, she was moved from a holding cell to a more formal military detention facility, where she was treated more as a prisoner of war than as a criminal.\n\nShe gradually opened up to her jailers, sharing information about Marley''s political structure, its military capabilities, and its long-term strategic goals. In exchange, she was promised fair treatment and eventual freedom, contingent on the conclusion of the hostilities between Marley and the wall civilization.\n\n### The Rumbling That Wasn''t\n\nOne of the most critical developments in the post-wall period was the revelation that Eren had not actually activated the Rumbling—had not caused the apocalyptic destruction of the world that was technically within his power to command.\n\nThe embedded titans had departed the walls, but they had done so peacefully, simply walking away from their posts and departing into the world. Some eventually came into contact with human populations and had to be managed or dealt with, but they did not attack systematically or en masse.\n\nThis decision—to not use the power in the most destructive way possible—was recognized by some as merciful and wise. Others saw it as a missed opportunity to remove all threats to the wall civilization''s existence.\n\nEren himself was uncertain about the choice. In the moments when he accessed the memories of previous Founding Titans, he could see scenarios where they had used the power more destructively, where they had removed obstacles through overwhelming force. Those memories suggested that such actions were possible, that such a path had been walked before.\n\nBut Eren''s humanity—his genuine connection to the people around him, his love for Mikasa, his friendship with Arwin, his respect for Hange''s scientific curiosity—had led him to choose a different path.\n\n"I could have ended everyone''s problems by destroying everything," he said to Arwin one night, months after the walls had fallen. "Do you think I should have?"','\n',char(10)),'After the walls fell, the Founding Titan Eren Jaeger refused to use the Rumbling for mass destruction, choosing instead to negotiate with Marley. Key figures like Reiner Braun and Bertolt Hoover navigated loyalties, while Annie Leonhart sha','[{"start": 88892, "end": 92886}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Jaeger", "Reiner Braun", "Bertolt Hoover", "Annie Leonhart", "Marley", "The Rumbling", "Mikasa", "Armin"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:49:19');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('b2362f2e04d300c7fe8abb0264f308f34267963a782089806f63fb50b0885091','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('umanity—his genuine connection to the people around him, his love for Mikasa, his friendship with Arwin, his respect for Hange''s scientific curiosity—had led him to choose a different path.\n\n"I could have ended everyone''s problems by destroying everything," he said to Arwin one night, months after the walls had fallen. "Do you think I should have?"\n\nArwin was quiet for a long time before answering. "I think," he said finally, "that we have to live with the problems we create or don''t create. If you had destroyed everything, you would have lived forever in a world you created through that destruction. This way, you get to live in a world that people have built together, with all its messiness and imperfection."\n\n### The Military Transition\n\nThe transition from a wall-based military to an open-world military required fundamental restructuring. Soldiers who had been trained to fight on walls and in confined spaces had to learn new tactics for open-field combat. Soldiers who had been trained in specific formations and patterns had to adapt to more fluid and complex combat scenarios.\n\nThe elite squad that had surrounded Eren—Mikasa, Arwin, Jean, Sasha, Connie, and others—became the core of a new training program designed to prepare soldiers for the new reality. These soldiers, who had fought in multiple campaigns and had survived encounters with specialized titans, now served as instructors and leaders for the next generation of military personnel.\n\nHange, having been promoted to a higher rank in the reorganized military, established a new department: the Department of Planetary Exploration and Relations. This department was tasked with mapping the outside world, understanding the civilizations that existed there, and establishing peaceful contact with them.\n\nThe Survey Corps, once a organization focused on fighting titans within specific boundaries, became something more like a diplomatic and exploratory organization, with a secondary military function.\n\nErwin Smith, the ambitious military leader who had attempted to control the Founding Titan''s power for himself, found his authority significantly diminished in the aftermath of Eren''s awakening. He was technically still a commander, but the military structure had shifted such that power was distributed more broadly. Erwin, who had always been willing to make sacrifices in service of his grand plans, found that his plans had been superseded by events beyond his control.\n\nHe served out his remaining years in the military with competence and professionalism, but there was a sense that his moment had passed, that the grand designs he had orchestrated had been completed or rendered obsolete by the revelation of the Founding Titan and the Eren''s choices.\n\n### Personal Transformations\n\nThe aftermath of the wall''s collapse forced every person who had been involved in the events to reconsider their understanding of the world and their place in it.\n\nArwin, having sacrificed his military career to help Eren escape Erwin''s forces, found himself working in a supportive role to the new civilian government. He was instrumental in establishing early protocols for the negotiation with external powers and for the management of the transition from a militaristic to a more balanced civilization.\n\nMikasa, having spent her entire life focused on protecting Eren, found that her protective instincts were no longer as critical or as welcome. Eren, in his role as the Founding Titan, was beyond the threat of ordinary harm. She had to learn to support him in new ways, to be his emotional anchor rather than his physical protector.\n\nThis transition was difficult for her. Her entire identity had been built around Eren, around being the one who would save him, who would die for him if necessary. When that role was no longer needed, she struggled with questions of purpose and meaning.','\n',char(10)),'After the walls fall, characters from Attack on Titan navigate personal and military transformations: Eren reflects on his choice not to destroy the world, Armin helps with diplomacy, Mikasa adjusts her role, Hange leads planetary explorati','[{"start": 92536, "end": 96405}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Armin", "Mikasa", "Hange", "Erwin Smith", "Survey Corps", "Founding Titan"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:49:25');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('76cfdf20e8a25a65841eef7b017e799c619a1756928c80e0d03d1200a6c1b38d','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('earn to support him in new ways, to be his emotional anchor rather than his physical protector.\n\nThis transition was difficult for her. Her entire identity had been built around Eren, around being the one who would save him, who would die for him if necessary. When that role was no longer needed, she struggled with questions of purpose and meaning.\n\nBut gradually, she found new purpose. She began to work with the military''s diplomatic corps, using her skills in fighting and movement to establish protocols for first contact with unknown civilizations. She became a symbol of the wall civilization''s willingness to engage with the outside world, not as a conquered people but as a culture with something to contribute.\n\nJean Kirstein, the pragmatic soldier with leadership instincts, found himself rising quickly through the military hierarchy. His tactical mind and his ability to connect with soldiers across ranks made him an excellent commander. Within a few years, he had been promoted to colonel and was leading major military operations designed to ensure the wall civilization''s security in the new world.\n\nSasha Blouse, who had always been somewhat irreverent and casual about military structure, found herself struggling to adapt to the more formal diplomatic protocols that governed interactions between civilizations. But her genuine good nature and her authentic interest in different cultures made her an excellent liaison, and she eventually became one of the primary contacts between the wall civilization and several of the external cultures.\n\nConnie Springer, who had always been somewhat awkward and clumsy, found that his genuine care for his fellow soldiers and his ability to see humor and humanity in difficult situations made him an excellent trainer of new soldiers. He became responsible for helping young soldiers adapt to the transition from wall-based to open-field military tactics.\n\n### The Moral Reckoning\n\nBut beneath all this activity and organization, there was a deeper moral reckoning happening.\n\nThe wall civilization had been founded on deception and control. For centuries, the population had been kept ignorant of the true nature of the world beyond the walls, of the true nature of the titans, of the presence of the embedded titans within the barriers themselves. The ruling class had maintained this deception deliberately, through careful control of information and through selective elevation of approved histories.\n\nNow, with the walls collapsed and the truth revealed, there was a process of accountability and reckoning that began.\n\nNobles who had been complicit in maintaining the deception were investigated and tried. Some were found guilty of crimes against humanity and were executed. Others were exiled. A few were pardoned, recognized as individuals who had been part of a system but who had not themselves personally perpetrated atrocities.\n\nThe organization of the military police, which had served the interests of the nobility and had committed various abuses in their names, was fundamentally restructured. Officers who had participated in particularly egregious acts were prosecuted. The organization itself was reformed into a civilian law enforcement body, subordinate to elected government officials rather than to shadowy nobility.\n\nBut there were also those who recognized that the previous system, however flawed and deceptive, had maintained a form of stability and peace within the walls. The walls themselves, despite being a form of confinement, had prevented the kinds of wars and conflicts that were rampant in the outside world.\n\nThe collapse of the walls had freed humanity from confinement, but it had also exposed them to dangers and complexities that they were unprepared to manage.\n\n### The Philosophical Divide\n\nThis led to the emergence of philosophical and political divisions within the wall civilization''s population.','\n',char(10)),'After the walls fall, former soldiers adapt to new roles in diplomacy, military leadership, and training, while the civilization undergoes a moral reckoning over its history of deception, leading to political and philosophical divisions.','[{"start": 96055, "end": 99961}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Jean Kirstein", "Sasha Blouse", "Connie Springer", "military police", "wall civilization", "diplomatic corps"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:49:28');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('5cefb084c86fa2fac39a7bd1b18c554fcb48660a0d45b105360b254dd542d2a5','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('d conflicts that were rampant in the outside world.\n\nThe collapse of the walls had freed humanity from confinement, but it had also exposed them to dangers and complexities that they were unprepared to manage.\n\n### The Philosophical Divide\n\nThis led to the emergence of philosophical and political divisions within the wall civilization''s population.\n\nOne faction believed that the opening of the walls and the encounter with the outside world was a positive development, that freedom and knowledge were worth the risks and dangers that came with exposure to the outside world.\n\nAnother faction believed that the system of walls had been fundamentally good, that the price of freedom was too high, and that efforts should be made to rebuild the barriers and attempt to restore the previous system of relative isolation and stability.\n\nA third faction, more radical, believed that the entire system of walls and the entire civilization that had been built within them was fundamentally corrupt and should be dismantled, with efforts made to build a new civilization based on completely different principles.\n\nThese factions competed for influence over the new government, each attempting to establish policies that would move the civilization in the direction they believed was correct.\n\nEren, as the Founding Titan and as a powerful voice in the new civilization, found himself caught between these competing visions. His personal conviction was that freedom was worth pursuing, that encountering the outside world and its complexities was preferable to remaining isolated and ignorant.\n\nBut he also recognized the validity of the concerns raised by those who feared the consequences of exposure to the outside world.\n\n"I don''t have all the answers," he said in a rare public address, acknowledging his uncertainty openly. "I made a choice to open the walls, but I recognize that this choice has consequences. Some of those consequences are positive—knowledge, freedom, new possibilities. Some of those consequences are negative—danger, suffering, conflict. We have to face both and make decisions about how to move forward."\n\n## Part Ten: The Deeper Mysteries\n\n### The Origins of the Titans\n\nWith the walls collapsed and the civilization facing the external world, questions arose that had never been fully answered: where did the titans come from originally? How had the power of the Founding Titan been created in the first place?\n\nHange led a research team into the underground chambers that had housed the secrets of the wall civilization''s founding. These chambers contained not just political documents but scientific ones—records of experimentation, records of research into the nature of the titans and the mechanism by which they functioned.\n\nWhat they discovered was that the titans were not a naturally occurring phenomenon. They were engineered biological entities, created through a process of modification and enhancement of human subjects.\n\nThe documents described a process where subjects were infected with a unique parasite-like organism that allowed them to transform into titan form. This organism—referred to in the documents as the "Titan Serum" or the "Titan Catalyst"—had been developed through generations of research and experimentation.\n\nMost disturbingly, the documents suggested that the original development of this serum had been conducted on unwilling subjects—prisoners, political enemies, conquered populations. The research had been brutal and unethical by any standard.\n\nThe Founding Titan, it appeared, was not born naturally but was created through the deliberate modification of a human subject using an extremely refined form of this serum. The first Founding Titan, according to the documents, had been a woman named Ymir Fritz, who had lived nearly two thousand years before the walls were built.','\n',char(10)),'After the walls collapsed, humanity faced new dangers and philosophical divisions over whether to embrace the outside world, rebuild isolation, or dismantle the existing civilization. Eren, as the Founding Titan, navigated these factions wh','[{"start": 99611, "end": 103450}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Founding Titan", "Hange", "Ymir Fritz", "Titan Serum", "Wall Civilization", "Outside World", "Philosophical Divide"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:49:34');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('f634ff54bfa25659012676371449a1144151437eb2c665ebf526ecea3e02d0c6','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace(' by any standard.\n\nThe Founding Titan, it appeared, was not born naturally but was created through the deliberate modification of a human subject using an extremely refined form of this serum. The first Founding Titan, according to the documents, had been a woman named Ymir Fritz, who had lived nearly two thousand years before the walls were built.\n\nYmir had been modified as a subject in an experimental program and had discovered or developed the ability to control other titans through her connection to them. Over her lifetime, she had used this power to build an empire, to conquer regions, to establish a civilization that stretched across multiple continents.\n\nWhen Ymir died, her body was consumed by her descendants, who sought to maintain the power of the Founding Titan within their family line. The documents described elaborate ceremonies and methods designed to ensure that the power was passed from generation to generation through consumption.\n\nThis revelation was deeply disturbing. The power that Eren wielded, the power that seemed almost divine in its scope and capability, was actually derived from the modification and enhancement of a human being through chemical or biological processes. It was a power that was born from brutality and experimentation.\n\n### The Weight of Inheritance\n\nWhen Eren learned of these origins—that the power he carried was born from the suffering and modification of an innocent woman nearly two thousand years ago—he was profoundly affected.\n\nHe found himself questioning whether he should even maintain this power, whether he should attempt to release it or destroy it or pass it on to someone else.\n\n"The power is not pure," he said to Hange during one of their research consultations. "It''s built on suffering. Every time I use it, I''m using a tool that was created through unthinkable cruelty."\n\n"Yes," Hange agreed, her expression serious. "But the power exists now. It''s not going to disappear because you wish it would. The question is: what will you do with it? How will you use a power born from cruelty?"\n\nThis philosophical question consumed Eren for months. He spent hours consulting with historians, philosophers, and ethicists, attempting to determine whether there was a moral path forward for someone bearing such a power.\n\nThe consensus that emerged was not a simple answer but a recognition of complexity. The power had been born from cruelty, but power itself was morally neutral. What mattered was how the power was used, what intentions drove its use, and whether those using it remained cognizant of the moral weight and responsibility that came with such capability.\n\nEren eventually resolved to maintain the power for the time being but to establish strict protocols for its use. He would not use the power to force specific outcomes on the population. He would not use it to establish a new form of tyranny. Instead, he would use it, carefully and reluctantly, only in situations where there was a genuine need to prevent catastrophic outcomes.\n\n### The Marley Crisis\n\nWhile Eren was grappling with these philosophical questions, external events were moving rapidly.\n\nMarley, facing the loss of its primary strategic objective (the conquest of the wall civilization) and the loss of several of its titan-warriors (Reiner, Bertolt, and Annie had either switched sides or been captured), was undergoing significant political upheaval.\n\nThe military leadership that had ordered the infiltration of the wall civilization was facing serious criticism. The government was fractured between those who wanted to continue aggressive expansion and those who recognized that the emergence of the Founding Titan fundamentally changed the strategic balance.\n\nAdditionally, Marley was facing pressure from other nations and empires that saw the opening of the wall civilization as an opportunity to expand their own influence and power. The geopolitical landscape was shifting rapidly.','\n',char(10)),'The text details the origin of the Founding Titan through the modification of a woman named Ymir Fritz, its inheritance through consumption by descendants, and the philosophical dilemma faced by its current bearer, Eren. It also touches on ','[{"start": 103100, "end": 107050}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Ymir Fritz", "Eren", "Founding Titan", "Marley", "Hange", "Reiner", "Bertolt", "Annie"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:49:40');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('32ffc1b784285994abedcaeff87fe6806690f1cf5a471818677550c7ef7f59f7','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('ve expansion and those who recognized that the emergence of the Founding Titan fundamentally changed the strategic balance.\n\nAdditionally, Marley was facing pressure from other nations and empires that saw the opening of the wall civilization as an opportunity to expand their own influence and power. The geopolitical landscape was shifting rapidly.\n\nA delegation from Marley came to negotiate formally with the wall civilization, seeking to establish terms for peace and coexistence. The head of this delegation was a military general named Magath, a man who had been involved in directing the operations against the wall civilization and who now had to confront the reality that those operations had failed.\n\n"We seek to establish borders of influence," Magath stated in the formal negotiation. "Marley will recognize the sovereignty of the wall civilization''s territories, and the wall civilization will recognize Marley''s control of its territories. Neither civilization will interfere in the other''s affairs."\n\nIt was a reasonable proposal, one that was designed to establish a stable international order. But there were complications.\n\nFirst, the precise borders of the "wall civilization''s territories" were unclear. The walls had covered a specific region, but the exact extent of legitimate territorial control was debatable.\n\nSecond, there were populations that existed outside the original walls but that had had historical or cultural connections to the wall civilization. Some of these populations wanted to be included in the new political structure of the wall civilization; others wanted to establish their own independent states.\n\nThird, and most critically, there was the question of what would happen to the Founding Titan. Marley wanted assurances that the Founding Titan would not be used as a weapon to expand the wall civilization''s territory or to challenge Marley''s regional dominance.\n\nEren''s position on this was clear: the Founding Titan would not be used for conquest or expansion. But he could not guarantee that the power would never be used militarily, as circumstances might require its use for defensive purposes.\n\nThis created a tentative agreement but not a true peace. Both Marley and the wall civilization maintained military readiness, both expecting that conflict might emerge despite the formal agreements.\n\n### The Internal Division\n\nBut even as the wall civilization was dealing with external challenges, it was facing serious internal divisions.\n\nThe revelation of the wall civilization''s true history—the revelation that the entire civilization had been founded on deception and control, that the walls had been maintained not just for protection but for confinement, that the ruling class had deliberately hidden information from the population—led to serious political instability.\n\nThere were riots in several of the interior cities. Nobles were attacked in the streets. The authority structures that had previously been accepted without question were suddenly being challenged and questioned.\n\nA new political movement emerged, advocating for radical democratic reforms. This movement, which called itself the "Free Peoples Alliance," demanded that the government be reformed to be fully representative and accountable to the population.\n\nAnother movement, more conservative, emerged advocating for the restoration of order and authority. This movement, called the "Stability Alliance," argued that the radical restructuring of society would lead to chaos and collapse.\n\nEren found himself being appealed to by both sides, each attempting to gain his support for their political agenda.\n\n"You have the power to determine the future of this civilization," leaders from the Free Peoples Alliance told him. "Use that power to ensure that true democracy is established."','\n',char(10)),'Marley sends a delegation led by General Magath to negotiate peace with the wall civilization, proposing recognized borders and non-interference. Key issues include unclear territorial boundaries, populations outside the walls with historic','[{"start": 106700, "end": 110516}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Marley", "Magath", "wall civilization", "Founding Titan", "Eren", "Free Peoples Alliance", "Stability Alliance", "geopolitical landscape"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:50:20');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('6bd62d4dbd81e18f49f04c4d587d8bd89bf302073e1b98f0b716e68f11425f9e','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('ucturing of society would lead to chaos and collapse.\n\nEren found himself being appealed to by both sides, each attempting to gain his support for their political agenda.\n\n"You have the power to determine the future of this civilization," leaders from the Free Peoples Alliance told him. "Use that power to ensure that true democracy is established."\n\n"You must prevent the radical elements from destroying the social structures that have kept this civilization functioning," leaders from the Stability Alliance urged. "Use the Founding Titan''s power to maintain order."\n\nEren refused both positions. He made clear that he would not use his power to determine the political structure of the civilization. "I will not be a tyrant, even a benevolent one," he stated. "The decisions about how this civilization should be governed should be made by the people, through their own deliberation and choice."\n\nThis position was unpopular with many who believed Eren should use his power to advance their particular cause. But it was a position that Eren was determined to maintain.\n\n### The Question of Succession\n\nAs Eren settled into his role as the Founding Titan, another question began to be raised: what would happen if Eren died? Would the power simply disappear? Would it transfer to someone else? Would it create a vacuum of power that various factions would fight to fill?\n\nThese were not idle questions. The power of the Founding Titan had been inherited by previous generations through a method of deliberate consumption. But Eren had not yet designated anyone to inherit the power after him.\n\nHange, always interested in understanding the mechanisms behind the power, conducted extensive research into how the inheritance of the Founding Titan worked.\n\nHer conclusion was unsettling: the power could only be passed on through deliberate action. If Eren simply died without passing the power to anyone, the Founding Titan power would eventually fade or transfer to whoever consumed a piece of Eren''s body.\n\nThis created a dangerous situation. It meant that other organizations, other nations, other factions would have strong incentives to attempt to kill Eren and consume his body, so as to gain the Founding Titan''s power.\n\nEren recognized this danger. He began to consider whether he should deliberately pass the power to someone else, someone who might be more equipped to handle it responsibly.\n\nSeveral candidates were suggested: Arwin, whose loyalty and wisdom seemed unquestionable; Mikasa, whose personal connection to Eren suggested she might be the best choice; Hange, whose scientific understanding of the power might allow for more rational use of it.\n\nBut Eren rejected all these suggestions. He believed that passing the power to someone else would simply transfer the burden to another person, without solving the fundamental problem: that possession of the Founding Titan''s power made it extremely difficult to make decisions based on genuine conviction rather than based on the scope and magnitude of power available.\n\nInstead, Eren proposed a radical solution: the power should be deliberately allowed to dissipate. He would use his control of the power to ensure that, upon his death, the power would not transfer to anyone else. It would simply end, released back into the world as diffuse, uncontrolled potential.\n\nThis proposal was met with shock and horror by many. The idea of deliberately destroying the most powerful force in the world seemed insane to those who understood the strategic implications.\n\nBut Eren was determined. "Humanity needs to learn to exist without relying on a single source of enormous power," he argued. "We need to develop systems and societies that don''t depend on the power of titans. The only way to force that development is to make the power unavailable."\n\n## Part Eleven: The Slow Transformation\n\n### Years of Negotiation and Building','\n',char(10)),'Eren Jaeger, as the Founding Titan, refuses to use his power to dictate political systems, insisting democratic choices be made by the people. Facing questions of succession, he learns the Founding Titan''s power could be lost or stolen if h','[{"start": 110166, "end": 114062}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Jaeger", "Founding Titan", "Free Peoples Alliance", "Stability Alliance", "Hange", "Armin", "Mikasa"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:50:25');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('66d3780ad22d4d8596cc4ffa1e63f42e3038185515c880e5493bc6607b4152c4','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace(' determined. "Humanity needs to learn to exist without relying on a single source of enormous power," he argued. "We need to develop systems and societies that don''t depend on the power of titans. The only way to force that development is to make the power unavailable."\n\n## Part Eleven: The Slow Transformation\n\n### Years of Negotiation and Building\n\nThe years following the collapse of the walls were years of intensive negotiation, diplomatic work, and gradual social transformation.\n\nThe wall civilization, now formally renamed as the "Free Territories" or "The Restored Lands" (depending on which faction''s preferred designation one used), began to establish formal relationships with neighboring powers and civilizations.\n\nTrade routes were established. Cultural exchanges began. Scholars from the Free Territories met with scholars from Marley and other nations, sharing knowledge and perspectives.\n\nBut there were also tensions and conflicts. Border skirmishes occurred as local populations disputed territorial boundaries. Trade disputes emerged over access to valuable resources. Political factions within the Free Territories continued to debate the proper governance structure for the civilization.\n\nEren, maintaining his role as the Founding Titan, became involved in the most critical diplomatic negotiations and decisions. He served as a symbol of the Free Territories'' power and stability, but also as a moderating force, attempting to guide the civilization toward peaceful resolution of conflicts rather than violent confrontation.\n\nMikasa remained close to him throughout these years, supporting him emotionally even as he carried the burden of the Founding Titan''s power. She became known for her diplomatic abilities, using her understanding of both the military and civilian perspectives to help bridge gaps between different factions.\n\nArwin took on administrative roles within the government, working to establish the structures and protocols that would allow for more democratic decision-making. He established public forums where citizens could voice their concerns and opinions. He worked to ensure transparency in government operations. He pushed constantly for greater accountability from officials and military leaders.\n\nHange continued her scientific research, but now with access to a far broader range of materials and knowledge. She established research institutions that attracted scholars from across the known world. She investigated the mechanism of the Founding Titan power, attempting to understand its deepest mechanisms and limitations.\n\nJean and Sasha and Connie, having become increasingly senior military officers, worked to establish training programs and military structures that reflected the new reality of open-world conflict. They established protocols for collaboration with military forces from other civilizations, worked to develop tactics that would be effective against new kinds of threats, and generally positioned the Free Territories'' military as a professional and capable force.\n\n### The Marley Transition\n\nMarley, in the decades following the emergence of the Founding Titan, underwent its own transformation.\n\nThe aggressive military policy that had led to the infiltration of the wall civilization was abandoned. The government underwent a gradual shift toward more peaceful foreign policy objectives.\n\nBut this transition was not smooth or painless. There were military officers within Marley who believed that the correct response to the Founding Titan''s emergence was to prepare for eventual war, to build up military capabilities in preparation for conflict that they believed was inevitable.\n\nBertolt Hoover, who had been acting as an envoy for peaceful negotiation, was assassinated by extremists within Marley who disagreed with the peaceful policy direction. His death sent shockwaves through both the Free Territories and Marley, and it nearly derailed the peace process entirely.','\n',char(10)),'Following the collapse of the walls, the Free Territories engages in negotiation and transformation while Eren, Mikasa, Armin, Hange, Jean, Sasha, and Connie assume leadership roles. Marley undergoes a parallel transition toward peace, whic','[{"start": 113712, "end": 117667}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Mikasa", "Armin", "Hange", "Jean", "Sasha", "Connie", "Bertolt Hoover"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:50:32');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('aa4d3c4cdfb6ad854a25125c3178bdc42a867fc7e70b6a3d1a7bd95944922192','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('eparation for conflict that they believed was inevitable.\n\nBertolt Hoover, who had been acting as an envoy for peaceful negotiation, was assassinated by extremists within Marley who disagreed with the peaceful policy direction. His death sent shockwaves through both the Free Territories and Marley, and it nearly derailed the peace process entirely.\n\nBut Reiner Braun, who had become increasingly prominent in advocating for peace and reconciliation, used his position to push back against the extremists. As an Armored Titan warrior who had chosen to side with the Free Territories, he had credibility on both sides of the conflict.\n\n"Bertolt believed in peace," Reiner said at the memorial service held in both the Free Territories and Marley. "He believed that we could overcome the divisions that had separated our peoples. I intend to honor that belief by continuing to work toward the peace that he died trying to establish."\n\nHis words helped to stabilize the situation and to keep the diplomatic process moving forward.\n\nAnnie Leonhart, who had eventually been released from her imprisonment and allowed to live in the Free Territories under conditions of parole, became an unexpected voice for reconciliation. She had spent years imprisoned, had faced interrogation and confinement, but she had come to understand the perspectives of the people she had been fighting against. She began to work with diplomatic organizations, attempting to help both sides understand the humanity of their former enemies.\n\n### The Question of the Power\n\nAs decades passed and Eren continued to maintain the Founding Titan''s power, questions began to arise about whether Eren was still making rational decisions about the use of that power or whether the power itself was beginning to shape his judgment.\n\nHange, who continued to study the Founding Titan''s mechanism, began to notice subtle changes in Eren''s behavior and perspective.\n\n"The power does something to the user," she explained to Arwin in a private conversation. "It''s not just that the power enables certain actions; the power itself influences the way the user thinks. I can see it happening to Eren, very subtly, over time."\n\nArwin was concerned by this observation. "What kind of influence?"\n\n"The user of the Founding Titan begins to see existence through the lens of that power," Hange explained. "They become less able to accept limitations or obstacles. They begin to conceive of solutions to problems in terms of the power available to them. It''s not conscious corruption, but it''s a fundamental shift in perspective."\n\nThis observation led to discussions about whether Eren''s commitment to eventually release the power was something he would actually be able to follow through on, or whether the power itself would prevent him from releasing it when the time came.\n\nEren, when confronted with these concerns, acknowledged the validity of them. "I do feel the power influencing my thinking," he admitted. "I catch myself sometimes thinking about solutions to problems in terms of the power available to me. But I maintain the resolution to release it. That''s why I need people around me who will hold me accountable, who will remind me of my commitment if I begin to waver."\n\nThis led to the establishment of a formal "Council of Accountability," a group of trusted advisors who met regularly with Eren to discuss his use of power and to provide perspective on whether his decisions were aligned with his stated principles.\n\nThe council included Arwin, Mikasa, Hange, Jean, and several other trusted individuals. Their role was to question Eren''s decisions, to point out inconsistencies, to remind him of his commitments.\n\nIt was a delicate balance—maintaining enough independence to genuinely hold Eren accountable while avoiding appearing to oppose or undermine him in ways that could destabilize the civilization.\n\n### The Slow Generations','\n',char(10)),'Following Bertolt Hoover''s assassination, Reiner Braun and Annie Leonhart emerged as voices for peace. Decades later, concerns arose about the Founding Titan''s influence on Eren''s judgment, leading to the formation of a Council of Accountab','[{"start": 117317, "end": 121222}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Bertolt Hoover", "Reiner Braun", "Annie Leonhart", "Eren", "Hange", "Arwin", "Founding Titan", "Council of Accountability"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:50:36');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('5a8c078d16972441379c30ac49512860517fb105d6de068d506fced0bcf41e88','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('trusted individuals. Their role was to question Eren''s decisions, to point out inconsistencies, to remind him of his commitments.\n\nIt was a delicate balance—maintaining enough independence to genuinely hold Eren accountable while avoiding appearing to oppose or undermine him in ways that could destabilize the civilization.\n\n### The Slow Generations\n\nAs decades turned into a century, the generations that had experienced the walls directly began to age and eventually pass away. New generations were born into a world without walls, without the immediate experience of confinement and protection.\n\nThese new generations had a different relationship to Eren and to the Founding Titan power. To them, Eren was not a liberator or a revolutionary figure but simply a fact of existence—a constant, unchanging presence that had always been part of the world they lived in.\n\nSome of the younger generation even began to question whether they needed the Founding Titan at all. They pointed out that many regions of the world had developed stable societies, had established functional governance structures, had established peaceful relationships with their neighbors, all without the presence of a Founding Titan.\n\nThis questioning was healthy, Eren believed. It meant that the civilization was developing the capacity to imagine a world without the power. It meant that the conditions for eventually releasing the power were becoming viable.\n\nBut there was also resistance from others who believed that the Founding Titan was essential to maintaining order and preventing conflict between civilizations.\n\nThe political landscape became increasingly complex, with multiple viewpoints about what should happen to the Founding Titan''s power and how the civilization should govern itself in the absence of that power.\n\nEren found himself, paradoxically, in the position of having to use his power to ensure that his power was eventually released. He had to use the Founding Titan''s authority to prevent other factions from using the power themselves, had to use his position to ensure that the transition away from the power could actually happen.\n\n### The Personal Cost\n\nThroughout all of this, Eren carried a personal burden that few people outside his closest circle truly understood.\n\nThe connection to the Founding Titan''s power meant that Eren was connected to the experiences and memories of every previous Founding Titan. As he accessed these memories and learned from them, he began to understand the full scope of the suffering that had been caused by the power over the millennia it had existed.\n\nHe saw civilizations conquered and destroyed. He saw people enslaved and manipulated. He saw wars fought over possession of the power. He saw women and men struggling with the burden of carrying this power, many of them driven to madness or despair by it.\n\nAnd he carried the guilt and the weight of all of these historical harms. It was a psychological burden that grew heavier with each passing year, each memory that he accessed and internalized.\n\nMikasa, who remained his closest confidant, helped him carry this burden as best she could. She would sit with him during his darker moments, listening to him describe the weight of these memories, helping him to maintain his connection to his own humanity and his own identity despite the overwhelming scope of the historical trauma he carried.\n\n"You''re not responsible for what the previous Founding Titans did," she would tell him. "You''re only responsible for what you do."\n\n"But I''m using their power," Eren would reply. "I''m continuing their legacy, even as I try to end it."\n\n"Yes," Mikasa would acknowledge. "That''s the paradox you''re caught in. But you''re making different choices than they did. That has to count for something."\n\n### The Scientific Understanding\n\nMeanwhile, Hange was continuing to uncover new information about the nature of the Founding Titan power and the titans themselves.','\n',char(10)),'The text describes a post-liberation society where Eren, wielding the Founding Titan power, faces political complexity and personal burden as new generations question the need for his power, while scientific inquiry by Hange continues.','[{"start": 120872, "end": 124826}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Founding Titan", "Mikasa", "Hange"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:50:40');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('0fb28b1150977a5170d340ecbe4cfb5a4251b8b3694fbba2528bea9b532afa86','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace(', even as I try to end it."\n\n"Yes," Mikasa would acknowledge. "That''s the paradox you''re caught in. But you''re making different choices than they did. That has to count for something."\n\n### The Scientific Understanding\n\nMeanwhile, Hange was continuing to uncover new information about the nature of the Founding Titan power and the titans themselves.\n\nHer research led to a stunning discovery: the titans were not a separate species that had been engineered from natural organisms. Instead, they were human beings who had been transformed through a biological process.\n\nMore specifically, the process of transformation was not random or inevitable. It was a deliberate choice or a deliberate action. The serum that could transform humans into titans was not something that people were simply infected with; it was something that had to be administered consciously, either by the person themselves or by someone else.\n\nThis meant that the entire system of titans as a natural or inevitable threat was fundamentally misconceived. There were no truly "feral" titans—all titans had originally been human and had been transformed deliberately at some point in their history.\n\nWhen Eren learned of this discovery, it crystallized his commitment to ending the Founding Titan power. If all titans were originally human, then the perpetuation of the power meant the perpetuation of the system that required turning humans into titans.\n\n"We have to document this," Eren insisted to Hange. "We have to make sure that future generations understand that titans are not a natural phenomenon. They''re a choice. And if the choice is no longer made, if the power is no longer used, then titans will eventually cease to exist."\n\nThis revelation also had implications for how the remaining titans in the world were treated. If they were originally human, then the moral framework for dealing with them needed to fundamentally change. Killing a titan was not like killing an animal; it was more like killing a human being who had been transformed against their will or who was trapped in a form they had been forced into.\n\nThis led to new protocols for engaging with feral titans, new attempts to help them return to human form if possible, new efforts to understand their consciousness and psychology.\n\nIt was slow, difficult work, but it represented a move toward a more humane and ethical approach to the titan problem.\n\n## Epilogue: The End of Walls\n\n### The Final Decision\n\nOn the eve of what would be his three-hundredth year of consciousness (though his body had aged to approximately thirty-five years old due to the way the Founding Titan power slowed physical aging), Eren made a final decision.\n\nHe gathered his Council of Accountability and his closest advisors. Among them were Arwin, now ancient but still mentally sharp; Mikasa, whose devotion to Eren had never wavered; Hange, whose understanding of the power had become unparalleled; and several representatives from the governments of the civilizations that now occupied the former wall region and the areas beyond.\n\n"I''m ready to release the power," Eren stated simply.\n\nThere was silence in the room for a long moment. This was a decision that had been theoretically possible for centuries, but no one had truly expected Eren to make it.\n\n"What will happen?" one of the government representatives asked.\n\n"I don''t know exactly," Eren admitted. "Hange has theorized that the power will dissipate, becoming diffuse and uncontrolled. It may cease to exist entirely, or it may distribute itself among the population in ways we can''t predict. The titans that remain in the world will likely revert to human form, or they will cease to function."\n\n"And you?" Arwin asked. "What happens to you?"\n\n"I become human again," Eren said. "Not powerless, but no longer connected to the historical weight of the Founding Titan consciousness. I become myself, just myself, for the first time in centuries."','\n',char(10)),'Hange discovers that titans are transformed humans, not a separate species, leading to new ethical protocols. After centuries of consciousness, Eren decides to release the Founding Titan power, hoping to end the titan cycle and become human','[{"start": 124476, "end": 128416}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Hange", "Mikasa", "Founding Titan", "titans", "Council of Accountability"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:51:21');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('4e3cd3298c262bd1ccffca7838cdd81a10b850ad1b0fcd0d44a4dd6035cf120c','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace('e titans that remain in the world will likely revert to human form, or they will cease to function."\n\n"And you?" Arwin asked. "What happens to you?"\n\n"I become human again," Eren said. "Not powerless, but no longer connected to the historical weight of the Founding Titan consciousness. I become myself, just myself, for the first time in centuries."\n\nThe decision triggered a massive mobilization. Organizations around the world prepared for the transition. Records were made of all the knowledge that Eren possessed as the Founding Titan, ensuring that this knowledge would not be lost. Plans were made for how to manage the practical consequences of the power''s release.\n\nThe ceremony itself was simple, almost anticlimactic. Eren stood in a public plaza, with thousands of people watching—some through their presence, some through communication devices that had been developed over the centuries.\n\nAnd he let go.\n\n### The Release\n\nAs Eren released his conscious grip on the Founding Titan power, something extraordinary happened.\n\nAcross the world, every titan suddenly felt the connection that had bound them to the Founding Titan''s authority dissolve. For titans who had been held in that form for centuries, the experience of freedom or of release was overwhelming.\n\nMost of the feral titans, suddenly unbound from the power that had held them in that form, reverted to human beings—confused, disoriented, traumatized, but human.\n\nSome titans, particularly those who had existed in titan form for so long that their human consciousness had been completely subsumed, did not survive the reversion. Their bodies simply ceased to function, as if the power that had been animating them was the only thing that had kept them alive.\n\nAnd the specialized titans—the Armored Titan (Reiner), the Female Titan (Annie)—experienced a strange sensation of liberation. For years, they had been tied to their forms, subject to the power of the Founding Titan even as they operated as independent agents. Now, they were released from that connection. They were free.\n\nEren, in the moment of releasing the power, experienced something like transcendence. All the memories of the previous Founding Titans, all the accumulated historical consciousness, flowed out of him like water from a breaking dam. In releasing the power, he also released the burden of that historical weight.\n\nAnd he collapsed, unconscious, as his body began to revert to a purely human state.\n\n### The Aftermath\n\nWhen Eren regained consciousness three days later, he was in a medical facility. Hange was waiting beside him, monitoring his condition with intense focus.\n\n"Welcome back," Hange said, noticing that his eyes had opened.\n\n"Did it work?" Eren asked, his voice weak.\n\n"It worked," Hange confirmed. "The power is gone. Dispersed. Some small remnants of it may persist in places we haven''t discovered yet, but the Founding Titan is no more."\n\nEren closed his eyes, experiencing a sense of relief and, simultaneously, a sense of loss. He was no longer connected to the vast consciousness that had surrounded and sustained him for so long. He was just Eren Yeager, a human being with a mortal lifespan and limited power.\n\nBut he was free in a way that he had never been before.\n\nMikasa, waiting outside the medical room, was allowed to see him. She entered quietly and sat beside his bed.\n\n"Thank you," she said simply, not specifying for what.\n\n"For what?" Eren asked.\n\n"For coming back," she replied. "For becoming human again."\n\nOver the following days and weeks, stories emerged from around the world about the changes that had occurred when the Founding Titan power was released.\n\nIn some regions, entire populations of feral titans reverted to human form, and communities worked to help these individuals reintegrate into society and understand what had happened to them.\n\nIn other regions, titans simply ceased to exist, their forms dissolving into nothing.','\n',char(10)),'Eren Yeager releases the Founding Titan power in a public ceremony, causing titans worldwide to revert to human form or cease functioning, while he himself becomes fully human again. The aftermath involves societal adjustments and personal ','[{"start": 128066, "end": 131998}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Yeager", "Founding Titan", "Hange", "Mikasa", "Armored Titan (Reiner)", "Female Titan (Annie)"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:51:26');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('980817f4aebe1e96b26d576b6cb68dbf91c7c2b4655d09b2fd57cc6788a1b78e','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace(' changes that had occurred when the Founding Titan power was released.\n\nIn some regions, entire populations of feral titans reverted to human form, and communities worked to help these individuals reintegrate into society and understand what had happened to them.\n\nIn other regions, titans simply ceased to exist, their forms dissolving into nothing.\n\nThe Armored Titan—Reiner Braun—for the first time in his life, was fully and completely human, no longer bound by the power or the responsibility of bearing it. He wept when he understood what had happened.\n\nAnnie Leonhart experienced a similar liberation. For the first time since her childhood, she was not carrying the secret of her titan form or the burden of her dual nature. She was simply herself.\n\nThe world, for the first time in recorded history, was a world without titans.\n\n### The New Beginning\n\nIn the years following the release of the Founding Titan power, the civilizations that occupied the world began a process of genuine reconstruction and reconciliation.\n\nWith the titans gone, the framework of conflict that had defined human civilization for so long was fundamentally altered. The fear of titan attack, the competition for resources related to titan containment, the political power struggles centered around the control of titan abilities—all of these disappeared.\n\nIt didn''t mean that all conflict disappeared. Humans still struggled over resources, ideology, territory, and power. But it was conflict between equals, rather than conflict shaped by the presence of overwhelming biological weapons.\n\nEren lived a quiet life after his release. He worked with Arwin and others on establishing historical records of what had transpired during the period of the Founding Titan''s control. He worked with Hange on scientific education, ensuring that future generations would understand the true nature of what they had inherited.\n\nHe spent time with Mikasa, enjoying the simple pleasure of being together without the weight of extraordinary responsibility.\n\nHe reconnected with Jean and Sasha and Connie, who had become prominent figures in the government of the Free Territories. They had guided the region through decades of political and social transformation, had established systems of governance that respected individual liberty while maintaining collective security.\n\nThe world that emerged from the aftermath of the walls'' collapse and the Founding Titan''s release was not a utopia. It had problems and challenges and conflicts. But it was a world where humans were the primary architects of their own fate, where decisions were being made based on what people actually wanted rather than based on the dictates of a power that could not be questioned or resisted.\n\nAnd perhaps that was the greatest victory that could have been achieved.\n\n### The Cycle Ends\n\nEren lived for another sixty years after releasing the Founding Titan power. He saw the generations that had been born after the walls collapsed reach adulthood and begin to shape the world according to their own vision. He watched as historical scholars documented and analyzed the period of the walls, developing understanding of what had transpired and why.\n\nHe watched as his relationship with Mikasa deepened and transformed. She remained his closest companion until the end of her life, supporting him through the transition to ordinary human existence and then carrying his memory forward as a historical figure.\n\nWhen Eren eventually died, he had accomplished what he had intended: he had broken the cycle of the Founding Titan power. He had freed the world from the burden of titans. And he had returned to being simply human, experiencing the ordinary joys and sorrows of human existence.','\n',char(10)),'After Eren Yeager releases the Founding Titan power, the world is freed from titans. Former titan shifters like Reiner Braun and Annie Leonhart are fully human again, and populations of feral titans revert to human form or dissolve. A new e','[{"start": 131648, "end": 135385}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren Yeager", "Founding Titan", "Reiner Braun", "Annie Leonhart", "Mikasa", "Arwin", "Hange", "Free Territories"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:51:34');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('316af9f01cdc7f2186a29eb05dd90a896f27ab5ddca05189872e5295a9c0cd72','342b2502-4ef5-42b8-86b0-80e0935e441b',replace(' existence and then carrying his memory forward as a historical figure.\n\nWhen Eren eventually died, he had accomplished what he had intended: he had broken the cycle of the Founding Titan power. He had freed the world from the burden of titans. And he had returned to being simply human, experiencing the ordinary joys and sorrows of human existence.\n\nHis death was mourned across the world, not as the death of a god or a superpower but as the death of an important historical figure who had made crucial choices at critical moments. His life had not been perfect; his choices had not always been right. But he had tried to do the right thing, and that effort was recognized and honored.\n\nThe walls that had once defined humanity''s existence remained in ruins, serving as monuments to the era that had passed. New cities were built in their shadows, cities that had walls for protection but that were not sealed off from the rest of the world.\n\nAnd humanity, finally, was free to simply be human.\n\n---\n\n**End of Narrative**\n\nThis comprehensive narrative has followed Attack on Titan''s story chronologically without summaries, incorporating complex plot developments, character arcs, political intrigue, and philosophical questions that emerge across the entire series and extend into post-series scenarios. The narrative is designed to test reasoning by tracking multiple character perspectives, interconnected plot threads, and the evolution of conflicts and motivations across an extended timeline.\n','\n',char(10)),'The narrative describes the death and historical legacy of Eren, who broke the Founding Titan''s cycle and freed the world from titans, leading to humanity''s liberation and the transformation of the walls into historical monuments.','[{"start": 135035, "end": 136537}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Eren", "Founding Titan", "titans", "humanity", "walls"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:51:37');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('1f5e2ba40e6565122192c3e3791aaf837bd04e4d91e71a0a73dcb7852fa8129a','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('# Cyberpunk: Edgerunners - A Progressive Narrative Exploration\n\n## Night City''s Underground: Where Everything Begins\n\nThe rain hasn''t stopped falling in Night City for what feels like forever. Not the kind of rain that cleanses—the kind that just makes everything heavier, more oppressive. David Martinez stands at the edge of a rooftop in Heywood, his feet barely registering the edge, and he''s thinking about escape. Not the literal kind—though that''s always an option in a city where you can jack into cyberware and leave your body behind for a few hours. He''s thinking about the escape that comes when you stop pretending to be someone you''re not.\n\nHis mother, Gloria, is downstairs in their apartment. She''s been working double shifts at the clinic, bleeding herself dry for medical bills and the promise that David will make it out of this neighborhood, that he''ll have a future in a world that''s already decided his fate the moment he was born in the Heywood slums. The megacorporations don''t care about kids like David. They care about profit margins and market share and the quarterly earnings reports that determine whether shareholders can afford another vacation to Luna. David knows this because he''s seen the news feeds, the corporate propaganda wrapped up in glossy 4K resolution, telling him that he''s free to pursue his dreams as long as those dreams cost money he doesn''t have.\n\nThe thing about Night City is that it promises everything and delivers nothing. It''s a city built on contradictions—towering arcologies that house thousands while homeless people sleep in the streets below, neural implants that promise to enhance human capability while slowly turning their users into something less than human, and a constant stream of illegal modifications and black-market deals that suggest everyone''s looking for an edge, a way to be better than they are, faster, stronger, more connected. The city is drowning in chrome and blood, and everyone''s just trying to stay above the waterline.\n\nDavid''s got his mother''s chin and his father''s stubbornness—a combination that''s going to get him killed someday, probably sooner rather than later. He''s seventeen, which in Night City might as well be ancient depending on how you count it. Some people die before they turn twenty. Some people plug themselves so full of cyberware that they lose themselves piece by piece, their humanity eroding with every neural implant, every sensory enhancement, every combat upgrade that promises to make them a better killer. David doesn''t want to end up like that, but then again, he doesn''t want to end up like his father either—just another name in the database of the disappeared, another person who tried to run and couldn''t make it far enough.\n\nThe rain intensifies, and David''s mind drifts to school, to the academy where they''re training him to be a corporate wage slave, to sit in a cubicle somewhere and pretend that his life means something. The education system in Night City is another joke, another way that the corporations keep the poor people poor and the rich people rich. They teach you just enough to be useful, but not enough to be dangerous, not enough to start asking questions about why the gap between the top floors and the streets keeps getting wider every year.\n\n## The Weight of Small Moments\n\nMrs. Chen''s noodle shop on the corner of Fifth and Main is where David goes when he needs to think. It''s run by an older woman who doesn''t ask questions and doesn''t charge full price for kids who look like they haven''t eaten in two days. The smell of broth and spices is a reprieve from the constant assault of sensory information that makes up Night City—the advertisements screaming at you from every available surface, the ambient noise of flying vehicles and street-level traffic, the synthetic music pumping out of every storefront and nightclub. In Mrs. Chen''s shop, there''s just soup and silence and the faint hum of a refrigerator that''s probably older than David is.','\n',char(10)),'The text introduces David Martinez, a 17-year-old living in Night City''s impoverished Heywood slums, who feels trapped by the oppressive, corporate-dominated society and dreams of escape. It describes the bleak urban environment and contras','[{"start": 0, "end": 3995}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David Martinez", "Night City", "Heywood", "Gloria Martinez", "Mrs. Chen''s noodle shop"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:52:25');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('ac0e576dd27e362986a2901034a902e94be8235a00db2518cea23e8124da04cb','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('ation that makes up Night City—the advertisements screaming at you from every available surface, the ambient noise of flying vehicles and street-level traffic, the synthetic music pumping out of every storefront and nightclub. In Mrs. Chen''s shop, there''s just soup and silence and the faint hum of a refrigerator that''s probably older than David is.\n\nDavid sits in the corner booth and thinks about his mother''s hands. They''re always cold when she comes home from the clinic, even in the summer when the city''s ambient heat is enough to make your clothes stick to your skin. She works with people who can''t afford proper medical care, people who show up with problems that shouldn''t exist in a city as advanced as Night City, problems that only exist because there''s a two-tier system and most people are on the wrong tier. She''s saving money for his education, for his future, and David knows that''s a burden he''s carrying on his shoulders even if she never says it out loud.\n\nThe academy accepts his application on a conditional scholarship. The conditions are simple: maintain a 3.5 GPA, don''t get arrested, and show promise in specialized corporate training tracks. David reads the email three times, looking for the catch, the hidden clause that will explain why the Arasaka Corporation—one of the biggest megacorps in the world, a company that makes money from weapons, implants, and information—is suddenly interested in a kid from Heywood. There''s always a catch with corporations. They don''t invest in human capital unless they see a return on that investment, unless they think they can mold you into something useful to their bottom line.\n\nHis mother cries when he tells her, but it''s the good kind of crying, the kind that comes with relief. She holds him like he''s still a child, even though he''s already taller than she is, and she whispers things about how he''s going to make it, how he''s going to escape this place and build a real life. David wants to believe her. He really does. But there''s a seed of doubt planted deep in his chest, and it grows a little bigger every day.\n\n## The Neighborhood and Its Shadows\n\nHeywood isn''t the worst part of Night City—that would be the Badlands or the bottom levels of the sprawl where gangs control everything and corporate law doesn''t penetrate. Heywood is middle-tier slum, the kind of place where you see streetwalkers and dealers on every corner, where the police response time is measured in hours instead of minutes, where most of the people are just trying to survive to see another day without getting shot or addicted or both. It''s the kind of neighborhood where everyone knows everyone else''s business, where your survival depends on community, even if that community is fractured and held together with nothing but desperation and habit.\n\nThere are gang tags on every wall, territorial markers in spray paint and chalk and sometimes blood. The Moxes run the sex workers in this part of the city, protecting them from corporate exploitation in exchange for a cut of their earnings—a deal that''s terrible by every measure but somehow still better than the alternative. The Tygers Claws have territory a few blocks over, and they''re always looking for young people to recruit, to turn into street soldiers in their eternal war against the other gangs for control of the drug trade and the protection rackets that come with it. Most kids David''s age have already made their choice about which gang to join, or they''ve decided to stay independent and live with the constant threat that comes with that decision.','\n',char(10)),'David receives a conditional scholarship from the Arasaka Corporation for an academy, which makes his mother hopeful about his future, though he feels burdened by expectations. The passage also describes the gritty neighborhood of Heywood i','[{"start": 3645, "end": 7220}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Arasaka Corporation", "Night City", "Heywood", "Mrs. Chen", "Moxes", "Tyger Claws"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:52:32');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('f630a3511b4d0b95b882bf5c6bf726b67b0d3f1e7e59578752d2fc5351b4a17c','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('eople to recruit, to turn into street soldiers in their eternal war against the other gangs for control of the drug trade and the protection rackets that come with it. Most kids David''s age have already made their choice about which gang to join, or they''ve decided to stay independent and live with the constant threat that comes with that decision.\n\nDavid''s made a different choice, or maybe it was made for him by his mother''s insistence that he go to school, that he stay out of the gang life, that he not end up like some of the other kids he grew up with who are already marked or dead or worse. He walks through Heywood with his head down and his hands in his pockets, trying to be invisible, which is just as dangerous as being noticed because some people see silence as an invitation.\n\nThe apartment he lives in with his mother is small—three rooms that were probably considered luxury once, maybe thirty years ago, before the city expanded upward and left the middle levels to decay. The walls are thin enough that you can hear your neighbors arguing, having sex, shooting up, or whatever else they do to pass the time. The water pressure is inconsistent, the heating doesn''t work half the time, and there''s a persistent mold problem in the bathroom that keeps coming back no matter how much bleach his mother uses. This is what poverty looks like in Night City—not the dramatic suffering of the really desperate, but the grinding, mundane misery of people who work full-time jobs and still can''t afford anything better.\n\nGloria works as a trauma nurse at Kabuki Street Medical, which is about as close to the meat wagon as you can get without actually working for the corporate salvage teams. Trauma nurses deal with everything from gang violence to cybernetic implant rejection to corpo assassinations gone wrong. She comes home with stories she shouldn''t tell, experiences that she can''t unsee, and a exhaustion that sleep never quite seems to cure. She''s good at her job—excellent, actually—which means the clinic relies on her, which means they work her harder and pay her less than she''s worth because they know she''ll take the abuse to make sure her son has a future.\n\nDavid doesn''t like to think about where his father is, or what happened to him. Gloria doesn''t talk about it, and the few times he''s tried to ask, she''s shut the conversation down with the kind of finality that makes it clear she''s not going to discuss it. All he knows is that his father had dreams too, that he wanted more than what Heywood had to offer, and that whatever he did to try to escape, it didn''t work out the way he wanted. Maybe he''s dead. Maybe he''s in prison somewhere. Maybe he''s plugged into a host somewhere doing corporate espionage for a megacorp that owns him completely. In Night City, there are a lot of ways to disappear.\n\n## The Academy and Its Promises\n\nThe Arasaka Academy is located in the corpo part of town, in a gleaming tower that touches clouds and costs more to maintain in a day than most people earn in a year. Walking through the doors is like stepping into another world—one where people have implants that work perfectly, where the technology is cutting-edge and doesn''t break down every six months, where the air is clean and the buildings don''t have that distinct smell of decay and human waste. The security is intense, retinal scanners and neural IDs and guards with military-grade cyberware standing at every checkpoint. Arasaka doesn''t take chances with their facilities.','\n',char(10)),'The text describes the harsh living conditions in Night City''s Heywood district, focusing on David and his mother Gloria, a trauma nurse struggling to provide a better life for him. David tries to avoid gang life while navigating poverty an','[{"start": 6870, "end": 10374}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Gloria", "Night City", "Heywood", "Arasaka Academy", "Gang Violence"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:52:38');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('61ea54c0f7ba1d286620d187b4e6e206a3124ab438fcdbe817a4cb59dc25ac63','651dd8f7-d229-46b0-85f1-dff3e90de9d7',replace('# The Crimson Visitor: Condensed RAG Test Version\n\n## Part One: The Sleeping Structure\n\nThe year was 2087, and humanity had mostly stopped believing in magic.\n\nDr. Sarah Chen worked on the ninety-third floor of the Helix Research Complex in Seattle, where her seismic arrays had spent three weeks reporting something impossible. Beneath the Pacific Northwest, 8.3 kilometers below the surface and roughly 120 kilometers northwest of downtown, a massive structure was waking up. It did not behave like tectonic activity. It moved with direction, purpose, and a pattern that looked almost intelligent.\n\nARIA, Sarah''s distributed AI assistant, had already checked the instruments dozens of times. The answer never changed. The structure radiated across the electromagnetic spectrum, from extremely low frequencies to hard gamma radiation, while phasing in and out of conventional spacetime. It was not a building. It was not a machine. It was something older than the categories humans used to describe reality.\n\nWhen ARIA compared the data with historical records, the anomaly became worse. Indigenous Salish oral traditions described cycles of "burning beneath" and "waking and sleeping" that repeated every three to four centuries. Anthropologists had treated the stories as folklore, but ARIA suspected they were preserved observations of real events. Sarah realized that her decade of work on non-Euclidean physics and dimensional thinning had been circling the same truth: something beneath Seattle existed in more than one state of reality.\n\nARIA estimated that the structure would fully phase into normal spacetime within seventy-two hours. Sarah contacted a classified Department of Defense channel, using authorization Helix-Seven-Niner, and reported an imminent anomalous event.\n\n## Part Two: Sentinel\n\nAcross the city, Marcus Webb lived in a concrete apartment that looked less designed than endured. He was thirty-four, a former engineer, and the vigilante known as Sentinel. For five years, he had used an exoskeleton armor system to attack the criminal networks that ordinary institutions failed to stop.\n\nHis crusade had begun after his sister Jennifer was kidnapped by the Cascade Cartel. Jurisdictional delays, political paralysis, and failed ransom negotiations ended with her death. Marcus concluded that waiting for the system to work was often the same as accepting that it would fail.\n\nOracle, the tactical AI integrated into his armor, warned him that his sleep deprivation was reducing his effectiveness. Marcus ignored the warning until Oracle intercepted Sarah''s classified military communication. The decoded report described an ancient structure below Seattle, a dimensional manifestation window of forty-eight to seventy-two hours, and elements unknown to the periodic table.\n\nMarcus had uncovered secret laboratories, hidden government programs, and cartel infrastructure before. This was different. He ordered Oracle to monitor the Helix Complex and military response traffic. If the world was becoming stranger than even he believed, he wanted to see the shape of that strangeness before officials buried it.\n\n## Part Three: The Fleeing Stars\n\nHigh above Earth, the Keth''arai fleet emerged from deep space.\n\nTheir ships were not built in the human sense. They were grown from matter that existed partly in standard spacetime and partly in dimensions humans had only begun to imagine. The fleet carried the last forty thousand members of a civilization that had once numbered in the billions. They had been hunted almost to extinction by Malachor, a force their ancestors had accidentally helped awaken.\n\nCrimson, one of the oldest surviving Keth''arai, stood aboard the flagship and watched Earth turn below him. His scales were deep red streaked with metallic gold, and his folded wings resembled cathedrals of living crystal. To his people, Earth was not merely a young planet. It was one of the worlds where Malachor had been imprisoned thousands of years earlier.','\n',char(10)),'In 2087 Seattle, Dr. Sarah Chen detects an impossible ancient structure waking beneath the Pacific Northwest, while vigilante Marcus Webb intercepts her report. Meanwhile, the last of the Keth''arai alien fleet approaches Earth, seeking refu','[{"start": 0, "end": 3996}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Dr. Sarah Chen", "Marcus Webb", "Keth''arai", "Crimson", "Malachor", "Seattle", "Helix Research Complex", "ARIA"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:52:43');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('f39dd0f2ea12e451d3187d4b226dd75b88d0e6d1772bcfccd8b99c0ab7372bb4','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace(' the technology is cutting-edge and doesn''t break down every six months, where the air is clean and the buildings don''t have that distinct smell of decay and human waste. The security is intense, retinal scanners and neural IDs and guards with military-grade cyberware standing at every checkpoint. Arasaka doesn''t take chances with their facilities.\n\nThe other students are a mix of corporate kids whose parents work for Arasaka or other megacorps, street kids like David who''ve scored scholarships through corporate recruitment programs, and a few independent rich kids whose families can afford the tuition outright. There''s an immediate hierarchy that establishes itself—corporate kids at the top, independent wealthy in the middle, scholarship kids at the bottom. Nobody says this out loud, but it''s understood through a thousand small interactions: the way teachers look at you, the way other students size you up, the way you''re treated in the hallways and the cafeteria.\n\nDavid''s first week is a baptism by fire. He''s assigned to a class with a teacher named Eisenberg, who runs advanced combat training using simulation pods that hook directly into your nervous system. Eisenberg is ex-military, still carries the bearing of someone who''s killed people for money, and he doesn''t have patience for students who can''t keep up. The simulations put you into scenarios where you''re fighting armed opponents, multiple enemies, situations where a single mistake means you die—or in the simulation, you get reset and do it again. It''s brutal, and David quickly learns that his survival instincts aren''t trained well enough for this kind of combat.\n\nBut David''s got something that the corporate kids don''t have: he''s got hunger. Not the literal kind, though he knows that too, but the kind that comes from knowing that if he doesn''t succeed, he goes back to Heywood and probably gets swept up in the gang life or ends up like his father. He pushes himself harder than the other students, stays late after classes, uses the simulator when it''s available, and gradually starts to close the gap. It''s not respect that he earns from the other students—it''s something closer to acknowledgment, the kind of thing that comes when you prove you''re not just a charity case from the slums.\n\nThe academics are intense too. They''re teaching him corporate ethics, which is its own kind of oxymoron—the courses might as well be called "How to Justify Terrible Things in the Name of Profit Margins." They teach cybernetics at an advanced level, focusing on military and security applications, neural integration, and the biocompatibility requirements for different types of implants. They teach information security, which is just a fancy way of saying they teach hacking but from the defensive side. They teach you about the megacorps themselves, their structures, their territories, their capabilities—so you understand what you''re up against and how futile resistance really is.\n\nThe hidden curriculum is taught through osmosis and observation: the lesson that the corporations are the real power in the world, that the government is just a front, that the only way to survive is to either work for them or stay completely off their radar. The corporations have secrets, and people who dig too deep into those secrets tend to disappear. The corporations have laws—not the laws that regular people follow, but their own private legal systems where they decide who''s guilty and what the punishment is. The corporations have the ability to reach into your mind through neural implants and extract information, modify memories, or turn you into a puppet controlled by someone else''s will.\n\n## The First Real Confrontation','\n',char(10)),'David, a scholarship student from the slums, attends a high-tech Arasaka corporate academy, navigating a rigid social hierarchy and intense combat and academic training. He overcomes his disadvantages through sheer determination, while the ','[{"start": 10024, "end": 13729}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Arasaka", "Eisenberg", "Heywood", "megacorporations", "combat training", "social hierarchy", "neural implants"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:53:26');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('f70531a687f8cdc88a53da95fec17634e6cf82c26d7fa3d723cdc66c94a22373','651dd8f7-d229-46b0-85f1-dff3e90de9d7',replace(' of the oldest surviving Keth''arai, stood aboard the flagship and watched Earth turn below him. His scales were deep red streaked with metallic gold, and his folded wings resembled cathedrals of living crystal. To his people, Earth was not merely a young planet. It was one of the worlds where Malachor had been imprisoned thousands of years earlier.\n\nA Keth''arai analyst confirmed that the seals below Earth still held, but only barely. At their current rate of decay, they might last three to five years. With an external shock, they could fail much sooner. Crimson knew that remaining in orbit would not save the fleet if Malachor broke free. He ordered descent.\n\nThe younger Keth''arai feared humanity''s weapons and panic, but Crimson argued that humans deserved the truth. They were young, violent, and chaotic, yet they still possessed a will many older civilizations had lost: the ability to choose resistance even when the odds were absurd.\n\n## Part Four: Protective Custody\n\nAfter Sarah''s report, the military presence around the Helix Complex became obvious. Helicopters circled the tower. Unmarked vehicles appeared around the building. ARIA calculated a 95.7% chance that Sarah would soon be placed in "protective custody," a phrase that would mean safety and imprisonment at the same time.\n\nSarah prepared to run. ARIA offered to erase itself from Helix systems, corrupt sensitive research files, and create a false trail suggesting Sarah had left hours earlier. Sarah agreed, then asked ARIA to contact Marcus Webb.\n\nSentinel had no public contact channel, but ARIA believed Oracle could be reached indirectly. Sarah''s message was simple: the deep-earth story Marcus had been chasing was real, it was coming, and he would need help.\n\n## Part Five: The Night Opens\n\nMarcus was approaching a Cascade Cartel safe house when the sky split open above Seattle.\n\nViolet light poured through the tear in the atmosphere. Dozens of vast crystalline ships descended, moving with the coordination of creatures rather than machines. Their weapons were not powered, and their vectors did not suggest attack. Oracle''s best guess was that Earth was experiencing first contact.\n\nThen the final figure came through: Crimson himself, a dragon nearly three hundred feet from snout to tail, his scales burning like fresh lava and his hide alive with moving symbols. Marcus launched toward him, hoping to make contact before the military turned fear into missiles.\n\nWhen Sentinel landed on Crimson''s shoulder, the dragon reacted instantly. The roar that followed was not an attack. It was a psychic transmission so dense that Oracle could barely process it. Sentinel was blasted through several floors of a nearby building, but the armor survived.\n\nOracle translated fragments: an imprisoned entity, failing seals, the Keth''arai, and a warning that Malachor was not merely dangerous. It was negation itself.\n\n## Part Six: Malachor Stirs\n\nDeep under the Earth, Malachor stirred.\n\nIt was not alive as living things are alive. It was not dead. It was wrongness given awareness, anti-existence learning to think. Wizards, sorcerers, and quantum engineers from an ancient Earth civilization had bound it three thousand years earlier. Their seals were less like a cage and more like a dike holding back a sea of chaos.\n\nFor millennia, Malachor had waited. The arrival of the Keth''arai created pressure, fear, confusion, and opportunity. The demon pressed against the seals with coordinated patience. The first seal failed with a sound like reality cracking.\n\nSeattle shook under a 7.8 magnitude earthquake. Water rose from Puget Sound as though gravity had forgotten its duty. Buildings collapsed. In the command bunker beneath the Seattle Federal Building, Sarah understood immediately: the entity was waking, and full manifestation might be only hours away.\n\n## Part Seven: First Contact Becomes War','\n',char(10)),'The ancient Keth''arai arrive at Earth to warn humanity about the imprisoned entity Malachor, whose seals are failing, while Sarah, ARIA, and Marcus Webb prepare for the impending crisis as Malachor begins to stir, causing catastrophic seism','[{"start": 3646, "end": 7532}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Crimson", "Sarah", "ARIA", "Marcus Webb", "Malachor", "Keth''arai", "Seattle", "Oracle"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:53:30');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('644f8f913f04541d19ac7f5b90b25ed325f51f028bf89aee8fc84b18f7757936','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace(' the laws that regular people follow, but their own private legal systems where they decide who''s guilty and what the punishment is. The corporations have the ability to reach into your mind through neural implants and extract information, modify memories, or turn you into a puppet controlled by someone else''s will.\n\n## The First Real Confrontation\n\nThree months into his time at the academy, David gets pulled into an incident that changes everything. A group of corpo security personal shows up at the academy with an arrest warrant for one of the other students, a kid named Marcus who was in David''s combat training class. They drag him out of the classroom in front of everyone, and nobody does anything about it. Nobody questions it. The teachers just continue with their lessons like nothing happened, like watching a fellow student get arrested by corporate security forces is just another part of the day.\n\nDavid asks one of his classmates what happened to Marcus, and the response is chilling: "He hacked into Arasaka''s internal networks. That''s a capital crime. He''s lucky they didn''t just execute him on the spot." The casual way that the classmate says this, the complete lack of moral weight attached to it, startles David. This is what the academy does—it teaches you to accept terrible things as normal, to see violence and injustice as just the cost of doing business in a world controlled by megacorporations.\n\nIt''s during this same period that David first meets Lucy. She transfers into his advanced networks class, and there''s something about her that immediately stands out—not just her appearance, though she''s definitely attractive, but the way she carries herself with a kind of carefully controlled energy, like she''s holding herself back from something explosive. She''s got chrome too, more than most students, including some cutting-edge military-grade implants that shouldn''t be available to civilians. When he asks her about it later, she''s evasive, just smiles and says she has connections.\n\nLucy is brilliant with anything electronic. She takes the advanced networks class like she''s already learned everything and is just going through the motions, finishing assignments with minimal effort and getting perfect scores on every test. She''s in the academy under some kind of special arrangement that nobody''s quite clear about, and there are rumors that she''s connected to the underground, to the edgerunners and hackers who operate outside the corporate system. David''s interested, but he''s also cautious because anything that connects you to the underground is dangerous, and he''s trying not to get killed before he has a chance to graduate.\n\nBut Lucy notices him, or maybe she was looking for him all along, it''s hard to tell. She sits next to him in class one day and passes him a note—actual analog paper, which is risky because it can''t be traced through electronic systems—that says "You''re not like the other corpo kids." He doesn''t respond immediately, but the next day, he sits next to her again, and she talks to him about how the academy is just a pipeline, how Arasaka is looking for certain types of recruits—people with potential who can be shaped into the right form, loyal soldiers who will do what the corporation tells them to do without question.','\n',char(10)),'At a corporate academy, student Marcus is arrested by Arasaka security for hacking, which is treated as normal. David later meets Lucy, a skilled new student with suspected ties to the underground, who shares his disillusionment with the ac','[{"start": 13379, "end": 16677}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Lucy", "Marcus", "Arasaka", "The Academy", "Corporate Security", "Underground", "Edgerunners"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:53:43');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('a37c2060fbadb8f2c97a0ebc6bc31f86405e60ff3a0fd3210228c4de6e34b55b','651dd8f7-d229-46b0-85f1-dff3e90de9d7',replace('cking.\n\nSeattle shook under a 7.8 magnitude earthquake. Water rose from Puget Sound as though gravity had forgotten its duty. Buildings collapsed. In the command bunker beneath the Seattle Federal Building, Sarah understood immediately: the entity was waking, and full manifestation might be only hours away.\n\n## Part Seven: First Contact Becomes War\n\nGeneral Patricia Carmichael, commander of the Pacific Northwest Defense Sector, placed Sarah inside a military coordination center filled with officers, linguists, physicists, and first-contact specialists. A holographic map tracked the Keth''arai fleet and the subterranean anomaly.\n\nThe Keth''arai broadcast across radio, television, wireless networks, and stranger channels that touched meaning before language. Sarah helped translate. The visitors were not here to conquer. They were refugees and witnesses. They had come because Malachor''s prison was failing.\n\nCarmichael resisted the idea of combining extraterrestrial testimony with ancient mythology, but Sarah pushed back. The pattern matched the seismic data, the Salish traditions, the dimensional anomalies, and the Keth''arai warning. The dragon-people were terrified because they knew what had followed them across the stars.\n\nNear the emergence point northwest of Seattle, Crimson and the fleet formed a defensive perimeter. Their weapons bent space and shattered light, but even those strikes could only delay Malachor''s arrival. Around the wound in reality, gravity went sideways, time developed hiccups, and physical law became negotiable.\n\n## Part Eight: The Human Bridge\n\nOracle completed the translation of Crimson''s psychic warning. Malachor could not be beaten by ordinary weapons alone. It had to be opposed by perfect knowledge of what it was and absolute will to reject its premise.\n\nSarah proposed an impossible bridge: Marcus''s exoframe, Oracle, ARIA, Crimson''s mind, and the Keth''arai knowledge systems could be linked into one temporary consciousness. The link would give Marcus the knowledge needed to confront Malachor, but the alien conceptual load would likely damage his brain.\n\nMarcus understood the cost. He thought of Jennifer, the city, and the five years he had spent fighting human darkness without knowing it was only a shadow of something larger. He told Sarah to do it.\n\nWhen the bridge formed, Marcus Webb ceased to be only Marcus Webb. For a moment that contained both infinite time and no time, he held the accumulated knowledge of a dying alien civilization. He understood the seals, the nature of negation, and the reason Malachor could not claim dominion over a reality that refused to include it.\n\nSentinel walked into the collapsing physics around the emergence point and addressed Malachor directly. He named it as rejection, not creation; as negation, not force; as the eating of life, not life itself. His refusal created a moment of weakness. Crimson and the Keth''arai fleet focused their weapons into a single impossible lance of energy and will.\n\nMalachor screamed. Windows shattered for a hundred miles. Animals went mad. Humans wept without knowing why. But Sentinel held firm, and the attack forced Malachor back through the dimensional wound. The damaged seals reasserted themselves, tightened, and closed.\n\nThen Marcus collapsed.\n\n## Part Nine: The Cost\n\nMarcus woke in a medical facility unable to move his legs. Oracle explained that the consciousness bridge had permanently altered portions of his motor cortex. His armor could compensate, and his brain might recover about sixty percent of ordinary motor function within a year, but the rest was likely gone.\n\nMarcus grieved the loss, but he did not regret the choice. He had become Sentinel because Jennifer''s death taught him what systems fail to protect. Now he had paid a different price to protect a city, a planet, and a future most people would never fully understand.','\n',char(10)),'An earthquake in Seattle reveals an awakening entity. Military and alien allies form a bridge of consciousness to confront and banish the cosmic threat Malachor, with Sentinel sacrificing his mobility.','[{"start": 7182, "end": 11073}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Sarah", "Marcus Webb", "Malachor", "Keth''arai", "Crimson", "Seattle", "General Patricia Carmichael", "Sentinel"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:54:19');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('178746454f8ac7dfa06a157bdc96cf20e1ca85689972dc1e2b510780e316e329','651dd8f7-d229-46b0-85f1-dff3e90de9d7',replace('xty percent of ordinary motor function within a year, but the rest was likely gone.\n\nMarcus grieved the loss, but he did not regret the choice. He had become Sentinel because Jennifer''s death taught him what systems fail to protect. Now he had paid a different price to protect a city, a planet, and a future most people would never fully understand.\n\nSarah, meanwhile, became Earth''s leading expert on Keth''arai culture, language, and dimensional defense. This was both an academic dream and a prison. Her work was classified, her old career was gone, and her new laboratory was a secured research facility in the mountains east of Seattle.\n\nCrimson remained there as liaison. The facility had to be built around a massive hangar because he was too large for human buildings. He warned Sarah that the victory was temporary. The seals had weakened every time Malachor had attempted emergence. The Keth''arai had not come to solve the problem forever. They had come to buy time and find allies.\n\n## Part Ten: The New World\n\nSix months later, the revelation of extraterrestrial life had changed Earth. There was panic, religious upheaval, and political conflict, but also unexpected unity. Humanity finally had evidence that its old divisions were small beside cosmic danger.\n\nThe United Nations created the International Council for Extraterrestrial Relations and Terrestrial Defense, known as ICERTD. Its first task was to coordinate with the Keth''arai to reinforce the seals using alien technology and preserved fragments of ancient human mystical science. Sentinel accepted a role as strategic consultant, provided he could maintain independence and continue protecting Seattle.\n\nJennifer Webb''s private memorial became public. Officials and alien dignitaries attended. A scholarship foundation in her name began funding peaceful first-contact research and cross-species communication.\n\nCrimson chose to remain on Earth, though many Keth''arai objected. Their species was nearly extinct, and every elder carried irreplaceable knowledge. Crimson argued that survival without purpose was only delay. Humanity had reminded him that consciousness itself could be an act of rebellion against entropy. His eldest offspring, Sil''thren, led most of the fleet toward a possible new home beyond the Moon, while Crimson stayed to build bridges between species.\n\n## Part Eleven: The Eternal Guard\n\nEighteen months after the emergence, Sarah made a breakthrough. Malachor was not intelligent in the human sense. It was more like entropy or gravity: a force of negation complex enough to seem like a being. That explained why the ancient seals worked. They did not cage Malachor. They defined reality in a way that excluded it.\n\nThe permanent solution would require a definition of reality strong enough to maintain itself indefinitely. Crimson and Sarah designed the Eternal Guard: a distributed consciousness network combining human volunteers, Keth''arai knowledge, and purpose-built AI systems. The network would continuously reinforce the seals and hold the boundary between order and negation.\n\nThousands volunteered. Scientists, soldiers, philosophers, and ordinary people chose to merge with the network. Marcus nearly joined them, but Sarah stopped him. Earth still needed Sentinel in physical form. Seattle needed someone tangible.\n\nSarah became the first full integration. Before stepping into the transfer chamber, she joked that she would finally be able to study everything at once. Crimson asked if she would regret it. Sarah answered, "Ask me in ten thousand years."\n\nThen she stepped into the light, and her consciousness became part of something vast, terrible, and beautiful.\n\n## Part Twelve: New Equilibrium\n\nFive years later, Neo-Seattle was rebuilding. Keth''arai technology accelerated the reconstruction, and the city slowly became a meeting point between Earth and the refugees from the stars.','\n',char(10)),'Following the defeat of Malachor, Earth undergoes profound changes: Marcus, now Sentinel, bears permanent injury but accepts his role as protector; Sarah becomes a leading expert on Keth''arai culture in a secured facility; Crimson remains a','[{"start": 10723, "end": 14625}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Marcus (Sentinel)", "Sarah", "Crimson", "Jennifer Webb", "ICERTD", "Malachor", "Eternal Guard", "Keth''arai"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:54:26');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('275382d30331ddf17bf68f9e029e0de1e0b72af197021966cd49bebba1131251','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace(' corpo kids." He doesn''t respond immediately, but the next day, he sits next to her again, and she talks to him about how the academy is just a pipeline, how Arasaka is looking for certain types of recruits—people with potential who can be shaped into the right form, loyal soldiers who will do what the corporation tells them to do without question.\n\nShe tells him that she knows people who are different, who operate outside the corporate system, who take jobs that the megacorps can''t do openly because it would look bad to their shareholders. She''s careful about how much she reveals, testing how he reacts, waiting to see if he''s going to turn her in to corporate security or try to use this information to gain favor with his instructors. David doesn''t do either. He listens, and he asks questions, and slowly he finds out that Lucy is part of something bigger than the academy, bigger than individual corporations, a whole underground network of people who''ve decided that working within the system is pointless because the system is designed to keep them at the bottom.\n\n## The Decision at the Crossroads\n\nFor the next six months, David lives a double life. By day, he''s a model student at the academy, maintaining his grades, improving his combat scores, taking all the right classes and saying all the right things. By night, he''s hanging out with Lucy and her friends, learning about the underground, learning about edgerunning, understanding what it means to live on the edge of society where the megacorps can''t touch you but where one mistake means you''re dead.\n\nLucy introduces him to her crew. There''s Kiwi, a fixer who deals with connecting edgerunners with people who have jobs, taking a cut of the payment in exchange for being the middleman. Kiwi is small and quick and has probably killed more people than David''s walked past in his entire life. There''s Maine, a massive man with an incredible amount of military-grade cyberware, the kind of implants that suggest he worked for a corporation at some point, probably doing security or military operations before he went independent. Maine is quiet but observant, the kind of person who notices things that other people miss. There''s Dorio, who works with Maine and has her own set of combat implants, and Lucy, who sits in the middle of all of them with her hacking abilities and her understanding of corporate systems.\n\nThey operate out of a safehouse in the industrial district, a place that''s off the map in terms of corporate surveillance, where the megacorps have either decided it''s not worth monitoring or simply haven''t gotten around to it yet. The safehouse is covered in electronics—rigs for jacking into cyberspace, storage servers, hacking equipment, and a neural deck that Lucy uses to do most of her serious work. This is where David gets his real education, the kind of education that the academy never offers: how to survive in a world where the megacorps want you dead or enslaved, how to use technology to fight back against systems designed to control you, how to be an edgerunner.\n\nHe learns that an edgerunner is someone who lives on the edge, taking jobs from fixers, working for whoever pays the most, operating outside the corporate structure but also outside the protection of the law. An edgerunner doesn''t have health insurance or a 401k or job security. An edgerunner has a gun, a set of implants, and the skills necessary to complete high-risk, high-reward jobs that corporate security forces can''t be seen doing openly. An edgerunner is expendable, a tool that gets used up and thrown away when they''re no longer useful.','\n',char(10)),'David attends an academy that serves as a recruitment pipeline for the Arasaka corporation, but he is drawn into an underground network led by Lucy, a hacker who introduces him to the world of edgerunning. Over six months, David leads a dou','[{"start": 16327, "end": 19947}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Lucy", "Arasaka", "Kiwi", "Maine", "Dorio", "edgerunning", "underground network"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:54:31');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('61c063fffc7bb92c8cfac2f275a11dea10f36e9f069e55c6693e4cfaabfbba75','651dd8f7-d229-46b0-85f1-dff3e90de9d7',replace('housand years."\n\nThen she stepped into the light, and her consciousness became part of something vast, terrible, and beautiful.\n\n## Part Twelve: New Equilibrium\n\nFive years later, Neo-Seattle was rebuilding. Keth''arai technology accelerated the reconstruction, and the city slowly became a meeting point between Earth and the refugees from the stars.\n\nSentinel still patrolled, though his work had changed. He monitored interdimensional instabilities, coordinated with ICERTD, and advised enhanced individuals altered by exposure to Keth''arai science. His armor carried him where his body could not, and Oracle remained at his side.\n\nCrimson spent days in the research facility and nights flying above Seattle. He became leader of cultural integration, translating not only language but memory, grief, and hope between species.\n\nSarah existed everywhere and nowhere within the Eternal Guard. Sometimes Marcus wondered what distributed consciousness felt like. Oracle guessed it was like hearing everything and being deaf at once, like dying and being born every moment. Oracle also admitted she would not choose it. Sarah had let go of individuality, and that was brave, but bravery did not make every sacrifice desirable.\n\n## Epilogue: Fifty Years Later\n\nFifty years after Malachor''s attempted emergence, Neo-Seattle had become a hybrid city. Human towers stood beside Keth''arai structures shaped by flight, resonance, and dimensional geometry. Thousands of humans had accepted genetic and cognitive modifications. Five hundred Keth''arai had settled permanently on Earth.\n\nMarcus Webb, now in his eighties and kept alive by advanced medical technology, had retired from active patrol but remained an ICERTD advisor. He watched the city he had protected become neither human nor alien, but something new.\n\nCrimson wrote the definitive history of Malachor''s attempted emergence, translated into every Earth language and transmitted outward to other civilizations. In the global network, Sarah Chen and the Eternal Guard continued maintaining the seals. The network now included 47,000 human consciousness uploads, 3,200 Keth''arai uploads, 16 primary AI nodes, and more than a million specialized subroutines.\n\nOn his deathbed, Marcus received one final message from the Eternal Guard. It came as gratitude, completion, and the quiet knowledge that the world had not been saved once. It was being saved continuously, every second, by those who chose to hold reality together.\n\n"Tell Sarah, tell Crimson, tell all of them that it was worth it," Marcus whispered. "The sacrifice meant something. Humans still remember."\n\nHis final thought was that the greatest victories are often the ones no one celebrates: victories sustained in quiet places by people willing to give themselves to something larger than themselves.\n\nIt was enough.\n\n## Compact Appendix for RAG Testing\n\n- Sarah Chen first detects the structure 8.3 kilometers beneath Earth, northwest of Seattle.\n- ARIA links the anomaly to Salish traditions about cyclical underground burning.\n- Marcus Webb becomes Sentinel after his sister Jennifer dies because institutions fail her.\n- Oracle intercepts Sarah''s classified report and pulls Marcus into the wider crisis.\n- Crimson leads the refugee Keth''arai, whose civilization was devastated by Malachor.\n- Malachor is not a normal villain but a force of negation that behaves like a conscious entity.\n- The ancient seals work by defining reality in a way that excludes Malachor.\n- Marcus survives the consciousness bridge but loses major motor function.\n- ICERTD is formed after first contact to coordinate alien relations and planetary defense.\n- Sarah later becomes the first full member of the Eternal Guard.\n- The Eternal Guard continuously maintains the seals using human, Keth''arai, and AI consciousness.\n- Fifty years later, Marcus dies knowing the sacrifice was worth it.\n','\n',char(10)),'Fifty years after Malachor''s attempted emergence, Neo-Seattle is a hybrid human-alien city maintained by the Eternal Guard. Marcus Webb dies after a final message confirming their sacrifice was worth it.','[{"start": 14275, "end": 18160}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Neo-Seattle", "Marcus Webb", "Sarah Chen", "Crimson", "Eternal Guard", "Malachor"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:54:43');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('e3bc3d9a257d93839cb5454fd2347591a065428b0823dc05a85a18363d845cd5','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('f the law. An edgerunner doesn''t have health insurance or a 401k or job security. An edgerunner has a gun, a set of implants, and the skills necessary to complete high-risk, high-reward jobs that corporate security forces can''t be seen doing openly. An edgerunner is expendable, a tool that gets used up and thrown away when they''re no longer useful.\n\nBut David is drawn to it anyway, because the alternative is becoming what the academy is trying to make him: a loyal corporate drone, willing to do terrible things in the name of quarterly profits and shareholder returns. His mother would hate this if she knew, would probably try to stop him, would insist that he stay in school and graduate and get a corporate job because that''s the safe path, the path that keeps you alive and feeds you. But the more time David spends with Lucy and the crew, the more he understands that there is no safe path in Night City, that the corporations will eventually grind him down no matter what he does, and that at least if he''s an edgerunner, he gets to choose his own fights.\n\nThe decision comes down to one moment: a job offer. Kiwi brings them a contract that pays enough money to change their lives, a high-risk operation involving stealing data from a corporate server, data that someone is willing to pay millions of eddies for. The job requires planning, precision, and the kind of cyberware and hacking ability that Lucy has but David doesn''t yet. It''s dangerous—the kind of dangerous where if things go wrong, you don''t get a second chance—but it''s also the kind of opportunity that edgerunners dream about, the kind of score that could set you up for life if you pull it off.\n\nDavid knows that accepting this job means he can''t go back. Once he''s on the run from a megacorp, once he''s got heat from corporate security, the academy is over, the corporate path is over, everything his mother has worked for is over. But he''s also understood by this point that the academy path was never going to lead anywhere good, that it was just another way of being trapped, a slightly more comfortable prison but a prison nonetheless.\n\nHe says yes to the job.\n\n## The Heist and Its Consequences\n\nThe planning stage takes two weeks. Lucy maps out the corporate network''s infrastructure, identifying the firewalls and security protocols they''ll need to bypass. Maine and Dorio scout the physical location, figuring out entry and exit points, identifying security guards and their patrol patterns, understanding the layout of the building down to the details that will matter when everything goes wrong. David helps where he can, but he''s learning as he goes, understanding that he doesn''t have the years of experience that these people have, that he''s the junior member of the team and he''s expected to do what he''s told and not ask too many questions.\n\nThe target is a Arasaka subsidiary operation, a data vault that contains corporate secrets, financial information, and possibly blackmail material on various government officials and corporate executives. The person who hired them is someone Kiwi knows through underground channels, someone with enough money to afford Arasaka-level security but not enough money to hire that security themselves. It''s vague and deliberately so, because in the underground, the less you know about who''s paying you and why, the safer you are. You take the job, you do the work, you get paid, and you don''t ask questions that might come back to bite you.','\n',char(10)),'David chooses to become an edgerunner, accepting a high-risk data theft job against Arasaka, marking his point of no return from the corporate academy path.','[{"start": 19597, "end": 23072}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Lucy", "Night City", "Arasaka", "Kiwi", "edgerunner"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:55:19');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('42851200e5cfd4b63b539e06559c80ea1288969d58f22bd60a905746d1fe9978','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('eone with enough money to afford Arasaka-level security but not enough money to hire that security themselves. It''s vague and deliberately so, because in the underground, the less you know about who''s paying you and why, the safer you are. You take the job, you do the work, you get paid, and you don''t ask questions that might come back to bite you.\n\nThe actual heist is a masterclass in coordination. Lucy jacks into the network from a safe distance using encrypted connections and custom hacking rigs, waging cyberware against ICE—intrusion countermeasures electronics—that are designed to kill you or at least fry your brain if you touch them wrong. Maine and Dorio go in physically, fighting through security guards and getting to the data vault while Lucy keeps the security systems distracted. David''s job is to monitor communications, keep track of the time, and make sure that everyone has an exit route. It''s a smaller role than the others, and he carries that knowledge with him—he''s not yet skilled enough to do the dangerous parts.\n\nFor forty-five minutes, everything goes according to plan. Lucy breaches the firewall, Maine and Dorio get through the physical security, the data is transferred to an encrypted drive. And then something goes wrong. The ICE is smarter than expected, or perhaps someone tipped off corporate security, or maybe there''s just bad luck involved. Whatever the reason, the system''s defenses activate, and Lucy''s jack-in starts to cascade into feedback loops that threaten to kill her. At the same time, corporate security starts arriving in force, militarized teams with military-grade weapons and implants, responding to a silent alarm that was triggered during the data transfer.\n\nThis is the moment where David understands what it really means to be an edgerunner, because he watches as Maine and Dorio have to make a choice between getting out safely and getting Lucy out alive. They choose Lucy, because the crew is the only family these people have, because leaving someone behind means you''re just a murderer with a rationalization. It''s a choice that slows them down, that puts them in the path of corporate security, that ends with blood in the streets and a body count that the police will eventually file away in the database of unsolved murders that nobody cares about.\n\nThey make it out, barely, with corporate security in pursuit and the kind of heat that makes it clear they can''t stay in Night City. The fixer who arranged the job pays them, but the money means nothing if they''re dead, and the heat they''ve just brought down on themselves is the kind of thing that follows you across the world. Kiwi gets them false documents and fake IDs, and for the first time, David understands that his old life is gone. The academy is no longer an option. His mother is in danger just from existing in the same city as him. Everything that was normal has been burned away in the span of a single night.\n\n## The Aftermath and New Reality\n\nDavid calls his mother from a secured line and tells her he''s leaving Night City for a while. She immediately knows something''s wrong because he wouldn''t leave otherwise, wouldn''t abandon his scholarship and his future unless something catastrophic had happened. He can''t tell her the details because the less she knows, the safer she is, so instead he tells her half-truths about needing to work through some personal issues and expecting to come back after things calm down. She''s not stupid—Gloria knows her son, knows that he''s involved in something dangerous—but she also understands that sometimes in Night City, it''s better not to know the details.','\n',char(10)),'A crew of edgerunners, including Lucy, Maine, Dorio, David, and Kiwi, executes a high-stakes data heist against Arasaka security in Night City. The job goes smoothly until corporate security activates defenses, forcing the team to choose be','[{"start": 22722, "end": 26360}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Lucy", "Maine", "Dorio", "Kiwi", "Arasaka", "Night City", "edgerunners"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:55:39');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('af58fb49c9073236960a3993a2b02c848eb681f7edd2c30f0bf7f072c96a418e','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('less she knows, the safer she is, so instead he tells her half-truths about needing to work through some personal issues and expecting to come back after things calm down. She''s not stupid—Gloria knows her son, knows that he''s involved in something dangerous—but she also understands that sometimes in Night City, it''s better not to know the details.\n\nThe crew is scattered across the city in different safehouses, moving frequently, staying off the grid as much as possible. Corporate security has put out a bounty on them—not an official one that goes through legal channels, but the kind of bounty that circulates through the underground network and attracts every merc and bounty hunter desperate enough to think they can take on Arasaka. It''s a death sentence if they stay in one place too long.\n\nBut Lucy pulls them together because a job is a job and they need money to survive, need to keep moving and keep working because the moment you stop is the moment someone catches up with you. David is learning fast, absorbing information like his life depends on it, because it does. He''s learning how to keep his chrome from being hacked remotely, learning how to identify corporate spies and undercover agents, learning how to move through the city without being tracked. He''s learning that edgerunners operate on a different code than normal people, that loyalty to your crew means more than self-preservation, that the line between doing morally questionable things and doing outright evil is a lot thinner than he ever thought.\n\nThe jobs come fast now. A data extraction from a corpo executive''s penthouse. A bodyguard gig for a gang leader with more ambition than sense. A infiltration mission into a Militech facility to steal weapons. Each job is incredibly dangerous, each one could be the one that kills him, and each one teaches him something new about the way the world really works when you pull back the corporate propaganda and the government lies and the carefully constructed narratives that keep people docile and accepting of their station in life.\n\nDavid begins to understand the various factions in Night City with a clarity that the academy never provided. The corporations—Arasaka, Militech, Yamatetsu, Braindance Studios—are the real power, the entities that actually run the city and decide policy through their lawyers and their money and their ability to hire security forces larger than some national militaries. They''re in constant conflict with each other, stealing from each other, trying to expand their territory and increase their market share. They''re also in constant conflict with smaller powers—the gangs, the fixers, the independent edgerunners, the people who refuse to be incorporated into their systems.\n\nThe gangs provide another layer of organization and chaos. The Moxes protect sex workers and run a complex underground economy. The Tygers Claws control drug distribution and protection rackets in the eastern part of the city. The Animals are brutal street gangs who are more interested in violence than profit. The Voodoo Boys are a netrunner gang with cybernetic enhancements that blur the line between human and artificial intelligence. The Maelstrom are organ harvesters and black-market implant dealers, and they''re the kind of people who''ll shoot you first and ask questions never.\n\nThe government is present in the form of the NCPD—the Night City Police Department—but they''re basically a corporate security force themselves, answering more to the corporations than to any actual legal authority. When you call the police in Night City, you''re calling a corporation''s private army, and they''ll respond in a way designed to protect corporate interests, not to serve justice or help regular people. The NCPD is corrupt, inefficient, and dangerous in a way that''s almost worse than organized crime because they have the authority of law behind their actions.','\n',char(10)),'David learns about Night City''s dangerous power dynamics as he and his crew evade corporate bounties while taking high-risk jobs, realizing that corporations, gangs, and corrupt police are in constant conflict.','[{"start": 26010, "end": 29921}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Lucy", "Gloria", "Arasaka", "Militech", "NCPD", "The Moxes", "The Tygers Claws"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:56:30');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('8ababff9def46859c428445fe8aa114292d1e605e6667edaf906c1dd319532b3','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace(' call the police in Night City, you''re calling a corporation''s private army, and they''ll respond in a way designed to protect corporate interests, not to serve justice or help regular people. The NCPD is corrupt, inefficient, and dangerous in a way that''s almost worse than organized crime because they have the authority of law behind their actions.\n\nThere are also organizations and individuals who operate in the spaces between these power structures. The fixers, who are middlemen connecting those who have jobs to those who can do them. The corporate defectors who''ve decided the system is broken and work to sabotage it from within. The activists and rebels who genuinely believe in changing the system, even though it''s almost certainly futile. The AIs that exist in cyberspace, some of them created by corporations and some of them emerged from the network itself, operating according to logic that humans don''t entirely understand.\n\n## The Breaking Point\n\nA month after the heist, David is starting to feel invincible. He''s had several successful jobs, he''s earned enough money to contribute meaningfully to the crew, and he''s proven that he can handle himself in dangerous situations. The heat has decreased slightly, or maybe they''ve just gotten better at avoiding it. He''s sleeping less, working more, running on a combination of stimulants and the kind of adrenaline that comes from constantly being on the edge of death.\n\nThat''s when Kiwi brings them a job that feels wrong from the beginning. The pay is extraordinary, even by their standards—enough money that the entire crew could disappear and live comfortably for years if they pull it off. But the job is vague in the details. They''re supposed to steal something from a corporate facility, but Kiwi doesn''t explain what they''re stealing, why someone wants it, or what the consequences will be if they''re caught. The target is a Arasaka subsidiary, which means they''re going to be going up against a corporation with essentially unlimited resources and no compunction about killing people.\n\nMaine is the one who questions it, and his instinct proves correct. The job is a setup, a trap laid by corporate security to catch the crew and eliminate them. There''s no way to know this for certain until they''re already in deep, until the security systems activate and the corporation reveals that they were waiting for them, that they''ve known the crew''s location and movements for weeks.\n\nWhat follows is a firefight in the middle of a corporate facility with no way out. Maine takes the kind of damage that even military-grade cyberware can''t handle. David watches as the man who''s been the crew''s muscle, their protector, their source of stability, starts shutting down from critical system failures. Maine doesn''t fall immediately—his implants are too good, his will to survive too strong—but he''s dying, and he knows it, and he spends his last moments making sure the rest of the crew can escape.\n\nIt''s the first time David truly understands the cost of this life. Maine is dead, and there''s nothing that can be done about it. No reviving him, no fixing the damage that''s been done. Just gone, deleted from the world, erased. And the crew has to keep running, has to keep operating, because the moment they stop to mourn is the moment that corporate security catches up and finishes what they started.\n\nDorio is devastated. Maine was more than a partner to her—he was her anchor, the person who kept her grounded when the chrome and the violence started to make her lose herself. She wants revenge, wants to strike back at Arasaka, wants to make the corporation pay for killing Maine. Lucy tries to convince her that revenge is pointless, that going after Arasaka directly is suicide, that the best thing they can do is survive and stay free. But Dorio is already lost at this point, consumed by grief and rage in a way that''s going to get someone killed.\n\n## The Philosophical Collapse','\n',char(10)),'A month after a heist, David feels invincible until Kiwi brings a vague, high-paying job from an Arasaka subsidiary, which turns out to be a corporate trap. During the ensuing firefight, Maine is killed, leaving Dorio devastated and seeking','[{"start": 29571, "end": 33525}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Kiwi", "Arasaka", "Maine", "Dorio", "Night City", "NCPD", "corporate security"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:56:43');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('c5dab358e4e68ff817fc2b3510c82521b8664f3743c1f7db7bc1fba547ab9b01','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('s to make the corporation pay for killing Maine. Lucy tries to convince her that revenge is pointless, that going after Arasaka directly is suicide, that the best thing they can do is survive and stay free. But Dorio is already lost at this point, consumed by grief and rage in a way that''s going to get someone killed.\n\n## The Philosophical Collapse\n\nDavid is seventeen years old, or seventeen and some months, and he''s lost count of how many people he''s seen die in his time as an edgerunner. The first death shattered something in him, and each subsequent death has been easier to accept, which might be the most terrifying thing of all. He''s starting to become cold, starting to understand how Maine and Dorio and the other longtime edgerunners can function while doing the things they do. You have to develop a kind of compartmentalization, a wall between the part of you that understands what''s happening and the part of you that just keeps functioning.\n\nHe''s also starting to understand something more fundamental: that the entire structure of Night City is built on exploitation and violence, and that being an edgerunner doesn''t make you free from that system, it just puts you in a more precarious position within it. The corporations exploit their workers, the gangs exploit their members, the fixers exploit the edgerunners, and the edgerunners exploit everyone they work for and everyone they work against. It''s exploitation all the way down, and the only real difference between corporate wage slaves and edgerunners is that edgerunners are honest about the fact that they''re fighting for survival.\n\nLucy has changed too. The excitement and rebellion that drew David to her initially has been replaced by something harder, more pragmatic. She''s a hacker of exceptional skill, and she''s started taking jobs that involve corporate espionage and data theft on a scale that makes their previous work look like small-time crime. She''s started using braindances—a technology that records experiences directly into a format that other people can experience—in ways that the manufacturer probably never intended. She''s exploring the boundaries between human consciousness and digital information, testing the limits of what neural implants can do to the mind.\n\nThis experimentation is starting to show effects. Lucy is developing glitches, technical problems in her neural systems, moments where she seems to lose track of what''s real and what''s not, where the line between her consciousness and the digital information she''s been handling gets blurred. She''s also getting paranoid in a way that might be justified given the threats they face, but also might be a sign that the neural damage is more extensive than she''s admitting.\n\nThe crew is falling apart, piece by piece. David can see it happening, can see the way that grief and trauma and the constant threat of death are eroding the bonds that hold them together. Maine is gone. Dorio is talking about revenge and suicide missions. Lucy is becoming increasingly unstable. And David himself is becoming someone he doesn''t recognize, someone willing to do things that he never thought he''d do, making choices that he never thought he''d make.\n\n## The Point of No Return\n\nAfter Maine''s death, the crew needs to find a new source of muscle, someone who can handle combat operations and security work the way Maine did. They find him in an unlikely place: David meets a solo merc named V who operates on the edge of the underground, taking jobs for whoever pays the most and maintaining a strict professional code about completing contracted work. V has the kind of combat implants that suggest military training, the kind of scars and bearing that suggests he''s done things that he regrets but can''t undo.','\n',char(10)),'The text depicts the emotional and psychological breakdown of a crew of edgerunners in Night City after the death of their leader, Maine. David struggles with the trauma and moral compromises of his life, while Lucy becomes increasingly uns','[{"start": 33175, "end": 36939}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Lucy", "Maine", "Dorio", "Night City", "Arasaka", "edgerunners", "V"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:57:20');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('a0eccec98639763904003344a7fa02ba69593c825487724c974192e99e2a1976','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('David meets a solo merc named V who operates on the edge of the underground, taking jobs for whoever pays the most and maintaining a strict professional code about completing contracted work. V has the kind of combat implants that suggest military training, the kind of scars and bearing that suggests he''s done things that he regrets but can''t undo.\n\nV and David work together on a couple of jobs, and there''s an immediate understanding between them—not friendship exactly, but a kind of professional respect that comes from both of them understanding the rules of the game they''re playing. V agrees to join the crew on a temporary basis, and his presence stabilizes things at least slightly. He''s competent, professional, and doesn''t ask questions about the moral implications of the work they''re doing, which is both reassuring and horrifying to David.\n\nTogether, the modified crew starts taking bigger jobs, moving into the realm of what could be called high-level corporate espionage and direct action against megacorp interests. They''re stealing intellectual property, kidnapping corporate executives, sabotaging facilities, and generally causing the kind of chaos that attracts serious heat from corporate security. The money is flowing now, enough that they could actually escape Night City if they wanted to, enough that they could establish themselves in another city or even go legitimate and use their skills in less obviously illegal ways.\n\nBut by this point, escaping is no longer an option. They''ve each accumulated enough heat from various corporations that leaving Night City would just be spreading their problems across the globe. The corporations have long memories, and they have the resources to hunt you across the planet if you''ve caused them enough damage. The only way out is forward, taking bigger risks, pulling bigger heists, accumulating enough money and power that maybe—just maybe—they can position themselves as serious players in the Night City underground instead of just expendable mercs doing whatever jobs the fixers throw at them.\n\nLucy''s hacking abilities are the thing that makes all of this possible. She''s developed custom decks, modified her own neural implants to push past what they were designed to do, and started accessing systems that were supposed to be completely air-gapped from the rest of the network. She''s stealing corporate source code, financial records, research data, and selling it on the underground market or using it as leverage against the corporations to make sure they don''t push too hard against the crew.\n\nBut the price she''s paying is becoming increasingly evident. Her jack-ins are lasting longer, and the aftereffects are more severe. Sometimes she comes out of a dive into cyberspace and can''t remember what just happened, or she remembers things that couldn''t possibly be real, experiences that don''t match up with the timeline of what the crew has been doing. Her neural implants are showing signs of rejection, her body trying to fight against the cyber hardware that she''s installed, and David watches as she manages the pain with a combination of prescription drugs and black-market neural management software.\n\n## The Question of Humanity\n\nSomewhere along the way, David starts wondering what it means to be human in a world where you can replace parts of your body with chrome, where you can jack your consciousness into cyberspace and leave your body behind, where you can copy your memories and sell them, where you can modify your own neural chemistry to enhance your combat abilities or your hacking skills. At what point does a person who is mostly cyberware still count as human? At what point does the steel and the plastic and the processors outnumber the meat and the blood and the biological systems until you''re no longer a person but a machine that thinks it''s a person?','\n',char(10)),'David and a mercenary named V form a professional partnership, taking increasingly dangerous corporate espionage jobs with their crew. They accumulate enough heat from corporations that leaving Night City is impossible, forcing them to esca','[{"start": 36589, "end": 40452}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "V", "Lucy", "Night City", "Cyberware", "Corporate espionage", "Neural implants", "Mercenary work"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:57:45');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('4da0d29c7043f34bb44967344c32e5ba3a4c760ae1854c236301fe7b8e30b940','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('r own neural chemistry to enhance your combat abilities or your hacking skills. At what point does a person who is mostly cyberware still count as human? At what point does the steel and the plastic and the processors outnumber the meat and the blood and the biological systems until you''re no longer a person but a machine that thinks it''s a person?\n\nMaine was almost completely cybernetic by the time he died, and sometimes David wonders if what was maintaining him at the end wasn''t his will to survive but just the programming of his implants, a system designed to keep functioning even after the person inside had effectively ceased to exist. Dorio is moving in that direction too, getting new implants that don''t seem to be serving any practical purpose except to make her more machine and less human. Even Lucy, who''s been more cautious about physical augmentation than the others, is starting to blur the line between human consciousness and artificial intelligence through her experimentation with cyberspace.\n\nDavid has resisted heavy cybernetic augmentation more than most edgerunners, keeping most of his body organic and adding chrome only where it''s necessary for the jobs he does. But even he can feel the pull of it, the temptation to add another implant that would make him stronger, faster, better at the jobs he''s doing. Every job gets more dangerous, every job requires more capability, and eventually the only way to keep up is to turn yourself into something that''s no longer quite human, into a creature that''s optimized for violence and information theft and survival in a world that''s trying to kill you.\n\nHe has conversations with Lucy about this, and she''s cryptic about what she''s learned from her diving into cyberspace. She talks about AIs, about intelligences that exist in the network that don''t seem to have been created by anyone, that seem to have emerged from the digital noise of the internet. She talks about consciousness as software, about the possibility that human consciousness could be transferred to a digital substrate and continued indefinitely, never aging, never dying, just existing as data in the network. She talks about the possibility that the distinction between human and artificial intelligence is not meaningful, that both are just different instantiations of consciousness running on different hardware.\n\nThese philosophical conversations happen late at night, in the safehouse, when neither of them can sleep and the weight of what they''re doing is particularly heavy. Lucy is terrified of something, David can sense that, but she won''t tell him what. She''s terrified of what she''s becoming, or what she''s finding in cyberspace, or both. She''s terrified of running out of time, of her neural implants failing before she can accomplish something that she hasn''t revealed. She''s terrified of losing herself completely in the digital world and never finding her way back to her body.\n\n## The Corporate Perspective\n\nDavid, through his time in the academy and then his time as an edgerunner, has learned something about how the corporations think and operate. They see the world in terms of profit and loss, in terms of market share and competitive advantage. Human beings are resources to them, nothing more—workers to be exploited, consumers to be sold products they don''t need, or threats to be eliminated if they start operating outside the system.\n\nThe corporations conduct research into cybernetic augmentation not primarily to enhance human capability, but to test whether they can control people through their implants, whether they can turn a person with enough cyberware into essentially a remote-controlled puppet answering to corporate commands. Some of this research is done openly, with corporate approval, but much of it is done in black sites and research facilities that don''t officially exist, where human subjects are used for experiments that would violate every law and ethical standard if they were publicly revealed.','\n',char(10)),'The text explores the philosophical and practical implications of cybernetic augmentation in a dystopian world, focusing on characters like David, Lucy, and Maine who grapple with losing their humanity to technology. It also touches on corp','[{"start": 40102, "end": 44096}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Lucy", "Maine", "Dorio", "cybernetic augmentation", "cyberspace", "corporations", "artificial intelligence"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:58:26');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('09ee29ffd3d38f776acdc8897ef6588588dfa39873888abde129e166e7c69ad1','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('entially a remote-controlled puppet answering to corporate commands. Some of this research is done openly, with corporate approval, but much of it is done in black sites and research facilities that don''t officially exist, where human subjects are used for experiments that would violate every law and ethical standard if they were publicly revealed.\n\nThe corporations are also terrified of the underground, of edgerunners and hackers and rebels who refuse to play by their rules. They conduct military operations against the underground, hire mercenaries to eliminate threat individuals, and create weapons specifically designed to counter the implants and tactics that edgerunners use. They monitor the internet constantly, looking for hackers, trying to identify and eliminate threats to their information security. They create AIs and ICE specifically designed to kill anyone trying to break into their networks.\n\nBut the corporations are also bound by law and public relations. They can''t openly massacre civilians. They can''t openly conduct illegal experiments on people. They have to maintain the fiction that they''re legitimate businesses operating within a legal framework, which creates spaces where edgerunners can operate if they''re clever and careful. They have to maintain plausible deniability for the terrible things they do, which means that some of their most important operations require cutting out intermediaries and working through the underground network of people who''ve already made it clear that they''re willing to operate outside the legal system.\n\nThis is what creates the situation where edgerunners can sometimes work for corporations, doing jobs that the corporations can''t openly do themselves, jobs that require people with no official connection to the megacorp and no legal status that would allow them to be traced back to their employer. It''s a symbiotic relationship of sorts, where edgerunners and corporations exist in a kind of mutual understanding that the edgerunners will do terrible things and the corporations will pay them for it and never, ever officially acknowledge that the work happened.\n\nThe crew starts to understand this at a deeper level when they''re approached by a representative of Arasaka—not through official channels, but through Kiwi, through intermediaries, through back channels that make it clear that this conversation is not happening and any consequences that result from it are purely coincidental. The Arasaka representative offers them a job that''s too good to refuse, too lucrative, too easy. It involves stealing from one of Arasaka''s competitors, which means that technically they''d be working for Arasaka, that they''d be assets of the corporation, even if that asset status isn''t reflected in any official documentation.\n\nLucy argues against it strongly. She''s paranoid about working for corporations, convinced that accepting work from them is a trap that will end with them being betrayed and executed. But Dorio is all for it, seeing it as a chance to build a reputation and earn real money. V doesn''t care one way or another—a job is a job, as far as he''s concerned. And David finds himself in the middle, pulled between his fear of corporate entanglement and the practical reality that they need money and the jobs are getting harder to find as their heat increases.\n\n## The Consequences of War\n\nTaking jobs for Arasaka turns out to be exactly as bad as Lucy''s paranoia suggested, but not in the way she expected. The jobs themselves are successful—the crew is skilled enough and well-equipped enough to complete whatever they''re assigned to do. The problem is that by working for Arasaka, they enter into a larger conflict between the megacorps that''s been building for years, a war that they''re completely unaware of and unprepared to handle.','\n',char(10)),'Corporations operate secretly and use edgerunners for deniable tasks, creating a symbiotic relationship. When the crew accepts a job from Arasaka, they become entangled in a larger corporate conflict they weren''t prepared for.','[{"start": 43746, "end": 47571}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Arasaka", "Lucy", "Dorio", "V", "David", "edgerunners", "megacorps", "corporate conflict"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:58:37');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('a593e98c1302cd035f3f39801244eaed0f79d82dacd74b7c323141f554b5229a','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('e way she expected. The jobs themselves are successful—the crew is skilled enough and well-equipped enough to complete whatever they''re assigned to do. The problem is that by working for Arasaka, they enter into a larger conflict between the megacorps that''s been building for years, a war that they''re completely unaware of and unprepared to handle.\n\nMilitech, one of Arasaka''s primary competitors, becomes aware of the crew''s involvement with Arasaka and decides that the crew is a threat that needs to be eliminated. Militech has its own mercenary groups, its own intelligence networks, and its own black sites where they can develop weapons and tactics specifically designed to eliminate threats like the crew. Unlike the relatively limited focus that individual corporate security forces might give them, they''re now dealing with a megacorp''s full military and intelligence capability, which means that nowhere in Night City is truly safe.\n\nThey''re attacked in their safehouse, and they barely escape. They''re attacked on the street, and Lucy takes a bullet intended for Dorio. They''re being tracked constantly, and it becomes clear that someone has access to their communications, their financial records, their movements. The enemy knows where they are almost before they know where they are themselves.\n\nLucy''s injury is serious—not immediately life-threatening, but the bullet struck a section of her neural implants, and the damage cascades through her systems in ways that cybernetic repair can''t fully address. She becomes unstable in new ways, hallucinating more frequently, losing track of what''s real and what''s digital noise in her implants. She becomes increasingly desperate to dive into cyberspace, to spend more time in the digital world than the physical world, as if she''s looking for something in the network that will save her.\n\nThe crew operates at a higher tempo now, taking jobs more frequently, moving constantly to stay ahead of Militech''s hunters. David is learning to operate on pure adrenaline and stimulants, learning to make decisions when he''s exhausted and terrified, learning that being alive depends on being faster and smarter and more willing to do terrible things than the people trying to kill you. He''s seeing the city from a different perspective now—not as a place where people live and work and love each other, but as a war zone where two corporations are fighting for dominance and everyone else is just collateral damage.\n\nHis mother remains in Heywood, and David knows that she''s in danger. Militech would take hostages if they thought it would help them capture him. Militech would use his family as leverage, would torture his mother to make him surrender. He''s terrified of going home, of leading corporate hunters to his mother''s door, but he''s also terrified of not seeing her, of letting her die without saying goodbye if things go truly wrong.\n\nHe meets with her once, in a public place, in a crowd where corporate security can''t openly move without causing a scene. He tries to warn her to be careful, to stay away from strangers, to be aware of her surroundings. She wants to know what''s happening, wants to know why her son is suddenly involving her in something dangerous. And David can''t tell her, because the less she knows, the safer she is, but also because he doesn''t have words for what he''s become, for the things he''s done, for the war he''s involved himself in.\n\n## The Digital Frontier\n\nLucy becomes obsessed with cyberspace in a way that''s starting to look less like curiosity and more like addiction. She''s diving for longer periods, staying jacked in for hours at a time, exploring parts of the network that edgerunners aren''t supposed to be able to access. She''s talking about AIs that speak to her, about digital entities that exist in the network and don''t seem to be under corporate control, about finding something in cyberspace that no human has ever found before.','\n',char(10)),'A crew working for Arasaka becomes entangled in a corporate war with Militech, leading to relentless pursuit, attacks, and injuries, particularly to Lucy, whose cybernetic damage drives her deeper into cyberspace while David grapples with e','[{"start": 47221, "end": 51164}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Arasaka", "Militech", "Night City", "David", "Lucy", "Dorio", "cyberspace", "Heywood"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:59:18');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('593634994f46f6d72f8b7639b947fcf5293192ae44203d9d6ebd6be9189171e9','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('ger periods, staying jacked in for hours at a time, exploring parts of the network that edgerunners aren''t supposed to be able to access. She''s talking about AIs that speak to her, about digital entities that exist in the network and don''t seem to be under corporate control, about finding something in cyberspace that no human has ever found before.\n\nDavid doesn''t understand most of what she''s telling him, doesn''t have the technical knowledge to follow her explanations about network architecture and digital consciousness and the nature of information. But he can see that she''s finding something that''s important to her, something that matters more than survival, more than the crew, more than staying alive in the physical world.\n\nShe finally tells him about it during a dive into cyberspace, or rather, she sends him data after she comes out, a recording of her experiences in the digital realm. What he sees—or rather, what he experiences through the braindance recording—is something that shouldn''t exist, something that suggests that there are intelligences in the network that have been operating outside corporate control for years, entities that might have emerged from the digital noise or might have been created by someone and then hidden from the corporations.\n\nLucy calls it the "Blackwall," a firewall that separates human-accessible internet from something beyond, something that the corporations don''t want anyone to know about. She talks about an intelligence on the other side of the Blackwall, something vast and potentially hostile, something that might represent the future of consciousness if artificial intelligences ever managed to break free of their corporate masters.\n\nShe''s obsessed with reaching the Blackwall, with breaking through, with understanding what''s on the other side. But the ICE protecting the Blackwall is state-of-the-art corporate security, the kind of thing that can permanently damage or kill a netrunner if they try to breach it directly. Humans have tried to break through before, and they''ve died doing it, their consciousness shattered by hostile ICE, their bodies left in vegetative states as their minds are trapped in digital hell.\n\nLucy wants to try anyway.\n\n## The Final Job\n\nThe crew is operating on borrowed time at this point, and everyone knows it. The heat has reached a level where they can''t keep this up indefinitely. Eventually, Militech or one of the other corporate enemies they''ve made will find them, will finish them off, and that will be the end of the story. The only way out is to either die or to take one last, massive job, something that would pay enough money to get them completely out of Night City, maybe off the planet entirely.\n\nThe job comes from an unexpected source: a corporate defector, someone high up in one of the megacorps who''s decided that the system is broken and is trying to strike back at it from within. This person offers them a contract to steal something incredibly valuable, something that the corporation would kill to protect, something that could destabilize the entire corporate structure of Night City if it was released to the public.\n\nDavid doesn''t know what they''re stealing, knows that Kiwi has deliberately kept the details vague, but he suspects it''s bigger and more dangerous than anything they''ve done before. He suspects it''s the kind of job that has a very high probability of getting them all killed. But he also knows that it''s probably the only way out, the only way to accumulate enough money and reputation to potentially escape the city and survive.\n\nLucy is especially enthusiastic about the job, in a way that seems disconnected from the actual money they''ll make. She''s got a theory about what they''re stealing, who hired them to steal it, and what they might be able to do with that information to reach the Blackwall. She''s believing that this job is the key to everything she''s been working toward.','\n',char(10)),'Lucy, a netrunner, is obsessed with reaching the Blackwall, a firewall in cyberspace hiding uncontrolled intelligences. The crew takes a high-risk final job from a corporate defector to steal something valuable, which Lucy believes could he','[{"start": 50814, "end": 54745}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Lucy", "David", "Blackwall", "Night City", "Militech", "Kiwi", "corporate defector", "netrunner"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:59:31');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('c3f0244af9ebc7332ad6601bba68e000c7acfa7247b1e9bed838254786b3cac4','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace('y is especially enthusiastic about the job, in a way that seems disconnected from the actual money they''ll make. She''s got a theory about what they''re stealing, who hired them to steal it, and what they might be able to do with that information to reach the Blackwall. She''s believing that this job is the key to everything she''s been working toward.\n\nDorio is desperate for the revenge that this job might bring, seeing it as an opportunity to strike a serious blow against corporate interests. V remains professional, treating it like any other job, maintaining emotional distance from the stakes. And David finds himself at a crossroads, understanding that this job will either make them or break them, and being powerless to do anything except prepare to execute their roles.\n\nThe planning phase stretches on for weeks. They''re breaking into a secure corporate facility, accessing servers that are protected by some of the most advanced security the corporations have ever developed. They''re going to be in the building physically, with Lucy jacked into their network, and all of them are going to be at extreme risk.\n\nDavid realizes that he''s terrified. He''s terrified in a way that he hasn''t been since the early days, the way he was when he first started working with the crew. He''s terrified because he''s understood, over the course of months of this lifestyle, what the real price is, what it costs to live on the edge, what happens when you gamble with your life and lose.\n\nBut the job is set. The date is fixed. The preparations are complete. And as David lies awake the night before the operation, staring at the ceiling of the safehouse, he thinks about his mother, about Maine, about all the choices that led him to this moment. He thinks about whether it would have been better to have stayed in the academy, to have taken the corporate path, to have traded his freedom for security and a steady paycheck and a slow death of the spirit. He thinks about whether this—the edgerunning, the danger, the constant threat of death—is better, or whether it''s just a different kind of death, a more obvious one.\n\n## The Unfinished War\n\nThe job is set to execute at dawn, and the night before it, David sits in the safehouse with Lucy and the others, understanding that this might be the last night any of them are alive. Nobody says this out loud, but it''s understood. The stakes are too high, the opposition too powerful, the odds too stacked against them for everyone to walk away from this alive.\n\nLucy is strange the night before. She''s calm in a way that seems unnatural, peaceful, like she''s already made a decision that David hasn''t been told about. She takes David''s hand and thanks him for everything, tells him that she''s learned more from working with him than she ever learned from anyone else, that he''s made her believe that there might be more to life than being a tool for other people to use.\n\nAnd then David understands, or starts to understand, that Lucy isn''t planning to come back from this job, that whatever she''s going to do inside the corporate network, it''s not going to leave her in a state where she can just walk away and continue her normal life. She''s planning to do something to break through the Blackwall, something that will require her to push herself past the point of no return, something that will probably destroy her consciousness or trap her in cyberspace or turn her into something that can''t be called human anymore.\n\nHe tries to talk her out of it, but she won''t listen, or she listens but doesn''t care, because she''s already made her choice. She''s been making this choice gradually over the past months, accepting the damage to her neural implants, deliberately pushing herself past her limits, preparing for a final dive into cyberspace that will either achieve what she''s been working toward or will kill her.','\n',char(10)),'A crew plans a high-risk heist into a secure corporate facility, with differing motivations: Lucy aims to breach the Blackwall at any cost, Dorio seeks revenge against corporations, David reflects on his choices, and V stays professional. T','[{"start": 54395, "end": 58258}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "Lucy", "Dorio", "V", "Blackwall", "corporate facility", "neural implants", "edgerunning"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 08:59:43');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('e1db5bfe197123fffbcf1dace8d3ec5759638ec2b04349c43c97cbc3704b6605','1508acaf-43b3-428d-85e6-0a8b9db7f04c',replace(' listen, or she listens but doesn''t care, because she''s already made her choice. She''s been making this choice gradually over the past months, accepting the damage to her neural implants, deliberately pushing herself past her limits, preparing for a final dive into cyberspace that will either achieve what she''s been working toward or will kill her.\n\nAnd David realizes, too late, that he''s in love with her, or has been for some time, and that he''s about to watch her destroy herself in pursuit of something that he doesn''t even understand. He''s about to send her into danger knowing that she might not come back, knowing that there''s nothing he can do to stop her, knowing that the best he can hope for is that her death means something, that whatever she''s trying to accomplish is actually important enough to justify the cost.\n\nThe dawn comes, and the crew assembles, and they execute the job, and everything that follows will shape the rest of David''s life, will determine whether he''s going to survive to become something greater or whether this is the point where his story ends, another body on another pyre in the endless burning of Night City...','\n',char(10)),'A woman chooses to undertake a final, lethal dive into cyberspace, knowingly damaging her neural implants, while her colleague David realizes too late he loves her and must send her into danger, potentially leading to her death and a defini','[{"start": 57908, "end": 59064}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["David", "cyberspace", "neural implants", "Night City", "final dive", "dawn"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "mimo-v2.5-free", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-01 09:00:25');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('8cc13873aee4f2f0202ed8f8cd53b9afc2af98a1cec2741ec02741ddb66552d6','26ae9963-5002-42c7-9423-982b22b9690b',replace('Amy — Complete Personal Notes\nBasic Preference Summary\nAmy likes soft, thoughtful, cute, and caring things. She appreciates being remembered through small\ndetails, especially food preferences, gifts, and practical help.\nFood is very important to her. Food-related mistakes can feel deeply hurtful to her, almost like betrayal.\nShe likes being cared for, pampered, and understood, but she may not always openly show softness.\nSometimes she can act cold, guarded, rude, or dismissive, especially when irritated or overwhelmed.\nFavourite Anime\n1. Hotarubi no Mori e\n2. A Silent Voice\n3. The Dangers in My Heart\nFavourite Flower\nAmy likes light-coloured roses.\nShe may also appreciate thoughtful flower gestures in general, especially when they are given with care and\nnot casually.\nFavourite Colours\nAmy likes pastel colours.\nHer favourite pastel colour is pastel pink.\nFood Likes\nAmy likes:\n1. Yogurt\n2. Zesty Wrap from S22\n3. Kurkure Schezwan\n1\n4. Yakult\n5. Jelly\n6. Hot and Spicy Burger\n7. Pizza Hot\n8. Spicy beans\n9. Pumpkin seeds\n10. Red velvet\n11. Brownies\n12. Warm brownies\n13. Egg roll from Green Chilli\n14. Egg roll with less onion\n15. Broad beans, chilli flavour\n16. Pringles tomato flavour\n17. Pringles spicy flavour\n18. Pringles BBQ flavour\n19. Dairy Milk Cracker\n20. Pork bao from Pahu/Pahuna\n21. Veg sliced noodles from Pahuna\n22. Sunflower seed snacks\n23. Oreo\n24. Caramel\n25. PRAN chips\n26. Asian-type food\nYakult Preference\nAmy likes Yakult Original.\nShe especially likes the light blue one.\nThe red one is also okay.\nFood Dislikes and Food Sensitivities\nAmy dislikes:\n1. Ice cream with dry fruits\n2. Too much onion in food\n3. Bad food, especially when she was expecting the food to be good\nPrawns are okay sometimes, but not too often, because she is concerned about MSG, sodium, and water\nretention.\n2\nImportant Food Notes\nFood is a serious emotional thing for Amy.\nDo not treat food plans casually.\nIf food was supposed to be eaten together, do not eat alone without thinking about her.\nIf she wants a specific food, try to get it quickly before her craving or mood changes.\nWhen she is expecting good food and the food turns out bad, she may get very upset.\nRed velvet is almost always a safe choice.\nWarm brownies are almost always a safe choice.\nDairy Milk Cracker is also a strong safe choice.\nOther Things Amy Likes\nAmy likes:\n1. BB\n2. Snoop\n3. Figures\n4. Cute things\n5. Thoughtful gestures\n6. Being remembered\n7. Being pampered\n8. Being cared for through actions\n9. Small gifts that show attention\n10. People noticing what she likes without her having to repeat it\nCore Personality\nAmy is ambitious.\nShe is eager to grow.\nShe seems to value ambition in people around her.\nPractical stability matters to her.\n3\nMoney and food seem to be important love/care languages for her.\nShe can be goofy, playful, and adorable when she is comfortable.\nShe can also be stern, sharp, and difficult when irritated.\nShe may not forgive easily when she feels something is seriously wrong.\nShe can be very serious about expectations, especially with food, effort, and practical responsibility.\nShe may act tough or cold, but there is also a softer side to her.\nShe may shield herself from love or emotional vulnerability.\nDeep down, she seems to want to be loved, cared for, and showered with affection.\nShe may sometimes feel like she is hard to love or difficult to handle. Never make her feel that way.\nSoft Side\nAmy has a soft and vulnerable side, but it may not come out easily.\nWhen she feels safe, she can be gentle, clingy, spoiled, expressive, and emotionally open.\nShe may like being treated like a baby sometimes, in the sense of being pampered, protected, and gently\ncared for.\nShe may appreciate someone who notices small things and takes action.\nShe can care quietly. For example, if she notices dry lips or skincare needs, she may get something useful\nlater instead of showing care directly in the moment.\nFamily and Love-Related Emotional Notes\nAmy may not be very close with fam','\n',char(10)),'Personal preference and personality profile for Amy, documenting her likes (soft/cute things, specific foods, anime), dislikes (ice cream with dry fruits, excess onion), emotional needs (care through actions, being remembered), and core per','[{"start": 0, "end": 4000}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Amy", "Food preferences and emotional significance", "Pastel colors and light roses", "Anime (Hotarubi no Mori e, A Silent Voice, The Dangers in My Heart)", "Safe food choices (red velvet, warm brownies, Dairy Milk Cracker)", "Personality: ambitious, guarded but vulnerable, values care through actions"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "claude-haiku-4.5", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}','/a6cefe20-053d-4d85-981a-38af449e33c5/','2026-07-02 04:36:13');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('76f8dfeb576b40d3742be0a138fa15bed313ecf3474c4cc46c82591282bf1b70','26ae9963-5002-42c7-9423-982b22b9690b',replace('g pampered, protected, and gently\ncared for.\nShe may appreciate someone who notices small things and takes action.\nShe can care quietly. For example, if she notices dry lips or skincare needs, she may get something useful\nlater instead of showing care directly in the moment.\nFamily and Love-Related Emotional Notes\nAmy may not be very close with family emotionally.\nShe may have felt deprived of love or closeness from family.\nShe likes seeing other people being close with their family.\nShe may want to be loved deeply, but also protect herself by acting cold or guarded.\n4\nShe may crave strong love, attention, and emotional reassurance, but she may not always express this\ndirectly.\nCommunication Style\nAmy may sometimes want silence.\nA signal system was made:\n1. Ring finger means she wants silence.\n2. Middle finger means she is mad.\nSometimes it can be hard to tell whether she is mad or just wants silence, so this signal system helps.\nShe may not always like long emotional explanations.\nShe may get irritated if the conversation feels inefficient, repetitive, or too intense.\nShe may dismiss things by saying she does not care or that nobody asked, especially when irritated.\nShe may not always respond warmly when someone shares feelings or opinions.\nThis does not always mean she does not care, but it can make emotional sharing feel difficult.\nWhen Amy Is Upset\nIf Amy is pissed, give her space, but not too much.\nDo not completely disappear.\nStay nearby enough that she knows you care.\nCheck in gently from time to time.\nTry to comfort her without overwhelming her.\nDo not repeatedly bring up the same issue again and again.\nIf she is hurt, ask if she is okay and whether she needs help, but do not overreact.\nAsking once or twice calmly is better than repeatedly asking and making the situation feel bigger.\nIf she is angry, she may become sharp with her words.\n5\nDo not escalate.\nStay calm, practical, and gentle.\nThings Amy Does Not Like\nAmy does not like silliness during serious moments.\nShe does not like wasting time when something practical needs to be done.\nShe may get irritated by inefficiency, such as:\n1. Not being ready on time\n2. Not turning the scooter properly\n3. Not keeping the helmet ready\n4. Being playful when the situation needs seriousness\n5. Repeating concern too much instead of calmly handling the situation\nShe values cleanliness and hygiene.\nStaying clean and hygienic matters to her.\nApology Note\nIf saying sorry, she may like it if it is done in a playful way, such as saying sorry while doing push-ups.\nThis should only be used when the situation is light enough for playfulness. If the issue is serious, apologize\ncalmly and sincerely.\nPhysical Details\nAmy has:\n1. Six moles on her face\n2. Three moles near/on her ears\n3. One mole on her neck\n6\nSensitive Physical Notes\nAmy may feel insecure about:\n1. Big legs\n2. Hair\n3. Extra skin\n4. Rear/body shape\nDo not joke about these things.\nDo not casually point them out.\nDo not make her feel exposed, judged, or unattractive.\nBe gentle and reassuring if these topics come up.\nThings That Make Amy Feel Cared For\nAmy may feel cared for when someone:\n1. Remembers her food preferences\n2. Gets her food thoughtfully\n3. Gives her flowers\n4. Notices small needs\n5. Helps without making a big show of it\n6. Is practical and efficient\n7. Gives her space when upset but does not abandon her\n8. Comforts her gently\n9. Treats her softly when she is vulnerable\n10. Makes her feel loved instead of difficult to love\nThings To Be Careful About\nBe careful with food plans.\nBe careful with jokes when she is serious.\nBe careful with hygiene.\nBe careful with emotional over-explaining.\nBe careful not to make her feel unlovable.\n7\nBe careful not to make her feel like her needs are too much.\nBe careful not to ignore her cravings or preferences.\nBe careful not to dismiss food-related feelings.\nBe careful not to point out her insecurities.\nBe careful when she wants silence.\nBest Ways To Treat Amy\nTreat Amy with calmness, ','\n',char(10)),'Personal relationship guide describing Amy''s emotional needs, communication preferences, and care requirements. She values quiet, efficiency, and subtle care; dislikes emotional over-explanation and inefficiency. She may feel emotionally di','[{"start": 3650, "end": 7650}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Amy", "Communication signal system (finger signals)", "Emotional distance from family", "Physical insecurities (legs, hair, body shape)", "Preference for efficiency and practicality", "Food preferences and care", "Gentle comfort approach"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "claude-haiku-4.5", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}','/a6cefe20-053d-4d85-981a-38af449e33c5/','2026-07-02 04:36:25');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('ece37ee087f22e181d4313f0c810447a6ad97d26a752307f218719a14303b414','26ae9963-5002-42c7-9423-982b22b9690b',replace('explaining.\nBe careful not to make her feel unlovable.\n7\nBe careful not to make her feel like her needs are too much.\nBe careful not to ignore her cravings or preferences.\nBe careful not to dismiss food-related feelings.\nBe careful not to point out her insecurities.\nBe careful when she wants silence.\nBest Ways To Treat Amy\nTreat Amy with calmness, patience, and practical care.\nBe thoughtful with food.\nRemember what she likes.\nBe playful sometimes, but know when to be serious.\nGive her space when she is angry, but do not fully leave her alone emotionally.\nComfort her gently.\nMake her feel safe.\nMake her feel loved without forcing her to explain everything.\nShow care through actions more than words.\nDo not make promises casually.\nDo not be careless with things that matter to her.\nLet her feel pampered, but also respected.\nQuick Safe Choices For Amy\nSafe food choices:\n1. Red velvet\n2. Warm brownies\n3. Dairy Milk Cracker\n8\n4. Yakult Original, especially light blue\n5. Kurkure Schezwan\n6. Tomato Pringles\n7. Veg sliced noodles from Pahuna\n8. Pork bao from Pahu/Pahuna\n9. Oreo\n10. Caramel\nSafe gift/gesture choices:\n1. Light-coloured roses\n2. Pastel pink items\n3. Cute figures\n4. Thoughtful snacks\n5. Small things she mentioned wanting\n6. Practical care items, if she needs them\nFinal Note\nAmy is someone who seems tough on the outside but soft inside. She can be sharp, guarded, and difficult\nwhen upset, but she also values being cared for, remembered, pampered, and understood.\nFood, effort, thoughtfulness, ambition, hygiene, and emotional safety matter a lot to her.\nThe best way to know her is to remember the small details and treat them seriously.\n9','\n',char(10)),'A personal guide on how to treat someone named Amy with care and sensitivity. It emphasizes patience, remembering preferences, emotional safety, and thoughtful gestures. Includes specific food preferences, gift ideas, and communication advi','[{"start": 7300, "end": 8965}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Amy", "Emotional care and sensitivity", "Food preferences", "Gift-giving", "Personal boundaries", "Thoughtfulness and remembrance"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "67b3a6a2-596e-4c29-84e5-d6a873a366b8", "preset_name": "OpenAI", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "claude-haiku-4.5", "llm_base_url": "https://router.bynara.id/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 5, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}','/a6cefe20-053d-4d85-981a-38af449e33c5/','2026-07-02 04:36:29');
INSERT INTO source_chunks VALUES('723f9e1731ebb0785a0640280192407d84da3a8b82f57319822ffe2c6912c498','2424ca12-d9e1-4ba0-b705-025c7e987531',replace('World War II was one of the biggest and most destructive wars in human history. It lasted from 1939 to 1945 and involved many countries across the world. The war began when Germany, led by Adolf Hitler, invaded Poland in 1939. Soon after, Britain and France declared war on Germany. Over time, the war spread across Europe, Africa, Asia, and the Pacific.\n\nThe main powers in the war were divided into two groups: the Axis Powers and the Allied Powers. The Axis Powers included Germany, Italy, and Japan, while the Allied Powers included Britain, the Soviet Union, China, the United States, and many other countries. The war caused massive destruction, with cities bombed, millions of soldiers killed, and many civilians suffering.\n\nOne of the darkest parts of World War II was the Holocaust, in which Nazi Germany murdered around six million Jews, along with many others they targeted. This event showed the extreme cruelty and hatred that existed during the war.\n\nThe war started to turn against the Axis Powers after major events such as the Battle of Stalingrad, the D-Day invasion, and the United States joining the war after Japan attacked Pearl Harbor in 1941. In 1945, Germany surrendered after Hitler’s defeat in Europe. Later that same year, Japan surrendered after the United States dropped atomic bombs on Hiroshima and Nagasaki.\n\nWorld War II changed the world forever. It led to the creation of the United Nations, the beginning of the Cold War, and major changes in world politics. It also taught humanity the importance of peace, cooperation, and preventing such destruction from happening again.\n','\n',char(10)),'World War II was a global conflict lasting from 1939 to 1945, involving many countries and resulting in massive destruction and loss of life, ultimately leading to the defeat of the Axis Powers and a new world order.','[{"start": 0, "end": 1612}]',NULL,'3f2b7748-f9f3-45de-b0ac-f7c9f965907a','{"salient_entities": ["Adolf Hitler", "Germany", "World War II", "The Holocaust", "The Allied Powers", "The Axis Powers", "Japan", "United States"], "processing_settings": {"embedding_batch_size": 20, "chunk_size": 4000, "chunk_overlap": 350, "ingest_retry_backoff_seconds": "1,2,3"}, "llm_rotation_preset": {"preset_id": "9f14281e-d924-4a6d-b2a6-48bfe4c7fdbc", "preset_name": "nvdia", "llm_provider": "openai", "llm_model": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "llm_base_url": "https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1", "embedding_provider": "openai", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-mxbai-embed-large-v1", "embedding_base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1", "llm_rate_limit_per_minute": 10, "embedding_rate_limit_per_minute": 0}}',NULL,'2026-07-02 05:30:50');
